<node id="95809504-b954-435b-8fa9-5edfda35ba72">
  <data key="d0">{"name":"Indexed Annuity Investment Options","text":"═══════════════════════\nPrimary: Matthew Scott Thompson (Spouse) - 100%\nContingent: Thompson Family Trust - 100%\n\n═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\nARTICLE 1 - KEY DEFINITIONS\n═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n1.1 \"Index Account\" - An account where interest credits are based \n    on the performance of a stock market index.\n\n1.2 \"Fixed Account\" - An account earning a guaranteed fixed \n    interest rate.\n\n1.3 \"Cap Rate\" - The maximum interest rate that can be credited \n    to an index account in any crediting period.\n\n1.4 \"Floor Rate\" - The minimum interest rate (0%) that will be \n    credited, protecting against market losses.\n\n1.5 \"Participation Rate\" - The percentage of index gain that is \n    credited to your account.\n\n1.6 \"Point-to-Point Method\" - Interest crediting based on index \n    change from beginning to end of crediting period (annual).\n\n═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\nARTICLE 2 - INDEXING OPTIONS AND ALLOCATION\n═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n2.1 AVAILABLE INDEX ACCOUNTS:\n    \n    A) S&amp;P 500 Index Account (Annual Point-to-Point)\n       Current Cap: 10.5% | Participation Rate: 100%\n       Floor: 0% | Crediting Period: 1 year\n    \n    B) NASDAQ-100 Index Account (Annual Point-to-Point)\n       Current Cap: 9.0% | Participation Rate: 100%\n       Floor: 0% | Crediting Period: 1 year\n    \n    C) Global Diversified Index Account\n       Current Cap: 8.5% | Participation Rate: 100%\n       Floor","summary":"This document provides foundational definitions for indexing mechanisms in insurance products, including key terms like Cap Rate, Floor Rate, Participation Rate, and the Point-to-Point Method. It lists three available index accounts—S&amp;P 500, NASDAQ-100, and Global Diversified—each using annual point-to-point calculation with 100% participation and varying caps ranging from 8.5% to 10.5%. All accounts feature a 0% floor, ensuring no loss due to negative market performance. Ownership is designated primarily to Matthew Scott Thompson, with contingency held by the Thompson Family Trust.","topics":["Indexed Annuity","Investment Accounts","Interest Calculation Methods","Financial Planning"],"facts":[{"name":"Index Account Definition","sentence":"An 'Index Account' is an account where interest credits are based on the performance of a stock market index.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["Index Account","Interest Credits","Stock Market Performance"],"entities":[{"name":"Index Account","type":"CONCEPT","role":"account based on market index performance","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Fixed Account","type":"CONCEPT","role":"account with guaranteed fixed interest rate","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Cap Rate","type":"CONCEPT","role":"maximum interest rate creditable per period","relational_anchors":["10.5%","9.0%","8.5%"]},{"name":"Floor Rate","type":"CONCEPT","role":"minimum interest rate protection at zero percent","relational_anchors":["0%"]},{"name":"Participation Rate","type":"CONCEPT","role":"percentage of index gain credited to account","relational_anchors":["100%"]},{"name":"Point-to-Point Method","type":"CONCEPT","role":"interest calculation method over annual periods","relational_anchors":["annual"]},{"name":"S&amp;P 500 Index Account (Annual Point-to-Point)","type":"ACCOUNT","role":"available index-based investment option","relational_anchors":["Current Cap: 10.5%","Participation Rate: 100%","Floor: 0%","Crediting Period: 1 year"]},{"name":"NASDAQ-100 Index Account (Annual Point-to-Point)","type":"ACCOUNT","role":"available index-based investment option","relational_anchors":["Current Cap: 9.0%","Participation Rate: 100%","Floor: 0%","Crediting Period: 1 year"]},{"name":"Global Diversified Index Account","type":"ACCOUNT","role":"available diversified index-based investment option","relational_anchors":["Current Cap: 8.5%","Participation Rate: 100%","Floor"]}]},{"name":"Guaranteed Fixed Interest Account","sentence":"A 'Fixed Account' is an account earning a guaranteed fixed interest rate.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["Fixed Account","guaranteed interest rate","account types"],"entities":[{"name":"Index Account","type":"CONCEPT","role":"account based on market index performance","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Fixed Account","type":"CONCEPT","role":"account with guaranteed fixed interest rate","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Cap Rate","type":"CONCEPT","role":"maximum interest rate creditable per period","relational_anchors":["10.5%","9.0%","8.5%"]},{"name":"Floor Rate","type":"CONCEPT","role":"minimum interest rate protection at zero percent","relational_anchors":["0%"]},{"name":"Participation Rate","type":"CONCEPT","role":"percentage of index gain credited to account","relational_anchors":["100%"]},{"name":"Point-to-Point Method","type":"CONCEPT","role":"interest calculation method over annual periods","relational_anchors":["annual"]},{"name":"S&amp;P 500 Index Account (Annual Point-to-Point)","type":"ACCOUNT","role":"available index-based investment option","relational_anchors":["Current Cap: 10.5%","Participation Rate: 100%","Floor: 0%","Crediting Period: 1 year"]},{"name":"NASDAQ-100 Index Account (Annual Point-to-Point)","type":"ACCOUNT","role":"available index-based investment option","relational_anchors":["Current Cap: 9.0%","Participation Rate: 100%","Floor: 0%","Crediting Period: 1 year"]},{"name":"Global Diversified Index Account","type":"ACCOUNT","role":"available diversified index-based investment option","relational_anchors":["Current Cap: 8.5%","Participation Rate: 100%","Floor"]}]},{"name":"Cap Rate Definition","sentence":"The 'Cap Rate' is the maximum interest rate that can be credited to an index account in any crediting period.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["Cap Rate","Index Account","Crediting Period"],"entities":[{"name":"Index Account","type":"CONCEPT","role":"account based on market index performance","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Fixed Account","type":"CONCEPT","role":"account with guaranteed fixed interest rate","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Cap Rate","type":"CONCEPT","role":"maximum interest rate creditable per period","relational_anchors":["10.5%","9.0%","8.5%"]},{"name":"Floor Rate","type":"CONCEPT","role":"minimum interest rate protection at zero percent","relational_anchors":["0%"]},{"name":"Participation Rate","type":"CONCEPT","role":"percentage of index gain credited to account","relational_anchors":["100%"]},{"name":"Point-to-Point Method","type":"CONCEPT","role":"interest calculation method over annual periods","relational_anchors":["annual"]},{"name":"S&amp;P 500 Index Account (Annual Point-to-Point)","type":"ACCOUNT","role":"available index-based investment option","relational_anchors":["Current Cap: 10.5%","Participation Rate: 100%","Floor: 0%","Crediting Period: 1 year"]},{"name":"NASDAQ-100 Index Account (Annual Point-to-Point)","type":"ACCOUNT","role":"available index-based investment option","relational_anchors":["Current Cap: 9.0%","Participation Rate: 100%","Floor: 0%","Crediting Period: 1 year"]},{"name":"Global Diversified Index Account","type":"ACCOUNT","role":"available diversified index-based investment option","relational_anchors":["Current Cap: 8.5%","Participation Rate: 100%","Floor"]}]},{"name":"Floor Rate Protection","sentence":"The 'Floor Rate' is the minimum interest rate (0%) that will be credited, protecting against market losses.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["Floor Rate","Market Loss Protection","Interest Crediting"],"entities":[{"name":"Index Account","type":"CONCEPT","role":"account based on market index performance","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Fixed Account","type":"CONCEPT","role":"account with guaranteed fixed interest rate","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Cap Rate","type":"CONCEPT","role":"maximum interest rate creditable per period","relational_anchors":["10.5%","9.0%","8.5%"]},{"name":"Floor Rate","type":"CONCEPT","role":"minimum interest rate protection at zero percent","relational_anchors":["0%"]},{"name":"Participation Rate","type":"CONCEPT","role":"percentage of index gain credited to account","relational_anchors":["100%"]},{"name":"Point-to-Point Method","type":"CONCEPT","role":"interest calculation method over annual periods","relational_anchors":["annual"]},{"name":"S&amp;P 500 Index Account (Annual Point-to-Point)","type":"ACCOUNT","role":"available index-based investment option","relational_anchors":["Current Cap: 10.5%","Participation Rate: 100%","Floor: 0%","Crediting Period: 1 year"]},{"name":"NASDAQ-100 Index Account (Annual Point-to-Point)","type":"ACCOUNT","role":"available index-based investment option","relational_anchors":["Current Cap: 9.0%","Participation Rate: 100%","Floor: 0%","Crediting Period: 1 year"]},{"name":"Global Diversified Index Account","type":"ACCOUNT","role":"available diversified index-based investment option","relational_anchors":["Current Cap: 8.5%","Participation Rate: 100%","Floor"]}]},{"name":"Participation Rate Definition","sentence":"The 'Participation Rate' is the percentage of index gain that is credited to your account.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["Participation Rate","index gain credit","account allocation"],"entities":[{"name":"Index Account","type":"CONCEPT","role":"account based on market index performance","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Fixed Account","type":"CONCEPT","role":"account with guaranteed fixed interest rate","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Cap Rate","type":"CONCEPT","role":"maximum interest rate creditable per period","relational_anchors":["10.5%","9.0%","8.5%"]},{"name":"Floor Rate","type":"CONCEPT","role":"minimum interest rate protection at zero percent","relational_anchors":["0%"]},{"name":"Participation Rate","type":"CONCEPT","role":"percentage of index gai