<edge source="325410d2-10cd-4b16-9227-4b96221af7a2" target="1c5eba0f-2f29-43d1-b13a-bc342d4f4ae4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines Fixed Accounts offering stable, predictable returns, while fact_sentence_1 presents Index Accounts linked to volatile market gains. They represent opposing approaches to interest generation, used possibly alongside one another in product design.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRASTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="325410d2-10cd-4b16-9227-4b96221af7a2" target="1d4b712e-5e26-4cf9-a7ad-301c683e58e3">
  <data key="d3">A Fixed Account earns a guaranteed interest rate independently of market indices, while the Cap Rate limits how much interest can be earned through index-linked accounts. These concepts apply to distinct types of investment vehicles.</data>
  <data key="d4">UNRELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="325410d2-10cd-4b16-9227-4b96221af7a2" target="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955">
  <data key="d3">A Fixed Account earns a guaranteed interest rate, independent of market indices. The Participation Rate determines how much of an index's growth is applied to an indexed account, but it does not apply to fixed accounts.</data>
  <data key="d4">UNRELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="325410d2-10cd-4b16-9227-4b96221af7a2" target="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77">
  <data key="d3">A Fixed Account offers a guaranteed interest rate, independent of market fluctuations. The Floor Rate ensures no credit falls below zero during downturns, providing downside protection in variable-rate scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="325410d2-10cd-4b16-9227-4b96221af7a2" target="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3">
  <data key="d3">The concept of a Fixed Account, offering a guaranteed interest rate, contrasts with the variable returns tied to indices via the Point-to-Point Method. This distinction highlights alternative approaches to interest crediting but does not imply any functional dependence.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
