  <data key="d3">The Cap Rate limits potential gains in index-linked accounts, whereas the Year 10 surrender charge reflects costs tied to withdrawing funds before maturity. While both affect overall return outcomes, they operate independently—one governs growth mechanics, the other exit penalties.</data>
