</edge>
<edge source="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3" target="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75">
  <data key="d3">The Point-to-Point Method determines annual interest credited based on index performance, influencing long-term growth potential, while the Year 8 surrender charge affects cost efficiency when exiting early. Together, they inform decisions about holding duration versus return expectations.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3" target="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00">
  <data key="d3">The Point-to-Point Method determines annual interest credited based on index performance, while the Year 9 surrender charge reflects a penalty for early withdrawal. These elements coexist in the policy but operate independently.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">The point-to-point interest crediting method determines returns earned under the policy, which influence the account value upon which surrender charges are applied. Thus, higher credited interest may increase the account value subject to surrender fees in later years.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">The point-to-point interest crediting method determines returns over fixed periods, while the elimination of surrender charges after Year 12 encourages longer retention of the policy, potentially allowing more full-period applications of the method.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">The point-to-point interest crediting method determines returns earned under the policy, which influence the overall account value. This accumulated value affects the basis upon which surrender charges are applied, particularly relevant in Year 11 when the charge drops to 0.5%, suggesting it may reflect diminishing penalties relative to long-term growth potential.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">The Point-to-Point Method determines how the Account Value grows over time through indexed returns, which directly affects the basis for calculating Cash Surrender Value.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">The Point-to-Point Method determines how interest accumulates over time, which indirectly affects the account value that influences surrender charges. However, it does not directly determine or modify the surrender charge calculation itself.</data>
