  <data key="d3">The allocation to the NASDAQ-100 Index is specified at 30%, reflecting investor positioning within the indexed accounts. This detail stands independently from any calculation involving the S&amp;P 500’s hypothetical performance over a given period.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="13737585-4de1-4789-b42c-a05bc511593e" target="a7b1c147-442d-4852-b81d-665875dffa47">
  <data key="d3">The NASDAQ-100 index allocation reflects part of the investor’s strategy within an indexed account designed to benefit from market growth while being shielded from downside risk due to built-in protections like a 0% floor.</data>
