  <data key="d3">Free reallocations allow investors to shift assets among accounts up to four times annually at no charge. This benefit applies regardless of whether the investor chooses the Fixed Account or an indexed account.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e7acf52-f866-478f-91af-c99f9dc14a24" target="d2272e16-5b5e-4cf0-8180-275ee09c4556">
  <data key="d3">Free reallocation rights apply regardless of whether the Fixed Account has a floor; they concern access flexibility rather than investment safeguards.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e7acf52-f866-478f-91af-c99f9dc14a24" target="5970ce74-f216-4469-89e2-77ce18166763">
  <data key="d3">Investors may make up to four annual reallocation requests at no charge, enabling flexible management of assets among the indexed and fixed accounts. These adjustments do not impact the Fixed Account’s guaranteed 3% yield, which remains unchanged irrespective of rebalancing activity.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e7acf52-f866-478f-91af-c99f9dc14a24" target="b5a49b5f-16b1-4dba-94df-96a105e6000e">
  <data key="d3">The availability of four free reallocations annually enables investors to modify their current holdings, such as adjusting the 50% allocation to the S&amp;P 500 Index, without paying extra fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e7acf52-f866-478f-91af-c99f9dc14a24" target="13737585-4de1-4789-b42c-a05bc511593e">
  <data key="d3">The availability of four free reallocation opportunities allows investors to modify their holdings, including potentially increasing or decreasing their stake in the NASDAQ-100 Index, whose current allocation stands at 30%.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES_DECISION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e7acf52-f866-478f-91af-c99f9dc14a24" target="122014ab-154e-4331-94fc-e939755b46e6">
  <data key="d3">The rule allowing four free reallocations each year enables investors to modify their portfolio mix—including potentially changing the 20% allocated to the Fixed Account—without incurring fees, supporting flexible risk management.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_ADJUSTMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e7acf52-f866-478f-91af-c99f9dc14a24" target="2b2e3f84-59bf-4a6e-b26c-8b5ae353f6de">
  <data key="d3">Allowing four free reallocations annually supports the policyholder’s right to modify allocations on policy anniversaries without added costs.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e7acf52-f866-478f-91af-c99f9dc14a24" target="2601679e-fb90-4392-b3a8-8e4aaa913aa1">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 establishes that investors may make up to four free reallocation requests annually, which includes actions taken on a policy anniversary mentioned in fact_sentence_1, thereby validating those specific changes as exempt from fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENCOMPASSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e7acf52-f866-478f-91af-c99f9dc14a24" target="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3">
  <data key="d3">The first four reallocation requests being free sets a baseline; any additional requests beyond this number incur a $25 fee, establishing a conditional cost structure based on frequency.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_COST</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e7acf52-f866-478f-91af-c99f9dc14a24" target="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1">
  <data key="d3">The availability of free reallocations does not influence the minimum cap on index-based crediting, which remains independently enforced at 4%. The two rules operate under separate mechanisms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e7acf52-f866-478f-91af-c99f9dc14a24" target="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7">
  <data key="d3">The availability of free reallocations does not affect the minimum participation rate guarantee; they operate independently under separate policy provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e7acf52-f866-478f-91af-c99f9dc14a24" target="27176921-2e5c-44aa-bcf0-40ddf6e140f2">
  <data key="d3">The availability of free reallocations does not affect how interest is computed from index movements and participation rates. The two concepts relate to separate operational features of the investment product.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e7acf52-f866-478f-91af-c99f9dc14a24" target="c4dbdf51-a4cd-4a65-8903-f269d529eefd">
  <data key="d3">The availability of free reallocation attempts does not affect the minimum guaranteed return on the fixed account. The fixed account's 2% floor ensures stability regardless of how often an investor reallocates funds.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e7acf52-f866-478f-91af-c99f9dc14a24" target="665dbf69-ad45-49be-8a49-a811282557e1">
  <data key="d3">The first four reallocations per year are free of charge, allowing investors to rebalance their portfolios at no cost. This information does not affect or relate to how index returns are computed.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e7acf52-f866-478f-91af-c99f9dc14a24" target="6ff1f4bc-a2b4-4e15-b514-415d803bd39b">
  <data key="d3">The availability of free reallocations annually does not directly affect how interest is calculated under caps and floors, but frequent adjustments could impact exposure to index performance that is subject to those limits.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e7acf52-f866-478f-91af-c99f9dc14a24" target="3fe4c74a-f6e1-4f2e-874b-5a03244e9e44">
  <data key="d3">The availability of free reallocations does not influence or relate to the calculation of index gains over time.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e7acf52-f866-478f-91af-c99f9dc14a24" target="8886f5ce-b28a-43b5-85a1-63104105310a">
  <data key="d3">The availability of free reallocation attempts does not influence how interest is credited based on participation rates and caps. These features function separately within the product's design.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e7acf52-f866-478f-91af-c99f9dc14a24" target="5af4b2af-c88c-4ee5-ab6b-3214a72b0be8">
  <data key="d3">The availability of free reallocations does not influence how the 0% floor protects against negative index returns. This statement describes operational access to rebalancing, separate from market performance safeguards.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e7acf52-f866-478f-91af-c99f9dc14a24" target="a7b1c147-442d-4852-b81d-665875dffa47">
  <data key="d3">The ability to make four free reallocations annually relates to investor flexibility in managing assets, whereas the guarantee against negative returns ensures capital preservation during market downturns. The two concepts operate independently within the product design.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e7acf52-f866-478f-91af-c99f9dc14a24" target="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd">
  <data key="d3">Free reallocations allow investors to adjust allocations frequently, supporting proactive risk control. This flexibility complements the 0% floor, which protects against negative returns during downturns.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="07ead2ce-8c62-464b-b42c-6e038b197463" target="6e7acf52-f866-478f-91af-c99f9dc14a24">
