  <data key="d3">The $25 fee for extra reallocations does not influence the cap set for the Global Diversified Index Account, nor is it affected by that cap’s value.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3" target="e56d9b1f-113b-4961-abbd-159d8047aeca">
  <data key="d3">Fees for excess reallocations apply regardless of the specific participation rate used in the indexed accounts, including the Global Diversified Index Account.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3" target="f64306b3-60d7-48b6-82c2-6580397642e1">
  <data key="d3">Each reallocation beyond four annually incurs a $25 fee, reflecting cost control measures for investor activity. This rule does not affect the structural protections like the 0% floor in the Global Diversified Index Account.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3" target="7898028b-343b-4195-9f4c-a6280a62d640">
  <data key="d3">Fees applied after four annual reallocations may prompt investors to align their rebalancing actions with the 1-year crediting period to maximize credited returns before triggering extra charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSIDERED_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3" target="db06e7c6-2f5b-4dca-9e5a-d5dd96d2c405">
  <data key="d3">Each reallocation beyond four per year incurs a $25 fee, reflecting cost management for frequent trading activity. This fee does not affect the predetermined 3.0% guarantee offered by the Fixed Account.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3" target="b24459ef-4087-463c-8274-73d1eef85c9a">
  <data key="d3">Fees apply when changing allocations more than four times annually, regardless of whether the change involves the uncapped Fixed Account.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3" target="d2272e16-5b5e-4cf0-8180-275ee09c4556">
  <data key="d3">Each reallocation beyond four per year incurs a $25 fee, incentivizing strategic timing of investment shifts rather than frequent adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3" target="5970ce74-f216-4469-89e2-77ce18166763">
  <data key="d3">Fees apply when investors exceed four annual reallocations, charging $25 per extra change. These fees have no impact on the Fixed Account’s guaranteed 3% return, which remains unchanged irrespective of such transactions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3" target="b5a49b5f-16b1-4dba-94df-96a105e6000e">
  <data key="d3">Frequent reallocations beyond four per year incur a $25 fee, which may influence decisions about maintaining or altering the existing 50% allocation to the S&amp;P 500.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3" target="13737585-4de1-4789-b42c-a05bc511593e">
  <data key="d3">Exceeding four annual reallocation requests incurs a $25 fee, potentially affecting how investors manage allocations like the 30% held in the NASDAQ-100 Index.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3" target="122014ab-154e-4331-94fc-e939755b46e6">
  <data key="d3">The $25 fee for extra reallocations affects how frequently investors modify their allocations, including the portion held in the Fixed Account, thus shaping its long-term composition based on cost considerations.</data>
  <data key="d4">IMPACTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3" target="2b2e3f84-59bf-4a6e-b26c-8b5ae353f6de">
  <data key="d3">Frequent reallocations beyond four per year trigger a $25 fee, thus imposing a cost barrier on exercising the freedom granted by changing allocations on policy anniversaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3" target="2601679e-fb90-4392-b3a8-8e4aaa913aa1">
  <data key="d3">Each reallocation beyond the initial four per year incurs a $25 fee, except when occurring on a policy anniversary, where it remains free regardless of count.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_EXEMPTION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3" target="6e7acf52-f866-478f-91af-c99f9dc14a24">
  <data key="d3">When more than four reallocation requests occur in a year, a $25 fee applies—this rule only makes sense because the initial four are explicitly stated as free.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERS_FEE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3" target="665dbf69-ad45-49be-8a49-a811282557e1">
  <data key="d3">The fee for excess reallocations does not affect how index returns are calculated; it pertains solely to administrative actions outside the indexing computation process.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3" target="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7">
  <data key="d3">The $25 fee for extra reallocations does not affect the minimum participation rate guarantee of 25%. This fee relates solely to administrative actions on asset allocation, independent of how index gains are calculated.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3" target="c4dbdf51-a4cd-4a65-8903-f269d529eefd">
  <data key="d3">The $25 fee for excess reallocations relates to investor behavior regarding asset switching, while the fixed account's 2% minimum return ensures baseline performance stability regardless of market conditions. The two facts operate independently in terms of policy design.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3" target="27176921-2e5c-44aa-bcf0-40ddf6e140f2">
  <data key="d3">The fee for excess reallocations does not affect how interest is computed from index movements and participation rates. The two concepts relate separately to cost management and profit generation.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3" target="6ff1f4bc-a2b4-4e15-b514-415d803bd39b">
  <data key="d3">The $25 fee for excess reallocations relates to investor behavior in adjusting investments, whereas the cap and floor on interest apply universally to how returns are calculated regardless of trading frequency.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3" target="5af4b2af-c88c-4ee5-ab6b-3214a72b0be8">
  <data key="d3">The $25 fee for extra reallocations is unrelated to the market decline protection offered by the 0% floor. One governs administrative cost behavior; the other safeguards against negative credits.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3" target="8886f5ce-b28a-43b5-85a1-63104105310a">
  <data key="d3">The $25 fee for excess reallocations does not influence how interest is credited to indexed accounts; it pertains solely to administrative actions outside investment performance calculations.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3" target="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a $25 fee for extra reallocations does not affect the minimum cap of 4% on index-based crediting. The cap is independently governed by product design rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3" target="a7b1c147-442d-4852-b81d-665875dffa47">
  <data key="d3">The $25 fee for extra reallocations does not affect the guarantee against negative returns during market downturns, which remains independent of trading frequency.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3" target="3fe4c74a-f6e1-4f2e-874b-5a03244e9e44">
  <data key="d3">The $25 fee for excess reallocations affects investor decisions regarding portfolio shifts, potentially influencing whether investors choose to rebalance in response to significant market movements like those described in the S&amp;P 500 example.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3" target="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd">
  <data key="d3">The $25 fee for excess reallocations is unrelated to the zero-interest guarantee during market declines, as it pertains to transaction costs rather than performance outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
