<edge source="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7" target="326a19f6-3d06-4cde-a9f0-0b1923801873">
  <data key="d3">A minimum participation rate of 25% guarantees investor exposure to index performance regardless of the cap level, such as the 8.5% cap applied to the Global Diversified Index. This constraint operates separately from cap settings.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7" target="e56d9b1f-113b-4961-abbd-159d8047aeca">
  <data key="d3">The rule requiring participation rates to remain at least 25% ensures that even lower-tier indexes maintain meaningful upside potential; thus, the 100% rate on the Global Diversified Index remains within acceptable bounds.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSTRAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7" target="f64306b3-60d7-48b6-82c2-6580397642e1">
  <data key="d3">A minimum 25% participation rate ensures meaningful credit accrual when markets rise, working alongside the 0% floor to protect against loss while still enabling positive growth potential in favorable conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7" target="7898028b-343b-4195-9f4c-a6280a62d640">
  <data key="d3">A minimum participation rate of 25% ensures that at least a quarter of index gains are credited to the investor's account regardless of the crediting period, which itself governs frequency rather than magnitude of credit application.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7" target="db06e7c6-2f5b-4dca-9e5a-d5dd96d2c405">
  <data key="d3">The 25% minimum participation rate in index-based crediting enhances downside protection by ensuring meaningful upside potential when markets rise, reinforcing confidence alongside the Fixed Account’s guaranteed 3% return, thus maintaining balanced risk management across account types.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
