  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7" target="27176921-2e5c-44aa-bcf0-40ddf6e140f2">
  <data key="d3">The minimum participation rate of 25% ensures that even if the index performs poorly or moderately, the investor still receives at least some positive credit based on the index’s movement, limiting downside exposure while enabling upside potential within cap constraints.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7" target="6ff1f4bc-a2b4-4e15-b514-415d803bd39b">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee that participation rates remain at or above 25% ensures that even under low market performance, investors receive meaningful credit toward their returns, supporting the overall protection offered by the floor and cap system.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7" target="3fe4c74a-f6e1-4f2e-874b-5a03244e9e44">
  <data key="d3">The minimum 25% participation rate ensures that any positive market movement, such as the 15% increase described, results in a proportionally reduced but still positive credited return. This cap on participation limits upside exposure while guaranteeing non-negative outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
