  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="665dbf69-ad45-49be-8a49-a811282557e1" target="b5a49b5f-16b1-4dba-94df-96a105e6000e">
  <data key="d3">The formula for computing the index percentage change determines how gains or losses are quantified annually. These results directly influence the credited amounts to the S&amp;P 500-linked account, including those tied to an existing 50% allocation.</data>
  <data key="d4">USED_IN</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="665dbf69-ad45-49be-8a49-a811282557e1" target="13737585-4de1-4789-b42c-a05bc511593e">
  <data key="d3">The formula for calculating index percentage change enables the determination of credited growth for the NASDAQ-100 Index, which directly impacts the valuation of the 30% allocated to it within the account.</data>
  <data key="d4">USED_TO_CALCULATE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="665dbf69-ad45-49be-8a49-a811282557e1" target="122014ab-154e-4331-94fc-e939755b46e6">
  <data key="d3">The index percentage change calculation governs how returns are determined for indexed accounts, independent of the current allocation to the Fixed Account.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="665dbf69-ad45-49be-8a49-a811282557e1" target="2b2e3f84-59bf-4a6e-b26c-8b5ae353f6de">
  <data key="d3">Index performance calculations take place on policy anniversaries, providing data relevant to potential reallocation decisions made by policyholders.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
