  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="665dbf69-ad45-49be-8a49-a811282557e1" target="2601679e-fb90-4392-b3a8-8e4aaa913aa1">
  <data key="d3">The index percentage change is determined annually on the policy anniversary via a standardized formula involving start and end index values. This result informs potential credited gains, influencing whether investors choose to reallocate funds, especially since such changes are permitted without penalty on the same date.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFORMS_DECISION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="665dbf69-ad45-49be-8a49-a811282557e1" target="6e7acf52-f866-478f-91af-c99f9dc14a24">
  <data key="d3">Index performance is determined annually by calculating the percentage change based on the difference between the ending and starting index values. This metric governs credited gains but has no direct connection to the cost of making investment changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="665dbf69-ad45-49be-8a49-a811282557e1" target="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3">
  <data key="d3">The method used to calculate index percentage change has no bearing on whether a fee is charged for exceeding reallocation limits.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="665dbf69-ad45-49be-8a49-a811282557e1" target="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1">
  <data key="d3">The formula in fact_sentence_2 computes the raw index growth used to determine eligibility for crediting, which may later be constrained by the 4% cap specified in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="665dbf69-ad45-49be-8a49-a811282557e1" target="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7">
  <data key="d3">The annual index percentage change serves as the foundation upon which the actual credited amount is determined, scaled by the participation rate that cannot fall below 25%.</data>
  <data key="d4">INPUT_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="665dbf69-ad45-49be-8a49-a811282557e1" target="c4dbdf51-a4cd-4a65-8903-f269d529eefd">
  <data key="d3">Index percentage changes are computed annually based on the ratio of the difference between ending and starting index values to the starting value. This metric determines potential credited gains in indexed accounts but has no direct bearing on the fixed account’s guaranteed yield.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="665dbf69-ad45-49be-8a49-a811282557e1" target="27176921-2e5c-44aa-bcf0-40ddf6e140f2">
  <data key="d3">The index percentage change, derived from the difference in index values over time, forms the basis for calculating credited interest. This percentage is essential for determining how much gain is applied to the investment via the participation rate.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="665dbf69-ad45-49be-8a49-a811282557e1" target="3fe4c74a-f6e1-4f2e-874b-5a03244e9e44">
  <data key="d3">The formula described in fact_sentence_1 enables the computation of index returns, such as the 15% gain shown in fact_sentence_2 when applying it to actual start and end values.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="665dbf69-ad45-49be-8a49-a811282557e1" target="8886f5ce-b28a-43b5-85a1-63104105310a">
  <data key="d3">The index percentage change calculated from the starting and ending index values determines the basis for potential interest credits. This figure is then applied to the participation rate and capped at the specified limit to compute the final credited amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="665dbf69-ad45-49be-8a49-a811282557e1" target="6ff1f4bc-a2b4-4e15-b514-415d803bd39b">
  <data key="d3">The index percentage change calculated on each policy anniversary forms the basis for determining how much interest is credited, which is then constrained by a predetermined cap and a minimum floor guarantee.</data>
  <data key="d4">DRIVES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="665dbf69-ad45-49be-8a49-a811282557e1" target="5af4b2af-c88c-4ee5-ab6b-3214a72b0be8">
  <data key="d3">The index percentage change computation on policy anniversaries provides the basis for determining whether the floor applies; if the result is negative (e.g., a 5% decline), the floor enforces a 0% credit.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="665dbf69-ad45-49be-8a49-a811282557e1" target="a7b1c147-442d-4852-b81d-665875dffa47">
  <data key="d3">The formula used to calculate index percentage change on each policy anniversary determines whether gains or losses occur. However, because of the 0% floor protection, any resulting negative change from the formula is effectively nullified, ensuring no negative returns for the investor.</data>
