<edge source="8886f5ce-b28a-43b5-85a1-63104105310a" target="b24459ef-4087-463c-8274-73d1eef85c9a">
  <data key="d3">Indexed accounts use caps and participation rates to limit credited interest, whereas the Fixed Account offers uncapped growth tied only to its guaranteed yield, making it structurally independent of such limits.</data>
  <data key="d4">DIFFERS_FROM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8886f5ce-b28a-43b5-85a1-63104105310a" target="d2272e16-5b5e-4cf0-8180-275ee09c4556">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence outlines the calculation method for interest credits in an indexed account when specific parameters like cap and participation rate are applied. It does not reference or depend on whether the Fixed Account has a floor, making the connection tenuous.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8886f5ce-b28a-43b5-85a1-63104105310a" target="5970ce74-f216-4469-89e2-77ce18166763">
  <data key="d3">Indexed account growth depends on factors like participation rates and caps, such as a 10.5% maximum credit with full participation, unrelated to the stable rate of the Fixed Account.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8886f5ce-b28a-43b5-85a1-63104105310a" target="b5a49b5f-16b1-4dba-94df-96a105e6000e">
  <data key="d3">The stated cap and participation rate define the maximum possible interest that could be credited from the S&amp;P 500 Index, assuming it performs well enough to reach those limits.</data>
  <data key="d4">APPLIES_TO_INDEX</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8886f5ce-b28a-43b5-85a1-63104105310a" target="13737585-4de1-4789-b42c-a05bc511593e">
  <data key="d3">A 10.5% cap and 100% participation rate apply to the NASDAQ-100 Index’s performance, meaning its contribution to the overall return is limited to 10.5% regardless of index growth, assuming full participation.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8886f5ce-b28a-43b5-85a1-63104105310a" target="122014ab-154e-4331-94fc-e939755b46e6">
  <data key="d3">The potential interest credit from an indexed account depends on its cap and participation rate; however, this has no bearing on the actual allocation percentage held in the Fixed Account.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8886f5ce-b28a-43b5-85a1-63104105310a" target="2b2e3f84-59bf-4a6e-b26c-8b5ae353f6de">
  <data key="d3">A 10.5% cap limits potential growth from an indexed account, meaning even if markets rise more, only up to 10.5% of gain is credited, regardless of when reallocating occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">LIMITS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8886f5ce-b28a-43b5-85a1-63104105310a" target="2601679e-fb90-4392-b3a8-8e4aaa913aa1">
  <data key="d3">The interest credited under a 10.5% cap and 100% participation rate depends on index performance, independent of whether allocation changes were made free of charge.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8886f5ce-b28a-43b5-85a1-63104105310a" target="6e7acf52-f866-478f-91af-c99f9dc14a24">
  <data key="d3">Interest credits depend solely on index performance metrics like participation rate and cap, regardless of whether reallocation requests were made for free or incurred fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8886f5ce-b28a-43b5-85a1-63104105310a" target="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3">
  <data key="d3">Interest credits under a 10.5% cap and 100% participation rate do not affect the cost of reallocating funds among accounts, which remains governed separately by the fee policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8886f5ce-b28a-43b5-85a1-63104105310a" target="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1">
  <data key="d3">A 10.5% cap with full participation results in a maximum credited interest of 10.5%, demonstrating how actual credits are constrained by predefined upper bounds. These caps are themselves safeguarded from falling below 4%, reinforcing long-term predictability.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXAMPLE OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8886f5ce-b28a-43b5-85a1-63104105310a" target="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7">
  <data key="d3">A 100% participation rate combined with a 10.5% cap results in maximum possible credited interest of 10.5%. This outcome is only meaningful if participation rates meet the minimum 25% requirement, ensuring investor benefits aren’t arbitrarily suppressed.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES_MINIMUM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8886f5ce-b28a-43b5-85a1-63104105310a" target="c4dbdf51-a4cd-4a65-8903-f269d529eefd">
  <data key="d3">Indexed account growth is limited by a cap (e.g., 10.5%) when combined with a participation rate (e.g., 100%), capping potential gains. This rule operates separately from the fixed account’s guaranteed yield floor of 2%.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8886f5ce-b28a-43b5-85a1-63104105310a" target="665dbf69-ad45-49be-8a49-a811282557e1">
  <data key="d3">The capped interest credit of 10.5% assumes an underlying index gain derived from the difference between the ending and starting index values over the policy year, as defined by the calculation method described earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">USED_IN_CALCULATING</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8886f5ce-b28a-43b5-85a1-63104105310a" target="27176921-2e5c-44aa-bcf0-40ddf6e140f2">
  <data key="d3">A 100% participation rate means full exposure to index gains, but the interest credited remains limited by the cap; thus, the calculation from fact_sentence_1 is bounded above by the specified cap of 10.5%.</data>
  <data key="d4">LIMITED BY CAP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8886f5ce-b28a-43b5-85a1-63104105310a" target="6ff1f4bc-a2b4-4e15-b514-415d803bd39b">
  <data key="d3">A cap on interest credited sets an upper bound regardless of underlying index gain; thus, when combined with full participation, it determines the ceiling of actual credited interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8886f5ce-b28a-43b5-85a1-63104105310a" target="3fe4c74a-f6e1-4f2e-874b-5a03244e9e44">
  <data key="d3">Given a 100% participation rate and a 10.5% cap, the maximum interest credited on the S&amp;P 500’s 15% gain is limited to 10.5%, reflecting the product’s capping mechanism.</data>
  <data key="d4">LIMITED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8886f5ce-b28a-43b5-85a1-63104105310a" target="5af4b2af-c88c-4ee5-ab6b-3214a72b0be8">
  <data key="d3">The cap limits the maximum gain from the index performance, while the floor prevents any negative credits when the index falls, ensuring investors do not lose money even if markets decline sharply.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8886f5ce-b28a-43b5-85a1-63104105310a" target="a7b1c147-442d-4852-b81d-665875dffa47">
  <data key="d3">The cap limits potential gains from positive market movements, yet the 0% floor prevents any losses when markets decline, ensuring balanced protection across market scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8886f5ce-b28a-43b5-85a1-63104105310a" target="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes the ceiling on returns based on a cap and participation rate, while fact_sentence_2 explains that despite such ceilings, investors are shielded from negative returns through a guaranteed minimum of 0%. This creates a bounded risk-reward profile.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="55971b57-5771-411a-90ed-2670e5ee1a5f" target="8886f5ce-b28a-43b5-85a1-63104105310a">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has interest capped at</data>
</edge>
