  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">GUARANTEE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5af4b2af-c88c-4ee5-ab6b-3214a72b0be8" target="07a37dc6-8a4f-42c1-a5ed-5e78f62c3abd">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">GUARANTEE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5af4b2af-c88c-4ee5-ab6b-3214a72b0be8" target="326a19f6-3d06-4cde-a9f0-0b1923801873">
  <data key="d3">A 5% decline in the index triggers the 0% floor protection, preventing negative credits; meanwhile, any gain remains limited by the 8.5% cap, illustrating how both bounds shape performance outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES LIMITS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5af4b2af-c88c-4ee5-ab6b-3214a72b0be8" target="e56d9b1f-113b-4961-abbd-159d8047aeca">
  <data key="d3">The presence of a 0% floor ensures investors won’t lose money even if the index falls sharply, which complements the 100% participation rate by preserving upside potential without downside risk.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5af4b2af-c88c-4ee5-ab6b-3214a72b0be8" target="f64306b3-60d7-48b6-82c2-6580397642e1">
  <data key="d3">A decline of 5% in the index triggers the protective feature of the 0% floor, guaranteeing that the credited interest does not fall below zero.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5af4b2af-c88c-4ee5-ab6b-3214a72b0be8" target="7898028b-343b-4195-9f4c-a6280a62d640">
  <data key="d3">The 0% floor rule applies specifically during the 1-year crediting period, ensuring investors do not lose money even if the index declines significantly over that term.</data>
  <data key="d4">APPLIES_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5af4b2af-c88c-4ee5-ab6b-3214a72b0be8" target="db06e7c6-2f5b-4dca-9e5a-d5dd96d2c405">
  <data key="d3">During market declines such as a 5% drop, the 0% floor safeguards investors from losing money on indexed accounts, preventing negative returns. Meanwhile, the Fixed Account continues to earn its guaranteed 3% yield irrespective of market volatility.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5af4b2af-c88c-4ee5-ab6b-3214a72b0be8" target="b24459ef-4087-463c-8274-73d1eef85c9a">
  <data key="d3">The 0% floor prevents any negative interest credits during market downturns, protecting indexed account balances. However, since the Fixed Account lacks a cap, its returns may exceed those of indexed accounts under strong market conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5af4b2af-c88c-4ee5-ab6b-3214a72b0be8" target="d2272e16-5b5e-4cf0-8180-275ee09c4556">
  <data key="d3">While the floor prevents loss in indexed accounts during downturns, it does not apply to the Fixed Account, which operates independently without such protective features.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5af4b2af-c88c-4ee5-ab6b-3214a72b0be8" target="5970ce74-f216-4469-89e2-77ce18166763">
  <data key="d3">During a 5% market decline, the 0% floor protects indexed account earnings from going negative. Meanwhile, the Fixed Account continues earning its guaranteed 3% annually, unaffected by such fluctuations.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5af4b2af-c88c-4ee5-ab6b-3214a72b0be8" target="b5a49b5f-16b1-4dba-94df-96a105e6000e">
  <data key="d3">The 0% floor safeguards investors' credited interest when the underlying index falls; thus, regardless of the 50% allocation to the S&amp;P 500 Index, any potential losses from market declines are absorbed due to this built-in protection.</data>
  <data key="d4">PROTECTED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5af4b2af-c88c-4ee5-ab6b-3214a72b0be8" target="13737585-4de1-4789-b42c-a05bc511593e">
  <data key="d3">If the NASDAQ-100 Index falls by 5%, the investor’s credited interest cannot go below zero due to the established floor, regardless of the 30% allocation.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERS_FLOOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5af4b2af-c88c-4ee5-ab6b-3214a72b0be8" target="122014ab-154e-4331-94fc-e939755b46e6">
  <data key="d3">The 0% floor protects against negative returns when indices decline, ensuring non-negative interest credits regardless of allocation percentages. This safeguard operates independently of the specific portion allocated to the Fixed Account.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5af4b2af-c88c-4ee5-ab6b-3214a72b0be8" target="2b2e3f84-59bf-4a6e-b26c-8b5ae353f6de">
  <data key="d3">The presence of a 0% floor during index declines has no impact on the frequency or timing of allowed portfolio adjustments by policyholders.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5af4b2af-c88c-4ee5-ab6b-3214a72b0be8" target="2601679e-fb90-4392-b3a8-8e4aaa913aa1">
  <data key="d3">If an index drops by 5%, the contract's 0% floor prevents any loss of principal through negative interest credits. This safeguard operates regardless of whether allocation changes occur, including those made free of charge on policy anniversaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5af4b2af-c88c-4ee5-ab6b-3214a72b0be8" target="6e7acf52-f866-478f-91af-c99f9dc14a24">
  <data key="d3">The presence of a 0% floor during market downturns has no bearing on whether reallocation attempts incur fees. It relates solely to credit calculation under declining markets, independent of transaction costs.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5af4b2af-c88c-4ee5-ab6b-3214a72b0be8" target="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3">
  <data key="d3">The 0% floor prevents loss when indices fall, independent of any fees associated with changing allocations. This safety net operates regardless of how often investors rebalance.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5af4b2af-c88c-4ee5-ab6b-3214a72b0be8" target="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1">
  <data key="d3">A 5% decline in the index triggers a 0% floor on credited interest, protecting investors from losses. This protection complements the 4% minimum cap requirement, ensuring stable and bounded outcomes across varying market scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5af4b2af-c88c-4ee5-ab6b-3214a72b0be8" target="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7">
  <data key="d3">The 0% floor safeguards investors from losing money on downturns, making the presence of a minimum 25% participation rate more valuable by protecting potential gains during volatile periods.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5af4b2af-c88c-4ee5-ab6b-3214a72b0be8" target="c4dbdf51-a4cd-4a65-8903-f269d529eefd">
  <data key="d3">During market downturns, such as a 5% drop, the indexed accounts’ credits are floored at 0%, preventing negative returns. This safeguard operates separately from the fixed account’s guaranteed 2% yield.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5af4b2af-c88c-4ee5-ab6b-3214a72b0be8" target="665dbf69-ad45-49be-8a49-a811282557e1">
  <data key="d3">The 0% floor protects investors from losses due to declining indices, ensuring that even if the index percentage change derived from sentence 1 shows a drop like 5%, no negative interest is applied.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
