<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="326a19f6-3d06-4cde-a9f0-0b1923801873">
  <data key="d3">Despite the existence of a cap at 8.5% on the Global Diversified Index Account, the 0% floor protects investors from losing principal or earning negative returns when markets decline, ensuring minimum stability in performance outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d4">PROTECTS AGAINST</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="e56d9b1f-113b-4961-abbd-159d8047aeca">
  <data key="d3">Even though the Global Diversified Index Account offers full participation in gains, its design includes a 0% floor ensuring no loss of credited interest during market declines.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES POTENTIAL</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="f64306b3-60d7-48b6-82c2-6580397642e1">
  <data key="d3">The possibility of earning zero interest in the worst-case market scenario arises because the index account includes a 0% floor protection against losses.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="7898028b-343b-4195-9f4c-a6280a62d640">
  <data key="d3">Even though the crediting period is set at 1 year, the possibility of zero interest remains due to the 0% floor protection against negative market movements.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="db06e7c6-2f5b-4dca-9e5a-d5dd96d2c405">
  <data key="d3">A worst-case scenario of zero interest credits arises when indexed accounts perform poorly, reflecting downside risk inherent in those vehicles. This does not affect the Fixed Account, which maintains its guaranteed 3% yield regardless of market movements.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="b24459ef-4087-463c-8274-73d1eef85c9a">
  <data key="d3">The worst-case scenario of zero interest from market declines only affects indexed accounts; since the Fixed Account lacks a cap, it remains immune to such risks and continues earning guaranteed returns regardless.</data>
  <data key="d4">UNRELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="d2272e16-5b5e-4cf0-8180-275ee09c4556">
  <data key="d3">Since the Fixed Account ensures at least a 3% return regardless of market conditions, the risk of earning zero interest due to market decline does not apply to this component, making the lack of a floor irrelevant to such an extreme outcome.</data>
  <data key="d4">IRRELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="5970ce74-f216-4469-89e2-77ce18166763">
  <data key="d3">Zero interest due to market decline pertains solely to indexed accounts under poor performance, while the Fixed Account maintains its guaranteed 3% yield irrespective of such events.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="b5a49b5f-16b1-4dba-94df-96a105e6000e">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of zero interest in downturns reflects the protection built into the indexing mechanism, meaning that even with a high allocation like 50% to the S&amp;P 500, investors cannot lose principal—but also may receive no credit during poor market periods.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="13737585-4de1-4789-b42c-a05bc511593e">
  <data key="d3">The 0% floor protects investors against losses in volatile markets, ensuring that even if the NASDAQ-100 index drops, the credited return won’t fall below zero, regardless of its allocation.</data>
  <data key="d4">PROTECTS AGAINST</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="122014ab-154e-4331-94fc-e939755b46e6">
  <data key="d3">Even if the markets decline sharply, resulting in zero interest credited under worst-case conditions, the investor’s exposure remains protected by the 0% floor, independent of the 20% allocated to the Fixed Account.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="2b2e3f84-59bf-4a6e-b26c-8b5ae353f6de">
  <data key="d3">Even if market performance leads to zero credits due to declines, policyholders retain full control through periodic reallocations, enabling proactive adjustments to mitigate future risks or shift toward more stable assets like the fixed account.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="2601679e-fb90-4392-b3a8-8e4aaa913aa1">
  <data key="d3">The 0% floor protects investors from losing value during market drops, making it safer to make frequent allocation shifts. Since such changes incur no cost on policy anniversaries, holders can realign portfolios without penalty, enhancing control over risk exposure.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES FLEXIBILITY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="6e7acf52-f866-478f-91af-c99f9dc14a24">
  <data key="d3">Even in severe market declines, the 0% floor prevents any loss of credited interest, making it safe to use the available free reallocations to shift assets without fear of compounding losses.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3">
  <data key="d3">The absence of interest credit in a declining market is independent of any fees charged for reallocating funds, as it stems from protective design features, not cost structures.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1">
  <data key="d3">Even if the market declines, the policyholder’s credit is protected at 0%, meaning no loss occurs. This safety net complements the cap rule, which limits upside potential but maintains predictability.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7">
  <data key="d3">Even in scenarios where the market declines significantly, the 0% floor prevents any negative crediting; combined with a 25% minimum participation rate, this ensures non-negative returns under adverse conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENSURES MINIMUM RETURN</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="c4dbdf51-a4cd-4a65-8903-f269d529eefd">
  <data key="d3">During market declines, the indexed accounts offer a 0% floor, meaning no loss of principal or credit, though actual interest earned could be zero. The fixed account provides an alternative safety net with a guaranteed minimum yield of 2%, unaffected by such scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="665dbf69-ad45-49be-8a49-a811282557e1">
  <data key="d3">If the index percentage change computed via the given formula results in a negative value, the policyholder receives no interest credit, reflecting the protective 0% floor feature.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="27176921-2e5c-44aa-bcf0-40ddf6e140f2">
  <data key="d3">The 0% floor ensures that despite any negative index movement, the interest credited cannot go below zero, which is enforced through the application of the participation rate formula.</data>
  <data key="d4">IS ENFORCED BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="6ff1f4bc-a2b4-4e15-b514-415d803bd39b">
  <data key="d3">Zero interest credited in a declining market occurs because the product includes a 0% floor on returns, preventing negative credits despite poor performance.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESULT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="3fe4c74a-f6e1-4f2e-874b-5a03244e9e44">
  <data key="d3">The 0% floor protects investors from losing value when markets decline, ensuring that despite strong upward movements like a 15% rise in the S&amp;P 500, the credit mechanism still safeguards against any possibility of negative returns.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="5af4b2af-c88c-4ee5-ab6b-3214a72b0be8">
  <data key="d3">The worst-case outcome for investors—earning zero interest—is realized precisely when the index declines, triggering the 0% floor protection. Thus, the floor mechanism enforces this limit on downside risk.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="a7b1c147-442d-4852-b81d-665875dffa47">
  <data key="d3">Since the worst-case scenario is zero interest credited when markets fall, it confirms that investors cannot lose money, meaning declines never cause negative returns.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="8886f5ce-b28a-43b5-85a1-63104105310a">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 highlights the safety net preventing any loss, which contextualizes why the cap in fact_sentence_1 does not pose a downside risk—it only limits upside, ensuring the outcome never falls below zero.</data>
  <data key="d4">PROTECTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 highlights the worst-case outcome of zero interest during market decline, which is fully consistent with the floor protection mentioned in fact_sentence_2. The guarantee prevents losses even if the index drops by 5%, validating the zero-interest ceiling as realistic and protective.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains that the variable annuity has a 0% floor ensuring no negative interest credits during market declines, which corresponds directly to the floor protection described in fact_sentence_2, where the policy also protects against losses regardless of index drop magnitude.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains that zero interest may be credited when markets fall, and fact_sentence_2 confirms this occurs specifically when the index drops by 5%, illustrating a concrete instance of the general rule outlined in chunk_summary_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="70667dae-ff8c-4bac-bf04-03807ddb6bd7">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 highlights that zero interest may be credited during market declines, consistent with the guarantee stated in fact_sentence_2 that principal remains intact regardless of market performance.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of zero interest in adverse markets (fact_sentence_1) ensures stability regardless of premiums paid, which may influence long-term strategy but isn't affected by the $100 minimum premium requirement.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2">
  <data key="d3">The potential for zero interest credits due to market decline relates to performance mechanics, whereas the $50,000 premium cap defines funding constraints. These elements address separate operational facets of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 describes potential zero interest outcomes in indexed accounts during market declines, which reflects risk management features in the investment portion of the product. In contrast, fact_sentence_2 specifies the minimum allowable premium payment for a related life insurance component, highlighting a distinct operational constraint unrelated to performance mechanisms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
