<edge source="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db" target="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299">
  <data key="d3">The floor protection guarantees no loss on investment returns during a 5% drop in the index, and this safeguard operates because the floor protection level is fixed at 0%, preventing any negative performance.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db" target="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7">
  <data key="d3">The floor protection guarantees no loss when the index falls by 5%, resulting in zero interest being credited to the account because the minimum return is capped at zero.</data>
  <data key="d4">IMPLIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db" target="50dee1d7-a696-448d-92e6-11dfe14d068f">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee against market losses up to 5% does not affect when premiums may be paid. This clause focuses solely on protecting investment returns under adverse conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db" target="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1">
  <data key="d3">Floor protection guarantees no loss on index decline, meaning the minimum return is 0%. This directly results in the worst-case scenario being a 0% return.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db" target="70667dae-ff8c-4bac-bf04-03807ddb6bd7">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains how floor protection activates during a 5% market decline, preventing any loss. This directly supports fact_sentence_2, which confirms that such a decline results in no loss of principal.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db" target="86b72d75-5a59-44c2-b2d6-912ce393cf76">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee against losses due to a 5% index drop provides financial stability regardless of market conditions. This does not influence or rely upon the timing flexibility of premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db" target="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of no negative return during a 5% index drop protects the policyholder’s investment integrity regardless of premium levels. This safeguard operates independently of the minimum premium requirement set at $100 per payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db" target="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of no loss during a 5% index drop protects the policyholder’s account value regardless of market performance. This safeguard operates independently of the minimum premium requirement set at $100 per payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db" target="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence explains how the policy protects against market losses through a 5% floor, ensuring returns do not go below zero. The second sentence specifies the upper limit for annual premiums, setting a boundary on contributor outlays.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db" target="0d35c1ce-d96d-4562-80f8-0654abe126d2">
  <data key="d3">The floor protection prevents losses if the index falls by up to 5%, maintaining account value stability. This safeguard operates independently of the $50,000 annual premium cap, which is set to meet IRS tax qualification requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db" target="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6">
  <data key="d3">Floor protection prevents losses during market downturns, making the recommended contribution more reliable under adverse conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d3">Floor protection ensures the account maintains value during market downturns, preserving funds needed to cover future monthly fees and allowing temporary skips in premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db" target="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae">
  <data key="d3">Floor protection prevents losses during market declines, maintaining account value integrity. This preserved value supports continued coverage even when premiums are skipped, enabling payment flexibility without immediate lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">Floor protection prevents losses on investment returns when the index falls by 5%, preserving capital integrity. This safeguard supports long-term financial security, making it easier to meet sustained premium payments required to keep coverage active through age 100.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db" target="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a">
  <data key="d3">Floor protection prevents losses during market downturns, maintaining policy value stability regardless of index performance. This safeguard contributes to overall policy reliability, indirectly supporting its long-term viability.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">The floor protection prevents losses during market declines, maintaining account value integrity regardless of index performance. This safeguard operates independently of the premium load, which reduces the amount credited to the account after deduction.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">Floor protection prevents losses when the index falls by up to 5%, maintaining account value integrity. This safeguard operates independently of the monthly deduction of Cost of Insurance (COI).</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db" target="9639c325-d6a7-4181-a801-0a4fdfaefa94">
  <data key="d3">The floor protection guarantees no loss if the index falls by 5%, maintaining account stability regardless of market conditions. This stable foundation indirectly supports consistent calculation of the COI charge, though it does not determine its amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db" target="749f8b25-e9c6-4e2e-a60a-5fdcef1215c4">
  <data key="d3">Floor protection prevents losses during market declines, maintaining account stability. This contrasts with the COI charge, which reduces the account value based on mortality costs.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db" target="6bfb8452-bcec-4db6-b212-fd25bdcfbc79">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee against market decline up to 5% protects the policyholder’s account value from downside risk. This mechanism operates independently of the fixed monthly administrative charge of $12.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db" target="0b7e0a06-5166-489d-a873-3b798f915e2c">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee against losses due to a 5% index drop provides financial stability, independent of ongoing monthly charge structures like COI and admin fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db" target="1b6d4d68-07ed-4c80-987c-ddf958d36f08">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of no loss during a 5% index drop protects the account's value, indirectly preserving funds available before monthly deductions occur.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db" target="e2637b0a-dd20-4e01-8fa1-8779d2f346fa">
  <data key="d3">Floor protection prevents losses during market declines, maintaining account value integrity. This complements the guaranteed non-increase of COI rates, enhancing long-term financial predictability.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db" target="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 shows the real-world impact of the Floor Rate by describing a scenario where a 5% drop leads to no negative return, which aligns exactly with the definition provided in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONFIRMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db" target="faf66c9e-da0e-4813-9561-2d1480419596">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 highlights the protective role of the floor during market downturns, which is made possible by the 0% floor rate explicitly mentioned in chunk_summary_1, supporting the high participation rate's effectiveness under adverse conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db" target="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3">
  <data key="d3">The presence of floor protection during index declines, stated in fact_sentence_2, is made possible by the 0% floor rate inherent in the Point-to-Point Method described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
