  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERCENTAGE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="5c58875b-7841-4d7a-babc-c578b6872fb4">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CHARGE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="e2c793d4-cf9e-44be-a2fe-4dcc6475113b">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CHARGE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="5a9f5794-1230-4d60-b344-0ab510133329">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CHARGE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="7fd5f01c-66b3-432d-97b0-24acc72a9cdf">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DATE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db">
  <data key="d3">The worst possible outcome—earning 0% interest—is made possible because the policy includes floor protection preventing any negative returns during market downturns.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299">
  <data key="d3">If the worst-case scenario occurs—earning 0% interest—it confirms the effectiveness of the 0% floor protection, which prevents any decline in the account value despite adverse market conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7">
  <data key="d3">Earning 0% interest for the year occurs specifically when the index decline reaches or exceeds 5%, triggering the floor on interest crediting.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITION_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="70667dae-ff8c-4bac-bf04-03807ddb6bd7">
  <data key="d3">Since the policyholder cannot lose money due to market downturns, the maximum downside risk is capped at earning nothing—an outcome consistent with the principle described in the prior statement about guaranteed protection.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS_FROM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="50dee1d7-a696-448d-92e6-11dfe14d068f">
  <data key="d3">The statement about earning 0% interest describes a possible investment result during poor market performance, independent of when premiums are paid. This does not affect or rely upon the timing flexibility of premium contributions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="86b72d75-5a59-44c2-b2d6-912ce393cf76">
  <data key="d3">The statement about earning 0% interest describes a possible financial outcome due to market conditions, independent of when premiums are paid. This does not influence nor depend on the flexibility of payment timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176">
  <data key="d3">The statement about earning 0% interest describes a possible investment outcome, independent of the minimum premium requirement. It does not explain or rely on the $100 floor for contributions.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa">
  <data key="d3">The worst-case interest scenario does not affect the minimum required premium payment, which remains fixed regardless of investment outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2">
  <data key="d3">The worst-case interest scenario reflects performance risk, whereas the maximum premium amount defines a contractual payment ceiling unrelated to investment outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6">
  <data key="d3">The worst-case scenario of earning 0% interest hinges on the accuracy of the underlying actuarial and financial assumptions used to model risk and returns.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="0d35c1ce-d96d-4562-80f8-0654abe126d2">
  <data key="d3">The statement about earning 0% interest describes a possible financial outcome for the policyholder's account value. This does not relate directly to the reason behind the $50,000 annual premium cap, which is based on IRS tax qualification rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">A 0% interest rate represents a significant risk to policy sustainability; contributing $6,000 annually helps offset such losses and ensures continued coverage through age 100 despite poor performance.</data>
  <data key="d4">MITIGATES RISK</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d3">If the policyholder earns 0% interest, the account value grows minimally or stagnates, making it harder to maintain sufficient funds to cover monthly charges without additional contributions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INHIBITS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a">
  <data key="d3">The statement about earning 0% interest describes a possible result of poor investment performance, independent of how premiums are allocated toward administrative costs.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae">
  <data key="d3">If the policy earns 0% interest, the account value remains stagnant, increasing reliance on existing balances to cover ongoing costs. This makes it more likely that skipped premiums can still be tolerated as long as the account holds enough to absorb monthly fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES RISK MITIGATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.78</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">A 0% interest result may occur due to poor investment performance despite regular Cost of Insurance deductions affecting account value.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">If the policyholder pays premiums subject to a 3.5% load, less money is allocated to the account value, increasing the chance that the investment earns 0% interest over the year due to fees eroding gains.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="9639c325-d6a7-4181-a801-0a4fdfaefa94">
  <data key="d3">A zero-interest scenario impacts overall account growth, indirectly affecting the account value over time, which influences the basis for calculating monthly COI deductions tied to the difference between the death benefit and account value.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="749f8b25-e9c6-4e2e-a60a-5fdcef1215c4">
  <data key="d3">The statement about earning 0% interest describes a possible investment result, whereas the second sentence explains how the monthly cost-of-insurance charge is calculated based on death benefit and account value differences. These concepts operate independently in the policy’s mechanics.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="6bfb8452-bcec-4db6-b212-fd25bdcfbc79">
  <data key="d3">A zero percent interest return represents the lowest possible investment gain, affecting overall policy growth. This outcome occurs independently of the fixed $12 monthly administrative charge, which is consistently deducted regardless of returns.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="0b7e0a06-5166-489d-a873-3b798f915e2c">
  <data key="d3">The statement about earning 0% interest highlights a worst-case performance scenario, whereas the mention of total monthly charges clarifies what portions of the account value are deducted regularly. These elements address different dimensions of policy economics without direct causal or sequential dependence.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="1b6d4d68-07ed-4c80-987c-ddf958d36f08">
  <data key="d3">If the policy earns 0% interest, it means the account value does not grow despite any contributions. This stagnant balance may still be subject to monthly deductions, potentially reducing its size over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="e2637b0a-dd20-4e01-8fa1-8779d2f346fa">
  <data key="d3">A zero percent interest rate represents the lowest possible return on the policy’s account value, potentially reducing growth over time. However, since COI rates are locked at guaranteed maximums, the policyholder's exposure to rising insurance costs remains controlled regardless of poor performance.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77">
  <data key="d3">The worst-case scenario of earning 0% interest corresponds exactly to the Floor Rate's function, confirming that the 0% floor prevents any downside risk from market losses.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="faf66c9e-da0e-4813-9561-2d1480419596">
  <data key="d3">The assurance of earning at least 0% interest under adverse conditions is consistent with the 0% floor rate implied by the 100% Participation Rate on the S&amp;P 500 Index Account.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of earning at least 0% interest stems directly from the 0% floor embedded in the Point-to-Point Method’s design, making it consistent with the stated risk mitigation.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2bcdf3e6-a8e7-4e02-a72f-1005c4cd7478" target="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">limits minimum interest</data>
</edge>
