</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db">
  <data key="d3">A mandatory minimum premium of $100 per payment ensures consistent funding into the policy, enabling sustained access to benefits like the 5% floor protection, though it does not affect how the protection mechanism functions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299">
  <data key="d3">A mandatory minimum premium of $100 per payment enables access to the full suite of policy benefits, including the 0% floor protection, which prevents any decline in account value despite adverse market movements.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7">
  <data key="d3">A mandatory minimum premium of $100 per payment helps ensure ongoing funding of the policy, enabling it to maintain its protective features, such as the 5% downside buffer where no interest is lost despite market decline.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="70667dae-ff8c-4bac-bf04-03807ddb6bd7">
  <data key="d3">Maintaining a minimum annual premium of $100 helps ensure the policy's continued operation, thereby preserving the guaranteed protection against market losses described in the first statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES GUARANTEE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1">
  <data key="d3">The rule that premiums must be at least $100 sets a baseline for funding the policy, unrelated to whether the policy earns zero interest over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="50dee1d7-a696-448d-92e6-11dfe14d068f">
  <data key="d3">The rule requiring each premium payment to be at least $100 limits how frequently or when smaller amounts may be contributed, thereby shaping the practical application of the flexible payment schedule described earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="86b72d75-5a59-44c2-b2d6-912ce393cf76">
  <data key="d3">A mandatory minimum payment of $100 ensures that every premium contributes meaningfully, regardless of how frequently or irregularly payments are made within the allowed timeframe.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes the lower limit for premium payments, and fact_sentence_2 confirms this limit explicitly, reinforcing consistency in policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">REINFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 specifies the minimum allowable premium amount, ensuring that contributions meet a baseline threshold. This limit complements fact_sentence_2, which defines the cap on how much can be contributed annually.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="0d35c1ce-d96d-4562-80f8-0654abe126d2">
  <data key="d3">The $100 minimum ensures basic eligibility for contributions, while the $50,000 ceiling reflects compliance with federal tax regulations governing qualified plans.</data>
  <data key="d4">BOUNDARY_LIMITS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that premiums be at least $100 sets a baseline for eligibility, enabling individuals to participate in the plan. This floor supports the feasibility of the recommended $6,000 annual contribution, which ensures sustained coverage through retirement.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae">
  <data key="d3">The minimum $100 premium ensures that any contributions made meet basic eligibility requirements, enabling future flexibility such as skipping payments when account balances remain adequate.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d3">A minimum premium of $100 ensures adequate funding, enabling the account value to remain high enough to absorb monthly charges and permit temporary skips in premium payments without lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 defines the lower limit for premiums, ensuring affordability constraints are met. This constraint supports the viability of the recommended $6,000 annual contribution only if underlying assumptions remain stable.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the lower limit for premiums, ensuring that any payment subject to the 3.5% load meets a baseline requirement. Without this minimum, the load would have no meaningful application.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that premiums be at least $100 ensures sufficient funding into the policy, which indirectly supports the ability to cover ongoing costs like the monthly Cost of Insurance charge.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a">
  <data key="d3">The minimum premium amount of $100 ensures enough capital enters the system to support the application of the 3.5% load, which covers essential administrative and operational costs.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="9639c325-d6a7-4181-a801-0a4fdfaefa94">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that premiums be at least $100 ensures sufficient contributions enter the account, indirectly supporting the account value used in calculating the monthly COI deduction. However, the COI itself is determined solely by the difference between the death benefit and current account value, independent of the minimum premium amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="0b7e0a06-5166-489d-a873-3b798f915e2c">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that premiums be at least $100 ensures sufficient funding into the policy, which indirectly supports the ability to cover ongoing monthly charges like COI and admin fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="6bfb8452-bcec-4db6-b212-fd25bdcfbc79">
  <data key="d3">The minimum premium amount required ensures sufficient funding into the policy, while the administrative charge represents a recurring deduction from the account balance regardless of premium size.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="749f8b25-e9c6-4e2e-a60a-5fdcef1215c4">
  <data key="d3">A minimum premium of $100 ensures sufficient funds enter the policy, indirectly supporting the account value that feeds into the COI calculation. Without adequate contributions, the account value may decline, affecting future COI costs.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="1b6d4d68-07ed-4c80-987c-ddf958d36f08">
  <data key="d3">The minimum premium amount ensures sufficient funds enter the account before monthly charges are applied. This foundational rule supports the feasibility of deducting total charges from the account balance.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="e2637b0a-dd20-4e01-8fa1-8779d2f346fa">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that each premium payment be at least $100 supports ongoing policy funding, enabling the maintenance of benefits under which the guaranteed COI rates apply. Without sufficient regular contributions, the policy may lapse, undermining the effectiveness of fixed COI protections.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="f64306b3-60d7-48b6-82c2-6580397642e1">
  <data key="d3">The $100 minimum premium ensures participants can contribute to the annuity product, thereby gaining exposure to the Global Diversified Index Account’s 0% floor, which safeguards their invested amount against market decline.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_ACCESS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="a7b1c147-442d-4852-b81d-665875dffa47">
  <data key="d3">The $100 minimum premium ensures sufficient capital flow into the policy, supporting the overall stability of the product's guarantees—including the zero-floor protection discussed in fact_sentence_1—but the specific safeguard itself operates independently of premium size.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd">
  <data key="d3">The $100 minimum premium (fact_sentence_2) enables access to the policy’s features—including the 0% floor on interest credits—but has no impact on whether those credits are applied.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that each premium be at least $100 supports ongoing policy maintenance, reducing the risk of lapse and thereby influencing whether surrender charges would ever come into play due to premature cancellation.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018">
  <data key="d3">The minimum premium of $100 ensures sufficient funding to trigger potential surrender charges, such as the 10% fee in Year 1, meaning higher contributions increase the base upon which fees may be applied.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that each premium be at least $100 ensures sufficient funding to trigger applicable surrender charges like the 9% fee in Year 2, linking initial contributions to later exit costs.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332">
  <data key="d3">A minimum premium of $100 per payment supports sustained policy funding, which affects the basis for calculating surrender charges like the 7% fee in Year 4.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633">
  <data key="d3">The minimum premium requirement ensures sufficient funding that contributes to the basis for calculating surrender charges later in the policy term, such as the 6% charge in Year 5.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b">
  <data key="d3">The $100 minimum premium requirement ensures sufficient funding into the policy, affecting the base upon which the Year 3 surrender charge of 8% is applied. Without meeting this floor, the policy may lapse before such fees become relevant.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="84b84dec-45b7-4ca8-ae2f-a68466866f24">
  <data key="d3">The minimum premium of $100 ensures consistent funding, which indirectly supports maintaining the policy through Year 6 when a 5% surrender charge applies. Without sufficient contributions, the risk of lapsing increases before reaching later years where surrender fees decline.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that each premium be at least $100 ensures sufficient funding to trigger applicable surrender charges like the 4% fee in Year 7, linking initial payment thresholds to later withdrawal penalties.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75">
  <data key="d3">The $100 minimum premium ensures sufficient funding to maintain the policy’s longevity, reducing the risk of lapsing before Year 8, thereby influencing whether the 3% surrender charge would be incurred upon withdrawal.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00">
  <data key="d3">Meeting the $100 minimum premium ensures ongoing policy validity into later years like Year 9, when surrender charges remain applicable. Without sufficient payments, the policy may lapse before reaching such stages.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">The minimum premium requirement supports sustained policy funding, indirectly enabling the accumulation of account value that would be subject to surrender charges like the 1% fee in Year 10.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">The minimum premium requirement ensures sufficient contributions to maintain policy integrity over time, indirectly supporting long-term stability that aligns with lower surrender charges in later years like Year 11.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that each premium be at least $100 ensures sufficient contributions accumulate into the account value, which is a key factor in determining the cash surrender value described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that each premium payment be at least $100 ensures that there are meaningful contributions subject to surrender charges during the initial decade, enabling the surrender charge formula to function as intended.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">The requirement of a minimum $100 premium enables ongoing policy maintenance, supporting the viability of staying past Year 12 when surrender charges end, thus aligning with the long-term benefits outlined in the second fact.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="473055d4-24c0-4cd9-9fea-2517f653d142" target="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">minimum required amount</data>
</edge>
<edge source="349ab3be-d843-4617-9193-0fe90f6ed328" target="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">contributes_to_premium</data>
