  <data key="d4">CHARGE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="8bc470ae-59fc-49fc-8e17-d0824413bdaa">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DATE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence defines the highest allowable annual premium amount at $50,000. This figure does not affect nor depend on the mechanism described in the first sentence, which governs downside protection regardless of premium level.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299">
  <data key="d3">The cap on annual premiums does not affect the guarantee of zero loss during market declines.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7">
  <data key="d3">The maximum allowable annual premium of $50,000 sets a financial ceiling for contributions, separate from the policy’s built-in protections like the 5% buffer on index losses.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="70667dae-ff8c-4bac-bf04-03807ddb6bd7">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence establishes a hard limit of $50,000 on yearly premiums, defining contributor capacity. The first sentence assures that such contributions remain protected from market losses, reinforcing confidence in the policy’s design.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1">
  <data key="d3">The $50,000 annual premium cap sets a funding limit, independent of how much interest might be earned over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="50dee1d7-a696-448d-92e6-11dfe14d068f">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a $50,000 annual upper limit on premium payments defines the financial boundary within which the flexible timing of payments described in the first sentence is constrained.</data>
  <data key="d4">QUANTITATIVE_BOUNDARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="86b72d75-5a59-44c2-b2d6-912ce393cf76">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a $50,000 annual ceiling on premium payments sets a clear monetary boundary, ensuring that despite flexible timing, contributions cannot exceed this threshold regardless of when they're made.</data>
  <data key="d4">BOUNDARY_SETS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 sets the upper limit for annual premiums, defining the highest possible contribution. This boundary works in tandem with fact_sentence_1, which ensures payments do not fall below $100.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies the highest allowable annual premium at $50,000, providing context for the scale of payments. Fact_sentence_1 ensures that even small contributions down to $100 remain viable.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY_LIMITS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="0d35c1ce-d96d-4562-80f8-0654abe126d2">
  <data key="d3">The $50,000 annual premium cap exists because it meets IRS requirements for qualified life insurance policies, ensuring favorable tax treatment.</data>
  <data key="d4">JUSTIFIED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">A recommended annual premium of $6,000 ensures sustained coverage until age 100, operating under the cap established by the maximum allowable premium of $50,000 per year.</data>
  <data key="d4">WITHIN_LIMITS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae">
  <data key="d3">The $50,000 annual premium cap sets the upper bound for contributions, enabling sufficient accumulation in the account so that future skipped payments can still be covered by existing funds.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes the cap on premiums, while fact_sentence_2 clarifies that recommendations like those involving specific amounts depend on underlying assumptions, implying the limits might shift if assumptions change.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUALIZES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d3">The $50,000 annual premium cap enables higher accumulation in the account value, which supports the flexibility to skip future payments without lapsing coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">The $50,000 annual premium cap defines the maximum amount subject to the 3.5% load, ensuring the charge is consistently applied across all eligible contributions.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">The maximum annual premium of $50,000 sets a boundary for contributions, while the Cost of Insurance is subtracted monthly from the account value regardless of the premium level.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a">
  <data key="d3">The maximum annual premium of $50,000 sets a financial boundary for contributions, within which the 3.5% load is applied uniformly. This load helps fund administrative and operational costs regardless of the exact amount paid up to the cap.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="6bfb8452-bcec-4db6-b212-fd25bdcfbc79">
  <data key="d3">The maximum allowable annual premium is capped at $50,000, which sets a boundary for contributions. This figure does not influence or relate directly to the fixed monthly administrative charge of $12.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="749f8b25-e9c6-4e2e-a60a-5fdcef1215c4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the upper bound for annual premiums, which influences overall funding capacity. Fact_sentence_2 explains how the monthly cost-of-insurance charge is computed using current account and death benefits, independent of premium amount caps.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="9639c325-d6a7-4181-a801-0a4fdfaefa94">
  <data key="d3">The upper limit on annual premiums ($50,000) defines the funding ceiling, but it does not impact how the monthly cost-of-insurance is computed based on the death benefit-account value spread.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="0b7e0a06-5166-489d-a873-3b798f915e2c">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the cap on yearly contributions, whereas fact_sentence_2 explains that ongoing costs are assessed monthly through separate deductions. The information complements the broader financial framework but does not logically depend on one another.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="1b6d4d68-07ed-4c80-987c-ddf958d36f08">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the upper bound for annual premiums, independent of when fees are applied. Fact_sentence_2 specifies that total charges are subtracted from the account balance on a fixed date each month, regardless of the premium amount paid.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="e2637b0a-dd20-4e01-8fa1-8779d2f346fa">
  <data key="d3">The maximum annual premium amount does not affect the guarantee that COI rates won't exceed scheduled levels. These are independent features governing different aspects of the policy’s financial structure.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="f64306b3-60d7-48b6-82c2-6580397642e1">
  <data key="d3">The $50,000 annual premium cap sets a ceiling on investor contributions, influencing total exposure to the indexed accounts. However, it does not affect the structural design of the 0% floor, which remains active irrespective of contribution levels.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="a7b1c147-442d-4852-b81d-665875dffa47">
  <data key="d3">The $50,000 annual premium limit establishes a funding ceiling unrelated to the product’s downside protection mechanisms. Market decline protections remain active irrespective of contribution size.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd">
  <data key="d3">The $50,000 annual premium limit sets a boundary on contributions, which indirectly influences exposure to market risks like those outlined in the zero-interest scenario, though it does not directly affect the crediting formula itself.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e">
  <data key="d3">The $50,000 annual premium cap influences the total amount exposed to surrender charges over time, especially if the policy is surrendered early despite large contributions.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018">
  <data key="d3">The $50,000 annual premium cap defines the maximum amount that could contribute to the basis for calculating the 10% surrender charge in Year 1, establishing a financial ceiling relevant to early withdrawal penalties.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890">
  <data key="d3">The $50,000 annual premium cap defines the maximum contribution possible, which directly impacts the account value used to calculate the 9% surrender charge in Year 2.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332">
  <data key="d3">The $50,000 annual premium cap defines the maximum contribution that could trigger surrender charges like the 7% fee in Year 4, influencing overall policy cost exposure.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b">
  <data key="d3">The $50,000 annual premium cap defines the maximum contribution that could trigger surrender charges like the 8% fee in Year 3, making it financially relevant to early withdrawal costs.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELEVANCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633">
  <data key="d3">The $50,000 annual premium cap sets a boundary for contributions that affect cumulative premiums used in calculating surrender charges like the one in Year 5.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="84b84dec-45b7-4ca8-ae2f-a68466866f24">
  <data key="d3">The $50,000 annual premium cap sets the maximum possible contribution that could incur surrender charges in later years, such as Year 6 when the charge is 5%, making it relevant to calculating financial exposure upon early withdrawal.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca">
  <data key="d3">The $50,000 annual premium cap defines the maximum amount one may contribute per year, influencing overall account growth and potential surrender value, though it has no direct impact on the 4% surrender charge applied in Year 7.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75">
  <data key="d3">The $50,000 annual premium cap defines the maximum investment level that could influence future surrender values, potentially affecting the magnitude of the 3% surrender charge in Year 8.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00">
  <data key="d3">The $50,000 annual premium cap defines the maximum allowable investment into the policy, influencing total accumulated funds over time. This level of funding indirectly affects the magnitude of surrender charges in later years like Year 9, though the charge itself is based solely on prior contributions and tenure rather than the cap's presence.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">The $50,000 annual premium cap affects the total investment into the policy, influencing the account value upon which the Year 10 surrender charge is based. Higher contributions may lead to greater surrender charges before full reduction.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_AFFECTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">The $50,000 annual premium cap defines the maximum funding level possible under the policy, influencing total accumulated funds subject to surrender charges like the one in Year 11. This structural ceiling indirectly affects the magnitude of potential surrender charges over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">The maximum annual premium of $50,000 defines the cap used in calculating surrender charges applied over the first ten years, making it foundational to understanding potential exit penalties.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">The $50,000 annual premium cap affects the growth of the account value, which is a key factor in determining the cash surrender value described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">The $50,000 annual premium cap allows significant funding potential, enhancing the account value over time so that the absence of surrender charges from Year 12 onward becomes increasingly valuable for policyholders seeking liquidity without penalty.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="701024d0-1ae4-4ee8-8c41-8d052bef05e9" target="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">defines_maximum_annual_premium_limit</data>
</edge>
