  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d35c1ce-d96d-4562-80f8-0654abe126d2" target="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7">
  <data key="d3">The $50,000 annual premium cap meets IRS requirements for qualified policies, helping maintain favorable tax treatment. Such limits contribute to structural integrity, possibly reinforcing features like guaranteed minimum returns during market losses.</data>
  <data key="d4">REGULATORY BASIS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d35c1ce-d96d-4562-80f8-0654abe126d2" target="70667dae-ff8c-4bac-bf04-03807ddb6bd7">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence explains that the maximum annual premium allowed ($50,000) complies with IRS tax rules. This financial ceiling has no bearing on whether losses occur during market declines, which is addressed separately in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
