  <data key="d3">The $50,000 annual premium cap ensures alignment with IRS tax-deferred savings limits, maintaining policy eligibility. This structural constraint does not directly influence how the monthly COI charge is calculated, which instead relies on the disparity between the death benefit and current account value.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
