<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db">
  <data key="d3">A recommended annual premium of $6,000 helps secure continuous coverage until age 100, thereby supporting the ongoing viability of built-in features such as floor protection, which guards against down markets.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299">
  <data key="d3">A recommended $6,000 annual premium aims to ensure continuous coverage until age 100. This consistent funding contributes to maintaining the policy's integrity, allowing features like 0% floor protection to remain effective throughout its duration.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7">
  <data key="d3">Maintaining coverage through consistent $6,000 annual premiums helps preserve the account balance, making it more likely that the 5% market decline safeguard remains effective throughout the policy term.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="70667dae-ff8c-4bac-bf04-03807ddb6bd7">
  <data key="d3">Maintaining coverage through age 100 requires consistent contributions such as the recommended $6,000 annual premium; this steady funding helps preserve the account balance, ensuring the principal remains protected even amid market volatility.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1">
  <data key="d3">Contributing $6,000 per year is advised specifically to counteract scenarios like earning 0% interest, thereby preserving the policy's longevity during periods of minimal growth.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES RESILIENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="50dee1d7-a696-448d-92e6-11dfe14d068f">
  <data key="d3">Recommending an annual premium of $6,000 provides guidance on how much should be contributed within the window of opportunity allowed by the flexible payment schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">GUIDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="86b72d75-5a59-44c2-b2d6-912ce393cf76">
  <data key="d3">A recommended annual premium of $6,000 implies a need for regular contributions, which is feasible due to the absence of restrictions on when payments may be made.</data>
  <data key="d4">NECESSITATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176">
  <data key="d3">The suggestion to pay $6,000 annually implies a level well above the $100 minimum required, highlighting a strategic financial commitment necessary to meet long-term objectives like coverage until age 100.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCEEDS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa">
  <data key="d3">While the $6,000 recommended premium supports lifelong coverage, it operates above the $100 minimum threshold, meaning that meeting the minimum does not guarantee long-term sustainability under the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCEEDS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2">
  <data key="d3">The suggested $6,000 annual contribution is feasible because it falls well below the $50,000 yearly maximum permitted premium.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUBSET_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="0d35c1ce-d96d-4562-80f8-0654abe126d2">
  <data key="d3">A recommended annual premium of $6,000 supports lifelong coverage and reflects prudent planning within the product’s design. This figure remains well below the $50,000 tax-qualified maximum, ensuring alignment with regulatory standards without exceeding allowable contributions.</data>
  <data key="d4">WITHIN_LIMITS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6">
  <data key="d3">The suggested $6,000 annual premium depends on stable actuarial and financial conditions assumed at the time of recommendation.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae">
  <data key="d3">The recommendation of a $6,000 annual premium provides a benchmark that helps determine whether skipped payments remain sustainable, given that the account value must cover ongoing fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d3">The recommended $6,000 annual premium contributes to building sufficient account value, enabling the policyholder to skip future payments without lapsing coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 recommends a specific premium amount needed to ensure lifelong coverage, while fact sentence 2 explains that a portion of each payment is retained as a load, reducing the effective contribution to the policy's value.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a">
  <data key="d3">The recommended $6,000 annual premium ensures sustained coverage through age 100, partly because a portion of it—the 3.5% load—is designated to offset administrative and operational costs.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">The recommended annual premium ensures sustained coverage through consistent funding, enabling the policy's longevity despite periodic deductions like the Cost of Insurance (COI).</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="6bfb8452-bcec-4db6-b212-fd25bdcfbc79">
  <data key="d3">The recommended annual premium supports sustained policy coverage, indirectly influencing how much remains after recurring fees like the $12 monthly administrative charge.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="0b7e0a06-5166-489d-a873-3b798f915e2c">
  <data key="d3">The recommended $6,000 annual premium supports sustained coverage, accounting for regular monthly charges like COI and administrative fees that reduce the account balance over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="749f8b25-e9c6-4e2e-a60a-5fdcef1215c4">
  <data key="d3">The recommendation for a $6,000 annual premium supports sustained policy funding, indirectly influencing the account value used in the COI calculation. However, it does not directly determine or affect the COI formula itself.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY AFFECTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="9639c325-d6a7-4181-a801-0a4fdfaefa94">
  <data key="d3">The recommended $6,000 annual premium supports maintaining adequate account value, which directly influences the size of the monthly cost-of-insurance deduction that depends on the difference between the death benefit and account value.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="1b6d4d68-07ed-4c80-987c-ddf958d36f08">
  <data key="d3">The recommended annual premium supports sustained coverage, ensuring sufficient funds remain after monthly charges are applied to the account value.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="e2637b0a-dd20-4e01-8fa1-8779d2f346fa">
  <data key="d3">The recommended $6,000 annual premium depends on the stability of ongoing costs; knowing that COI rates won't rise ensures affordability over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e">
  <data key="d3">Maintaining the recommended $6,000 annual premium supports continuous coverage, reducing the risk of policy lapse and thereby minimizing potential exposure to surrender charges if the policy is terminated early.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890">
  <data key="d3">Maintaining the recommended $6,000 annual premium helps avoid lapses and reduces exposure to high surrender charges like the 9% assessed in Year 2.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b">
  <data key="d3">Maintaining the recommended $6,000 annual premium helps avoid lapses and reduces exposure to high surrender charges like the 8% assessed in Year 3, ensuring better long-term policy viability.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018">
  <data key="d3">Maintaining the recommended $6,000 annual premium supports sustained policy viability, helping avoid premature termination and thus minimizing potential impact from the Year 1 10% surrender charge if cancellation occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332">
  <data key="d3">Maintaining the recommended $6,000 annual premium ensures continued coverage through age 100, reducing risk of lapsing during periods when high surrender charges—like the 7% in Year 4—are still applicable.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75">
  <data key="d3">Maintaining the recommended $6,000 annual premium ensures sufficient account growth, reducing the impact of the 3% surrender charge in Year 8 should the policyholder consider termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633">
  <data key="d3">Maintaining the recommended $6,000 annual premium helps avoid policy lapse, thereby preserving eligibility for potential future surrender charges like the 6% fee in Year 5. Without sufficient contributions, the policy might lapse earlier, negating such charges altogether.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca">
  <data key="d3">Maintaining the recommended $6,000 annual premium helps ensure continuous coverage and reduces the risk of triggering surrender charges like the 4% fee in Year 7 due to lapses or withdrawals.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="84b84dec-45b7-4ca8-ae2f-a68466866f24">
  <data key="d3">Maintaining the recommended $6,000 annual premium helps ensure continued coverage into later years, reducing risk of lapsing before Year 6 when surrender charges still apply. This supports sustained policy viability despite existing surrender fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIES_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00">
  <data key="d3">Maintaining the recommended $6,000 annual premium helps preserve policy value, reducing risk of significant losses when surrender charges like the 2% in Year 9 are applied.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">Maintaining the recommended $6,000 annual premium increases the likelihood of avoiding policy lapse and reduces risk of paying higher surrender fees, such as the 1% charge in Year 10.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">Maintaining the recommended $6,000 annual premium ensures continued coverage into later policy years, where surrender charges have significantly decreased, such as the 0.5% rate in Year 11.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">The recommendation to pay $6,000 annually aligns well with the absence of surrender charges after Year 12, enabling policyholders to commit to sustained contributions without fear of penalties upon withdrawal.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">The recommended $6,000 annual premium ensures continued coverage up to age 100, reducing risk of policy lapse; however, withdrawing funds early may trigger surrender charges based on premiums paid in the initial ten years.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.78</data>
</edge>
