<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db">
  <data key="d3">The ability to skip premium payments relies on having enough account value after deducting monthly charges. Maintaining adequate value is supported by floor protection, which safeguards gains during downturns.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299">
  <data key="d3">If the account value is high enough to absorb ongoing monthly charges, policyholders can pause premium contributions. This financial buffer helps preserve the policy's integrity, especially when combined with built-in floor protections like the 0% guarantee.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7">
  <data key="d3">If the account value remains high enough to absorb monthly deductions—including cost-of-insurance and admin fees—it increases the likelihood that the policyholder can avoid paying premiums, thereby benefiting from the built-in 5% market decline protection.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES SAFETY NET</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="70667dae-ff8c-4bac-bf04-03807ddb6bd7">
  <data key="d3">The ability to skip premium payments relies on having enough account value to absorb monthly charges; this feasibility is supported by the policy’s protection against market-driven losses, preserving the account balance over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1">
  <data key="d3">The ability to skip premium payments depends on having sufficient account value to offset monthly charges; without positive growth or contributions, maintaining such reserves becomes harder when interest earnings are zero.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS ON ACCOUNT VALUE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.78</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="50dee1d7-a696-448d-92e6-11dfe14d068f">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder skips a premium payment, it implies they rely on accumulated account value; thus, the option to delay payments depends on having previously contributed via flexible premium schedules.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="86b72d75-5a59-44c2-b2d6-912ce393cf76">
  <data key="d3">Flexible payment timing permits skipped payments only when the account has enough value to withstand deductions, reinforcing the practical application of payment freedom.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder has maintained enough account value through prior payments meeting the $100 minimum, they may choose to skip current premiums without immediate risk of lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa">
  <data key="d3">Even though premiums can be skipped when the account has enough value to absorb fees, maintaining at least the minimum $100 payment helps preserve long-term sustainability and avoids depletion risks.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_SUSTAINABILITY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2">
  <data key="d3">If the account value remains high due to consistent or large contributions up to the $50,000 annual limit, policyholders gain the option to skip payments without lapsing coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="0d35c1ce-d96d-4562-80f8-0654abe126d2">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder skips a premium payment, the account value must cover ongoing costs like cost-of-insurance and fees; this condition relies on having accumulated enough funds, possibly influenced by prior contributions up to the $50,000 annual cap allowed under tax regulations.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">If the account value suffices to cover monthly charges without additional premiums, then maintaining the recommended $6,000 annual contribution becomes optional, though still advisable for longevity.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6">
  <data key="d3">If the account value remains sufficient to absorb monthly charges despite missed payments, the underlying actuarial and financial assumptions supporting the recommendation are validated or at least plausible.</data>
  <data key="d4">VALIDATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d3">Skipping premium payments depends on having enough account value to cover ongoing monthly fees. This ensures financial sustainability without active contributions.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITION REQUIRED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">The ability to skip payments relies on having enough account value, which could be impacted by the 3.5% load that reduces the effective growth per payment. However, the load itself does not determine eligibility for skipping payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">If the account value is sufficient to cover monthly deductions—including Cost of Insurance—the policyholder may skip paying premiums. This ensures continued coverage despite non-payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_DEPENDENCY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a">
  <data key="d3">If the account value is high enough to absorb monthly charges like the administrative fee, policyholders can forego paying premiums. This financial buffer relies on proper allocation of funds, such as those affected by the 3.5% load.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="0b7e0a06-5166-489d-a873-3b798f915e2c">
  <data key="d3">If the account value is high enough to cover total monthly charges—including COI and administrative fees—the policyholder may skip premium payments without lapsing coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="6bfb8452-bcec-4db6-b212-fd25bdcfbc79">
  <data key="d3">If the account value is insufficient to cover the $12 monthly administrative charge, skipping premium payments would not be sustainable. This charge is part of the financial burden that must be managed within the account balance.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="1b6d4d68-07ed-4c80-987c-ddf958d36f08">
  <data key="d3">If the account value is sufficient to cover total charges, policyholders can skip paying premiums. These charges are consistently deducted on the third day of every month, ensuring predictable financial obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="e2637b0a-dd20-4e01-8fa1-8779d2f346fa">
  <data key="d3">The ability to skip premiums relies on adequate account value, which remains viable due to guaranteed stable COI rates that prevent unexpected increases in fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="749f8b25-e9c6-4e2e-a60a-5fdcef1215c4">
  <data key="d3">If the account value is high enough to absorb monthly deductions like COI, policyholders can skip paying premiums. The COI amount itself is calculated using a precise formula involving the death benefit and current account value.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="9639c325-d6a7-4181-a801-0a4fdfaefa94">
  <data key="d3">If the account value is high enough to cover monthly fees, policyholders can skip paying premiums. This same account value level determines the magnitude of the cost-of-insurance deduction, since it's calculated relative to the death benefit shortfall.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3a04b397-cd4d-461a-8e10-baf1f9c1d92f" target="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">affects account value</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dc4e868-72f3-4a82-bcc4-2dc4618b20a4" target="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">reduces account value</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a10ab3ab-e6c6-4850-9d07-f3102d640055" target="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">monthly deduction</data>
</edge>
<edge source="331d3e03-d7ec-4dd9-890b-c2d852d57015" target="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">account value</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e6598607-fadd-4c12-905f-0aad288a8f3d" target="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">covered_by_account_value_when_premiums_skipped</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c63da4c9-eaae-4c1f-9ee4-7bd7dd903385" target="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">covered_by_account_value_when_premiums_skipped</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="08297671-4782-4819-a6a9-1473ccbb5f05">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="95ebe390-f4a9-4a87-a597-928d18a03d7d">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="7650a77f-2cf2-4bc7-bad1-dbbd19c55151">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="b78c5928-fb64-4a29-96b6-ae8774ad142a">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">AMOUNT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="48c760de-2670-464d-8364-5750775aa35b">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">AMOUNT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="742e18dd-2ff0-4be4-8a4c-861a509e4cd2">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">AMOUNT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="7c80a6eb-0783-4a8e-b0c9-5e355e97aaf6">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERCENTAGE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="9d9a7295-ad46-45bc-a6f2-5aa148930295">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CHARGE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="18d960e9-4b64-4111-b7e5-f2a041c0d03c">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CHARGE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="0226db91-f1c9-4cd1-9aec-54aa60220d1e">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CHARGE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="d673b95e-c66c-4b70-b7c6-3888237440a1">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DATE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db">
  <data key="d3">Sufficient account value is necessary to absorb monthly charges, making it possible to rely on floor protection when markets fall without risking lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299">
  <data key="d3">To maintain flexibility in paying premiums, the account value must stay above the threshold needed to cover monthly deductions, which relies on having effective floor protection preventing negative balances.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7">
  <data key="d3">Sufficient account value is crucial to withstand monthly deductions; this financial cushion allows the policyholder to skip premium payments safely, especially important given the 5% downside protection feature.</data>
  <data key="d4">NECESSITATED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="70667dae-ff8c-4bac-bf04-03807ddb6bd7">
  <data key="d3">Sufficient account value to cover monthly deductions relies on preserved principal due to market protections, ensuring long-term sustainability of the policy’s funding.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1">
  <data key="d3">To avoid paying premiums, the account value must remain high enough to absorb monthly deductions; however, earning 0% interest reduces the ability to build such reserves over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">NECESSITATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="50dee1d7-a696-448d-92e6-11dfe14d068f">
  <data key="d3">Sufficient account value enables the option to skip premium payments, supporting the claim that payments can be made at any time due to built-in financial safeguards.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="86b72d75-5a59-44c2-b2d6-912ce393cf76">
  <data key="d3">To legally or practically skip premium payments, the account value must remain high enough to cover mandatory monthly deductions, which reinforces why payment timing cannot be arbitrary unless supported by adequate reserves.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176">
  <data key="d3">Sufficient account value to cover monthly deductions allows flexibility to skip premium payments; however, such flexibility requires prior contributions meeting the $100 minimum to maintain balance.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa">
  <data key="d3">To legally or contractually skip premium payments, the account value must remain high enough to cover ongoing costs, which implies any such skipped payment still needs to respect the minimum requirement of $100 when made.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2">
  <data key="d3">Maintaining adequate account value to cover monthly fees allows policyholders to potentially skip premium payments, making the $50,000 annual ceiling more meaningful for long-term sustainability.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="0d35c1ce-d96d-4562-80f8-0654abe126d2">
  <data key="d3">To skip premium payments without causing lapse, the account value must remain high enough to absorb ongoing costs like COI and admin fees. This requirement operates independently of the $50,000 tax-based ceiling.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">Maintaining enough account value allows for skipped premium payments, making it feasible to meet the long-term goal of sustaining coverage through the recommended $6,000 annual contribution.</data>
  <data key="d4">NECESSITATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6">
  <data key="d3">To maintain eligibility for skipping premium payments, the account value must remain high enough to cover recurring costs, which only holds under the assumption that underlying actuarial and financial models remain valid.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae">
  <data key="d3">Sufficient account value is necessary to permit skipping premium payments, ensuring continued policy validity despite non-payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">The need to maintain adequate account value to avoid triggering penalties when skipping payments depends on how much of each premium actually contributes to the account, which is reduced by the 3.5% load.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to maintain sufficient account value hinges on ongoing monthly deductions like the Cost of Insurance, which reduces the balance over time and affects the ability to skip future premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_DEPENDENCY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a">
  <data key="d3">A sufficient account value ensures that monthly fees—including those tied to the premium load—are covered, enabling flexibility in premium payments without lapsing coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="6bfb8452-bcec-4db6-b212-fd25bdcfbc79">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that account value covers monthly deductions relies on knowing what those deductions entail; one such deduction is the fixed $12 administrative charge.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="0b7e0a06-5166-489d-a873-3b798f915e2c">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that account value covers monthly deductions relies on knowing exactly what those deductions entail; total monthly charges being composed of COI and admin fees explains why maintaining adequate balance matters.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="749f8b25-e9c6-4e2e-a60a-5fdcef1215c4">
  <data key="d3">If the account value is insufficient due to high COI charges calculated using the given formula, it may prevent the ability to skip premium payments without depleting reserves.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="9639c325-d6a7-4181-a801-0a4fdfaefa94">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to maintain enough account value to skip premium payments depends on the magnitude of the monthly COI deduction, which itself increases with larger gaps between the death benefit and account value.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="1b6d4d68-07ed-4c80-987c-ddf958d36f08">
  <data key="d3">If the account value isn't sufficient to cover total charges, skipping premiums could lead to policy lapse; since these charges are deducted on the third day of each month, ongoing monitoring of the account value relative to this schedule is essential.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="e2637b0a-dd20-4e01-8fa1-8779d2f346fa">
  <data key="d3">The necessity to maintain enough account value to avoid lapses hinges on predictable expenses; since COI rates are capped, they ensure long-term sustainability of the account balance needed to skip payments without triggering termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647">
  <data key="d3">Adequate account balance ensures long-term policy viability, making it possible to qualify for policy loans after one year of activity.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">A sufficiently high account value ensures eligibility for policy loans up to 90% of surrender value, linking financial stability for premium flexibility with access to liquidity.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">A high policy loan interest rate may reduce account value over time, potentially undermining the sufficiency required to skip premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_AFFECTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.55</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">Adequate account value ensures continued coverage despite skipped premiums, which is impacted by outstanding loans that draw from the account. Since loaned amounts still earn 3%, they help preserve some value, reducing risk of lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d">
  <data key="d3">Frequent or large partial withdrawals, especially within the first ten free ones, risk depleting the account value needed to cover ongoing monthly deductions, potentially undermining the ability to skip future premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9">
  <data key="d3">A sufficiently funded account ensures continued coverage despite skipped premiums, which indirectly enables meaningful partial withdrawals like the $500 minimum allowed.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">Adequate account value ensures premium skips remain viable, and the low net cost of policy loans helps preserve that value over time by minimizing erosion due to borrowing.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPRTS_SUSTAINABILITY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">If policyholder loans accumulate, they reduce the account value needed to avoid premium payments, making it harder to meet the threshold required to skip premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5">
  <data key="d3">If frequent partial withdrawals occur beyond the allowed number, accumulated fees and reduced account balance may compromise the fund’s ability to support required monthly deductions, risking policy lapse despite intent to skip premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="08297671-4782-4819-a6a9-1473ccbb5f05" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">protects against</data>
</edge>
<edge source="95ebe390-f4a9-4a87-a597-928d18a03d7d" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">increases account value</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7650a77f-2cf2-4bc7-bad1-dbbd19c55151" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">reduces account value</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b78c5928-fb64-4a29-96b6-ae8774ad142a" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">represents monthly deduction amount</data>
</edge>
<edge source="48c760de-2670-464d-8364-5750775aa35b" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">minimum required account value</data>
</edge>
<edge source="18d960e9-4b64-4111-b7e5-f2a041c0d03c" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">affects eligibility for</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0226db91-f1c9-4cd1-9aec-54aa60220d1e" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">affects eligibility for</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d673b95e-c66c-4b70-b7c6-3888237440a1" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has_condition_for_skipping_premiums_based_on_account_value</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="393dca0e-22d0-43f1-b00c-8e63a7e8f57e">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="33082ee6-2488-4303-9312-d5ca065050f2">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="43e079f8-bd5e-4e81-ac7f-76cf6d6117ae">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="e5a57ea1-57cc-4798-ad39-f4958d3b0156">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">AMOUNT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="b35bf046-d0c4-4809-8d8a-ea63bce693ac">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">AMOUNT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="2b6c6d48-3e26-4f83-bb3b-82794efaa2aa">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">AMOUNT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="621286da-2504-4f73-9a6f-3bf829245f83">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERCENTAGE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="a4d5e668-4c9a-470a-be26-7d692372ccd9">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CHARGE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="0f8d859f-a7b7-4e92-971f-a7d5e30e44a4">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CHARGE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="1208334e-58a6-4a6f-a971-766a201e482b">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CHARGE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="ec38e075-4226-41a5-adf4-821d29c142e7">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DATE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db">
  <data key="d3">Each premium payment incurs a 3.5% load, reducing the net amount added to the account. This fee does not affect the floor protection mechanism, which remains active irrespective of payment amounts or loads.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299">
  <data key="d3">Each premium payment incurs a 3.5% load, reducing the effective contribution to the account. This charge has no impact on the floor protection mechanism, which remains fixed at 0% regardless of loading.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7">
  <data key="d3">Each premium payment incurs a 3.5% load before being invested, meaning less money enters the account than contributed. This reduction affects long-term accumulation, though it does not impact the 0% interest rule when the index falls sharply.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="70667dae-ff8c-4bac-bf04-03807ddb6bd7">
  <data key="d3">Each premium payment incurs a 3.5% load, reducing the amount credited to the account. Despite this reduction, the policy still protects the remaining balance from losses caused by market downturns, preserving the adjusted principal.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1">
  <data key="d3">A 3.5% load on each premium payment reduces the effective growth of the account value, making it more likely that the policyholder experiences a 0% return in the worst case.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRIBUTES_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="50dee1d7-a696-448d-92e6-11dfe14d068f">
  <data key="d3">Each premium payment incurs a 3.5% load, which applies irrespective of when payments occur, reinforcing the flexibility described in the earlier statement about payment timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">APPLIES_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="86b72d75-5a59-44c2-b2d6-912ce393cf76">
  <data key="d3">Each premium payment incurs a 3.5% load, irrespective of when it is made, consistent with the lack of constraints on payment timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% load is contingent upon making a premium payment; therefore, its applicability assumes the payment exceeds or equals the $100 minimum established in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa">
  <data key="d3">A 3.5% load is applied uniformly to any premium payment, meaning it affects the effective value of the $100 minimum contribution, reducing the portion that actually goes toward coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">APPLIES_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% load applies uniformly to any premium payment up to the $50,000 annual limit, making the cap essential for determining the scope of the charge.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="0d35c1ce-d96d-4562-80f8-0654abe126d2">
  <data key="d3">Each premium payment incurs a 3.5% load regardless of amount, meaning higher contributions like the $50,000 maximum still face proportional fees. The load has no bearing on whether the cap meets tax requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% load on premiums impacts the net amount available for maintaining coverage; therefore, the recommended $6,000 annual premium accounts for this deduction to still achieve sustained benefits through age 100.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load reduces the effective amount contributed toward maintaining coverage, potentially impacting the validity of long-term projections underpinning the initial recommendation.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% load affects the net increase in account value when a premium is paid, influencing whether the account remains sufficiently funded to allow future skipped payments without lapsing coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load diminishes the net increase in account value, making it more challenging to meet the threshold required to support skipped premium payments due to ongoing monthly deductions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load on each payment is implemented to offset administrative and operational expenses associated with managing the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load is applied at the time of each payment, contributing to the total cost burden that also includes the monthly Cost of Insurance deduction.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="749f8b25-e9c6-4e2e-a60a-5fdcef1215c4">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load reduces the amount credited to the account value, indirectly influencing the variables used in the COI calculation. However, the COI formula itself does not depend directly on the load.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="6bfb8452-bcec-4db6-b212-fd25bdcfbc79">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 describes a 3.5% load applied to each premium payment, increasing the effective cost of contributions. This does not influence or depend on the fixed $12 monthly administrative charge mentioned in fact sentence 2.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="1b6d4d68-07ed-4c80-987c-ddf958d36f08">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load is a component of the total monthly deductions made from the account value, contributing directly to the overall fees charged each month.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRIBUTES_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="e2637b0a-dd20-4e01-8fa1-8779d2f346fa">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load impacts how much of each payment contributes to the account value, independent of future COI rate changes. The guarantee on COI rates ensures predictable ongoing expenses regardless of the initial load.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="9639c325-d6a7-4181-a801-0a4fdfaefa94">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load reduces the net amount credited to the account value, which in turn influences the calculation of the monthly cost-of-insurance (COI) deduction, since COI depends on the difference between the death benefit and the account value.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="0b7e0a06-5166-489d-a873-3b798f915e2c">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load affects how much of each payment contributes to the account value, indirectly influencing the funds available to cover ongoing monthly charges like COI and admin fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load reduces the net amount allocated to the account, potentially increasing the relative burden of surrender charges when exiting early. Together, these fees affect overall policy value retention.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load reduces the initial capital allocated to the account, indirectly increasing the relative burden of the 10% surrender charge if a withdrawal occurs early, since less money is invested upfront.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load reduces the account value incrementally with each payment, indirectly affecting the cash surrender value upon withdrawal, which may be further reduced by the 8% surrender charge in Year 3.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_COSTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load impacts the initial investment growth, indirectly affecting the account value used to calculate the 9% surrender charge in Year 2. Higher loads reduce accumulation, potentially lowering the cash surrender value subject to the charge.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_AFFECTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load reduces the net amount allocated to the account, indirectly affecting the account value that could be subject to the 7% surrender charge in Year 4.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load impacts the total funds allocated to the account, indirectly affecting the account value that determines the surrender charge in Year 5.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="84b84dec-45b7-4ca8-ae2f-a68466866f24">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load increases the total contributions made, which indirectly raises the basis for calculating surrender charges like the 5% fee in Year 6.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load impacts the total funds allocated to the account, indirectly influencing the cash surrender value upon withdrawal, which is subject to a 3% surrender charge in Year 8.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load impacts the account value over time, indirectly affecting the cash surrender value upon which the Year 7 surrender charge is based. Higher loads reduce accumulated value, potentially increasing effective surrender costs relative to benefits received.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES_COST</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load reduces the initial investment growth potential, indirectly affecting the account value upon which the Year 9 surrender charge is calculated. This means higher loads may lead to lower net accumulation before withdrawal or surrender.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES_COST</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% loading on premiums reduces the initial investment growth, potentially increasing the impact of future surrender charges like the 1% charge in Year 10 when withdrawing funds early.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_COSTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% load reduces the initial account value, indirectly affecting the base upon which surrender charges are calculated. Higher loads may increase total premiums paid, thereby increasing potential surrender charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load reduces the net amount credited to the account, indirectly increasing the impact of later surrender charges like the 0.5% in Year 11. Both affect the policyholder’s return on investment over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY_COSTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load reduces the portion of each payment that contributes to the account value, thereby indirectly lowering the potential cash surrender value over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_AFFECTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load impacts the initial investment growth, indirectly affecting the account value used to calculate surrender charges. Since surrender charges end at Year 12, maintaining consistent payments ensures higher accumulated value without penalty.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load increases the cost of maintaining the policy, potentially affecting long-term affordability, which could influence decisions about accessing policy loans after one year.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load increases the effective cost of contributing funds, potentially influencing decisions about taking policy loans, though it does not affect the 4% loan interest rate itself.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load reduces the effective amount credited to the account, potentially affecting the pool of funds that could be used for loans or investment gains. However, once a loan is taken, its earnings at 3% occur separately from premium loads.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load reduces the portion of each payment that contributes to the account value, indirectly affecting the surrender value used to determine the maximum loan amount. This creates a subtle indirect link where higher loads may lower future surrender values and thus limit loan availability.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_AFFECTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load increases upfront costs of maintaining the policy, indirectly affecting the funds available for future loans or investments. The 1% net borrowing cost represents the actual expense of accessing cash value later, separate from initial premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load increases the amount invested into the policy, potentially enabling larger future loan balances, which in turn reduce the death benefit when outstanding.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_AFFECTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load affects the total amount contributed toward the policy, which may impact the pool of funds available for future partial withdrawals, such as the minimum $500 allowed. However, the load itself does not determine or alter the withdrawal threshold.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load affects ongoing costs of maintaining the policy, whereas the fee-free partial withdrawals offer flexibility in accessing funds early without penalty. These features operate independently—one impacts contributions, the other access to accumulated value.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d" target="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load impacts overall funding efficiency, indirectly influencing how much money remains in the account before any withdrawals occur. However, it has no direct effect on the $50 fee charged per partial withdrawal after the tenth year.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
