<edge source="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a" target="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load funds essential operations and administration, enabling the insurer to maintain features like floor protection despite market volatility.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a" target="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299">
  <data key="d3">Premium loads fund administrative and operational expenses, ensuring the insurer’s ability to manage policies efficiently. This charge has no bearing on the floor protection mechanism designed to safeguard account value.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a" target="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load offsets administrative and operational costs. By covering these expenses, it supports the infrastructure necessary to enforce protections like the 5% floor on index losses.</data>
  <data key="d4">FUNDING_SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a" target="70667dae-ff8c-4bac-bf04-03807ddb6bd7">
  <data key="d3">Premium loads fund administrative and operational expenses, contributing to policy maintenance. This financial mechanism functions independently of whether the underlying index rises or falls, preserving principal under adverse conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a" target="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1">
  <data key="d3">The premium load covers operational expenses such as administration, which does not affect the calculation or likelihood of achieving zero interest earnings.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a" target="50dee1d7-a696-448d-92e6-11dfe14d068f">
  <data key="d3">The use of the premium load for administrative expenses does not constrain or enable the timing of premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a" target="86b72d75-5a59-44c2-b2d6-912ce393cf76">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% load on each premium payment serves to offset administrative and operational expenses, regardless of when the payment occurs. Thus, the charge remains consistent irrespective of the timing chosen by the policyholder.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a" target="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% load exists to offset administrative and operational expenses, making it necessary that premiums meet or exceed the $100 floor to maintain sustainable fund allocation.</data>
  <data key="d4">JUSTIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a" target="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% load on premiums serves to offset administrative and operational expenses; therefore, setting a minimum payment at $100 protects the sustainability of this funding model.</data>
  <data key="d4">JUSTIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a" target="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% load on each premium payment serves to offset administrative and operational expenses, ensuring consistent funding mechanisms even when payments reach the maximum allowable level of $50,000 per year.</data>
  <data key="d4">APPLIES_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a" target="0d35c1ce-d96d-4562-80f8-0654abe126d2">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% load covers administrative and operational costs associated with managing the policy. Since such fees are applied per premium dollar up to $50,000, the cap ensures that expense allocation remains consistent with tax-qualified design standards.</data>
  <data key="d4">JUSTIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load covers administrative and operational expenses, making larger premiums like the recommended $6,000 necessary to maintain coverage without depleting the account value.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a" target="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6">
  <data key="d3">A 3.5% premium load is implemented to offset administrative and operational costs associated with managing the policy. The existence of such a charge implies that ongoing financial planning requires adherence to certain economic assumptions, like those cited in the recommendation.</data>
  <data key="d4">JUSTIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a" target="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% load on each premium helps offset administrative and operational costs, ensuring the system remains viable—even when some policyholders choose not to pay premiums due to adequate account balances.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d3">The 3.5% premium load funds administrative and operational costs, influencing how much of each payment remains in the account to support future deductions and potential premium skips.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">Administrative and operational costs are covered through a 3.5% charge applied to every premium payment made into the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">The premium load covers general administrative and operational costs, whereas the Cost of Insurance is a separate monthly charge based on risk factors. These are independent financial components of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a" target="6bfb8452-bcec-4db6-b212-fd25bdcfbc79">
  <data key="d3">The premium load funds administrative costs, such as the $12 monthly administrative charge mentioned in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">COVERS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.9</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a" target="9639c325-d6a7-4181-a801-0a4fdfaefa94">
  <data key="d3">The premium load covers general administrative and operational costs, whereas the monthly COI charge varies depending on the disparity between the death benefit and account value. These are distinct components of policy expenses.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a" target="749f8b25-e9c6-4e2e-a60a-5fdcef1215c4">
  <data key="d3">The premium load covers general administrative and operational costs, whereas the cost-of-insurance charge is computed based on the death benefit minus the account value using a rate per thousand. These represent distinct types of fees within the policy’s funding mechanism.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a" target="1b6d4d68-07ed-4c80-987c-ddf958d36f08">
  <data key="d3">The premium load covers administrative and operational costs, which are part of the total charges deducted monthly. These deductions occur on the third day of every month, reflecting how the load contributes to ongoing fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a" target="0b7e0a06-5166-489d-a873-3b798f915e2c">
  <data key="d3">The premium load is applied to offset administrative costs, which directly includes the administrative fee subtracted monthly from the account value.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a" target="e2637b0a-dd20-4e01-8fa1-8779d2f346fa">
  <data key="d3">The premium load covers administrative and operational costs, whereas COI rates are locked at predetermined levels. These are separate financial mechanisms with distinct purposes.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
