  <data key="d3">The cost-of-insurance charge, calculated based on the gap between the death benefit and account value, reflects ongoing costs tied to maintaining coverage, independent of market performance protections.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="749f8b25-e9c6-4e2e-a60a-5fdcef1215c4" target="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1">
  <data key="d3">The formula for computing monthly COI does not rely on whether the policy earns zero interest; instead, it uses fixed rates and account balances at specific points in time. Therefore, the existence of a 0% interest scenario has no bearing on the application of the COI formula.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
