  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="749f8b25-e9c6-4e2e-a60a-5fdcef1215c4" target="9639c325-d6a7-4181-a801-0a4fdfaefa94">
  <data key="d3">The formula for computing the monthly COI uses the difference between the death benefit and the account value as its core component, reflecting how this gap influences the charge amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">USED_IN</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="749f8b25-e9c6-4e2e-a60a-5fdcef1215c4" target="e2637b0a-dd20-4e01-8fa1-8779d2f346fa">
  <data key="d3">The formula for computing the monthly COI relies on a rate that is permanently capped at the level defined in the policy schedule, ensuring predictable calculations over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="749f8b25-e9c6-4e2e-a60a-5fdcef1215c4" target="0b7e0a06-5166-489d-a873-3b798f915e2c">
  <data key="d3">The formula in fact_sentence_1 defines how the Cost of Insurance (COI) charge is calculated, which is a key component included in the total monthly charges mentioned in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="749f8b25-e9c6-4e2e-a60a-5fdcef1215c4" target="6bfb8452-bcec-4db6-b212-fd25bdcfbc79">
  <data key="d3">The cost-of-insurance charge is calculated using a specific formula involving the death benefit and account value, whereas the administrative charge is a fixed $12 monthly fee applied regardless of those factors.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="749f8b25-e9c6-4e2e-a60a-5fdcef1215c4" target="1b6d4d68-07ed-4c80-987c-ddf958d36f08">
  <data key="d3">The cost-of-insurance (COI) charge, computed using the given formula, forms part of the total monthly deductions applied to the account value. These combined charges are systematically subtracted on the third day of every month.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRIBUTES_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
