  <data key="d3">Charges are deducted monthly on the third day, independent of the 0% floor protection mechanism, which safeguards against losses due to index performance.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1b6d4d68-07ed-4c80-987c-ddf958d36f08" target="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7">
  <data key="d3">Monthly charges are subtracted from the account balance on the third of every month, affecting how much capital remains after any potential interest credits—even those set at zero due to market decline.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1b6d4d68-07ed-4c80-987c-ddf958d36f08" target="70667dae-ff8c-4bac-bf04-03807ddb6bd7">
  <data key="d3">Monthly charges being deducted on the third day of each month impact the account balance, potentially reducing funds available to absorb losses—but since the policy already protects against such losses, the deduction timing doesn't affect the principle of capital preservation.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUALLY RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
