</edge>
<edge source="1b6d4d68-07ed-4c80-987c-ddf958d36f08" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">Monthly charges reduce the account value consistently over time, potentially impacting the accumulation needed to offset future surrender charges. However, since surrender charges vanish after Year 12, these ongoing deductions have less impact on long-term liquidity decisions beyond that point.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1b6d4d68-07ed-4c80-987c-ddf958d36f08" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">Monthly charges reduce the account value regularly, influencing long-term accumulation, while the Year 11 surrender charge represents a future withdrawal penalty tied to early termination. Both affect net account value but operate under different mechanisms and timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_AFFECTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1b6d4d68-07ed-4c80-987c-ddf958d36f08" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">The monthly deduction described in fact_sentence_1 occurs regularly regardless of surrender activity, whereas the surrender charge in fact_sentence_2 only applies if the policy is terminated early. Both affect the account value but operate under different triggers and timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
