<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="f48d18db-916a-4e9a-ad5c-8b176c59da3c">
  <data key="d3">The fixed $500,000 death benefit under Option 1 is complemented by lower ongoing charges, enhancing its cost efficiency over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678">
  <data key="d3">Option 1 offers a fixed death benefit of $500,000 regardless of account performance, whereas Option 2 dynamically increases the benefit based on the account's accumulated value alongside a guaranteed minimum.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPARATIVE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit under Option 1 is fixed at $500,000, consistent with its classification as a level benefit option, meaning it does not change over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="99ca8905-b57d-4689-9164-12678eda198b">
  <data key="d3">The fixed death benefit amount in Option 1 provides clarity on payout size but does not influence or reflect the level of ongoing charges associated with either option.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6">
  <data key="d3">Option 1 provides a constant death benefit of $500,000 regardless of policy performance, whereas Option 2 ties the death benefit to the growing account value, allowing it to increase over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRASTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76">
  <data key="d3">The fixed $500,000 death benefit under Option 1 provides a baseline value that can be altered via an annual switch to another option, such as the Increasing type.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit under Option 1 is fixed at $500,000, unrelated to the policy's cash value or surrender value used to determine loan limits.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit being fixed at $500,000 under Option 1 is unrelated to when policy loans become available after one year of policy activity.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25">
  <data key="d3">The fixed $500,000 death benefit under Option 1 sets the baseline for policyholder decisions, requiring that any future switches to other options follow formal procedures like providing 60 days’ notice.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES CHANGE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">Option 1 establishes a fixed death benefit of $500,000, independent of loan activity. The 4% loan interest rate applies separately when borrowers access funds against their policy’s cash value.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501">
  <data key="d3">The Level Death Benefit of $500,000 sets the standard payout unless modified. To increase this benefit beyond its current level, policyholders must provide evidence of insurability, linking eligibility for change to health qualification.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit under Option 1 remains fixed at $500,000 regardless of loan activity. Loaned amounts still accumulate interest at 3% annually in the fixed account, independent of the death benefit level.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9">
  <data key="d3">Fact Sentence 1 defines the fixed death benefit amount under Option 1. This figure remains unchanged regardless of withdrawals, though such actions may indirectly reduce it over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">The fixed death benefit of $500,000 under Option 1 establishes a baseline payout but does not affect the calculation of the 1% net annual cost associated with policy loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d">
  <data key="d3">The fixed death benefit of $500,000 under Option 1 does not influence the rule that allows ten free partial withdrawals. These features operate independently within the policy’s framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009">
  <data key="d3">The fixed death benefit of $500,000 sets the baseline financial commitment of Option 1, influencing the effective account value available for withdrawals. Maximum partial withdrawals are limited by the remaining account value after subtracting surrender charges, meaning the higher the account value relative to charges, the more can be withdrawn without impacting future benefits significantly.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit under Option 1 is fixed at $500,000, and any partial withdrawal reduces this amount proportionally. This creates a clear link where withdrawals directly lower the final payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit under Option 1 is fixed at $500,000, serving as the base amount before any deductions. Outstanding loans reduce this amount when a claim is made, diminishing the actual payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5">
  <data key="d3">The fixed death benefit of $500,000 sets the baseline payout under Option 1, while subsequent partial withdrawals beyond the tenth year trigger a $50 fee, contributing to reduced cash value over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="deefe5c8-640f-408f-a9d3-69fdb6670c3a">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies the death benefit amount under Option 1, providing contextual validation for fact_sentence_1’s assertion about the initial face amount being $500,000.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="db5f42b7-e216-4454-b4f0-97dfc9c2dbc6">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 states the death benefit under Option 1 is $500,000, which matches exactly with the provision described in fact_sentence_1 and supported by chunk_summary_1’s confirmation of the level benefit amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="03f1141d-d1b6-49f8-a326-19f21e643d95">
  <data key="d3">The $500,000 death benefit under Option 1 depends on consistent premium payments like the planned $6,000 annual contribution to remain active and fully funded.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="db06e7c6-2f5b-4dca-9e5a-d5dd96d2c405">
  <data key="d3">The $500,000 Level Death Benefit under Option 1 is unaffected by the Fixed Account’s 3.0% annual yield, as it is a predetermined amount; however, the fixed account’s returns do contribute to the underlying asset value that could otherwise support an increasing death benefit under different option settings.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="f64306b3-60d7-48b6-82c2-6580397642e1">
  <data key="d3">The $500,000 death benefit under Option 1 is unaffected by the 0% floor on the indexed account, as it represents a fixed guarantee regardless of underlying asset performance.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="326a19f6-3d06-4cde-a9f0-0b1923801873">
  <data key="d3">The fixed death benefit of $500,000 under Option 1 is independent of the cap applied to the Global Diversified Index Account. Changes in the index cap do not alter the death benefit amount, though lower investment returns due to the cap may affect long-term account value and thus indirectly impact future benefits under different option types.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="e56d9b1f-113b-4961-abbd-159d8047aeca">
  <data key="d3">While the Death Benefit under Option 1 is fixed at $500,000, increases in account value due to a 100% participation rate in the Global Diversified Index Account do not raise this cap, meaning higher returns don’t increase the death benefit unless switching to an increasing option.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="c4dbdf51-a4cd-4a65-8903-f269d529eefd">
  <data key="d3">The $500,000 Level Death Benefit remains constant regardless of the fixed account’s performance, so the 2% guaranteed interest rate does not alter its value. This means the guarantee in fact_sentence_1 operates independently of the death benefit level defined in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7">
  <data key="d3">While the $500,000 Death Benefit under Option 1 provides a stable payout ceiling, its actual impact depends on whether the account grows via indexed credits—which rely on a minimum 25% participation rate—but the benefit itself is not influenced by those credit levels.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1">
  <data key="d3">A fixed death benefit of $500,000 under Option 1 means its value remains unchanged regardless of indexed account performance. Therefore, even though the 4% cap supports better-than-minimal returns in those accounts, it has no effect on maintaining or altering the specified death benefit amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="9ac0c7c4-1321-469b-afaa-abe6d54dbd8e">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit detail under Option 1 is part of a broader policy offered by Horizon Wealth Protection Insurance, providing contextual credibility to the financial terms described.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="03e4f2e0-8fd5-4268-b333-707b317fcbd9">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount specified under Option 1 is a core feature of the insurance product offered by Horizon Wealth Protection Insurance, which can be contacted using the provided phone number for inquiries or support regarding such features.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="47c97675-2a23-4fd8-af2f-5cf44ebaf17b">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount specified under Option 1 is unrelated to the executive position held by the signatory on the document.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="7c78ce63-cb1f-4b61-bdcd-88d0ce4bcb53">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount specified in fact_sentence_1 is unrelated to the geographic execution point mentioned in fact_sentence_2. No causal or supportive link exists between the insurance terms and the place of signing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="dc9f1c71-4218-47d3-a2d6-f9dd0a3d8783">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit detail under Option 1 is part of a broader insurance product offered by Horizon Wealth Protection Insurance, which uses the provided website as a public-facing channel for customer engagement and information dissemination.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="ba1c52cb-9fba-4846-9a66-8e0c71e2a754">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a corporate seal on the document lends authority and legitimacy to the stated death benefit amount of $500,000 under Option 1, reinforcing trust in the accuracy of the financial detail.</data>
  <data key="d4">VERIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906" target="e9cf97a9-cf24-4d3c-adf8-586c6935d0e1">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit detail under Option 1 applies to policies offered by Horizon Wealth Protection Insurance, establishing that the financial terms belong to this insurer’s product suite.</data>
