  <data key="d3">The existence of a level death benefit under Option 1 does not influence when policy loans become available. Loan access is determined solely by the length of time since policy inception.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">Option 1 defines a constant death benefit, independent of policy performance. This feature does not influence or relate to the cap on policy loans set at 90% of surrender value.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">Option 1 establishes a stable death benefit amount, independent of investment performance. This feature does not influence the fixed 4% interest rate applied to policy loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">The level death benefit under Option 1 defines the guaranteed payout amount, independent of how borrowed funds grow over time. Loaned amounts continue to earn interest even though they reduce the final payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines the type of death benefit offered under Option 1. This information is independent of the minimum withdrawal threshold specified in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009">
  <data key="d3">Under Option 1's level death benefit framework, the maximum partial withdrawal is limited by the account value less any applicable surrender charge, ensuring that withdrawals do not exceed what remains after penalties.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">Under Option 1’s level death benefit structure, any outstanding policy loans reduce the final payout. The net annual cost of such loans being 1% reflects an ongoing expense tied to accessing cash value, thereby indirectly impacting the stability of the promised death benefit over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d">
  <data key="d3">Option 1 guarantees a constant death benefit amount over time. This stable benefit structure operates independently of the fee schedule governing partial withdrawals.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225">
  <data key="d3">The Level Death Benefit in Option 1 creates a stable foundation where any partial withdrawal results in an equivalent decrease in the payout amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5">
  <data key="d3">The level death benefit under Option 1 defines the guaranteed payout amount, while separate rules govern withdrawal fees. This second fact describes an additional cost incurred when withdrawing funds beyond the tenth year, independent of the death benefit structure.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">The level death benefit in Option 1 serves as the baseline payout, but it is reduced by any outstanding policy loans when a claim is made.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="db5f42b7-e216-4454-b4f0-97dfc9c2dbc6">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 states that Option 1 provides a level death benefit, which directly supports and clarifies the specific feature referenced in fact_sentence_1 about the selected benefit option.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONFIRMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="deefe5c8-640f-408f-a9d3-69fdb6670c3a">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 identifies Option 1 as offering a level death benefit, which explains why the initial face amount stated in fact_sentence_1 remains constant over time without adjustment.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONFIRMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="03f1141d-d1b6-49f8-a326-19f21e643d95">
  <data key="d3">The statement about Option 1 providing a level death benefit explains why the $6,000 annual premium is applicable, as this premium supports the fixed-benefit structure rather than variable or growing benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="db06e7c6-2f5b-4dca-9e5a-d5dd96d2c405">
  <data key="d3">While the Fixed Account offers a stable 3.0% yield, its impact on the total account value indirectly influences the amount available to support the Level Death Benefit. However, the death benefit remains static regardless of account growth unless modified via an option change.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_CONTRIBUTING</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="f64306b3-60d7-48b6-82c2-6580397642e1">
  <data key="d3">A Level Death Benefit reduces when partial withdrawals occur, which may counteract benefits derived from the 0% floor if account value erodes due to frequent withdrawals despite market safeguards.</data>
  <data key="d4">PARTIALLY OFFSETS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="326a19f6-3d06-4cde-a9f0-0b1923801873">
  <data key="d3">Option 1’s level death benefit remains unchanged regardless of investment performance, meaning even with an 8.5% cap on the index account, the death benefit won’t increase due to market gains.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
