</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="e56d9b1f-113b-4961-abbd-159d8047aeca">
  <data key="d3">Option 1 offers a stable, unchanging death benefit that is unaffected by fluctuations in the indexed account’s performance. As such, even with a high 100% participation rate, the death benefit amount stays constant unless modified externally.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="c4dbdf51-a4cd-4a65-8903-f269d529eefd">
  <data key="d3">While the fixed account ensures a baseline return of at least 2%, this feature only indirectly affects Option 1’s level death benefit, which is reduced by withdrawals and loan balances rather than being tied directly to interest credits.</data>
  <data key="d4">MINOR_INFLUENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7">
  <data key="d3">A Level Death Benefit remains unchanged over time, meaning it is unaffected by fluctuations in the participation rate used for index crediting, though lower earnings due to cap constraints might limit fund accumulation.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1">
  <data key="d3">A Level Death Benefit does not change with account value fluctuations, so even though the indexed accounts have a 4% minimum credit cap, any reductions due to withdrawals or loans would still affect the final payout independently of the cap’s presence.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="9ac0c7c4-1321-469b-afaa-abe6d54dbd8e">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 describes a specific feature of a life insurance product, while fact_sentence_2 names the insurer responsible for issuing it. The second fact provides organizational context but does not influence or modify the meaning of the first.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL</data>
