<edge source="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678" target="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906">
  <data key="d3">While Option 2’s death benefit grows with account value beyond the specified amount, Option 1 remains static at $500,000, offering predictability without growth potential tied to investment returns.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPARATIVE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678" target="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199">
  <data key="d3">Option 2 enhances the death benefit beyond the stated amount by including current account value, unlike Option 1, which maintains a constant payout independent of investment gains.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRASTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678" target="f48d18db-916a-4e9a-ad5c-8b176c59da3c">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit formula for Option 2 includes the account value, which is unrelated to the fee comparison described for Option 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678" target="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6">
  <data key="d3">Option 2’s death benefit includes the specified amount plus the current account value, and since the account value grows over time, the total death benefit naturally increases accordingly.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678" target="99ca8905-b57d-4689-9164-12678eda198b">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit under Option 2 includes an additional account value component beyond the specified amount, making it potentially larger than Option 1’s flat benefit. This feature contrasts with Option 2's higher ongoing charges, which could erode long-term accumulation.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678" target="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76">
  <data key="d3">Option 2’s death benefit is determined by adding the specified amount to the account value, providing clarity necessary for evaluating switching decisions between benefit options.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678" target="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25">
  <data key="d3">Option 2's death benefit is determined by adding the specified amount to the account value. This definition supports understanding what the benefit entails before any policyholder action like changing it.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">Option 2's death benefit includes the account value, which contributes to determining the surrender value used to calculate the maximum loan amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678" target="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501">
  <data key="d3">Option 2’s death benefit calculation depends on adding the account value to the base specification, but increasing coverage beyond current levels requires proof of insurability due to higher risk exposure.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678" target="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647">
  <data key="d3">Option 2's death benefit includes the specified amount plus the account value, independent of when loans may be accessed. The timing of loan eligibility does not affect how the death benefit is calculated.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">Option 2's death benefit includes the account value added to a base specification. This detail stands independently from the fixed interest rate applied to policy loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">Option 2's death benefit includes both a base amount and accumulated account value, independent of loan costs. The net cost of borrowing via policy loans is determined separately based on interest rates and investment returns.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678" target="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9">
  <data key="d3">Option 2's death benefit includes the specified amount plus the account value, but this does not influence the minimum withdrawal requirement of $500.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">Option 2’s death benefit includes the account value, which may grow due to ongoing investment returns like those from loans earning 3% annually. This creates an indirect linkage where loan performance affects long-term account value.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_AFFECTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678" target="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d">
  <data key="d3">Option 2's death benefit includes the specified amount plus the account value, but this detail has no bearing on whether early withdrawals incur fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678" target="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5">
  <data key="d3">Option 2's death benefit includes the specified amount and account value, but this does not influence or relate to the fee imposed on later partial withdrawals.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678" target="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009">
  <data key="d3">Option 2's death benefit includes the account value, which influences the upper limit of permissible partial withdrawals. Since withdrawals cannot exceed the account value less any applicable surrender charge, the account value serves as a foundational metric linking both statements.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">Option 2's death benefit includes the specified amount plus account value, but any outstanding loans subtract from this total before payment. Therefore, loans directly lower the net benefit received.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678" target="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225">
  <data key="d3">Option 2's death benefit includes both a specified sum and account value, whereas Option 1’s death benefit decreases proportionally when partial withdrawals occur. These rules apply separately based on the chosen option.</data>
  <data key="d4">DIFFERS_BY_OPTION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678" target="9ac0c7c4-1321-469b-afaa-abe6d54dbd8e">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit calculation under Option 2 depends on internal policy terms unrelated to the insurer’s identity. Knowing the company name does not alter understanding of how the benefit is computed.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678" target="03e4f2e0-8fd5-4268-b333-707b317fcbd9">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains how the death benefit is calculated under Option 2, while fact_sentence_2 gives the insurer's contact number. These statements operate independently, with no mutual dependency or interaction.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
