<edge source="99ca8905-b57d-4689-9164-12678eda198b" target="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906">
  <data key="d3">Higher ongoing charges in Option 2 compared to Option 1 indicate greater costs over time, though this information does not affect the predetermined $500,000 death benefit specified under Option 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99ca8905-b57d-4689-9164-12678eda198b" target="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199">
  <data key="d3">Higher ongoing charges in Option 2 may impact its overall cost efficiency compared to Option 1’s stable structure. In turn, Option 1's consistent death benefit stands out due to lower expense burden relative to Option 2.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPARATIVE DIFFERENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99ca8905-b57d-4689-9164-12678eda198b" target="f48d18db-916a-4e9a-ad5c-8b176c59da3c">
  <data key="d3">The higher ongoing charges of Option 2 are directly attributable to its increased costs relative to Option 1, emphasizing the trade-off in pricing models.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPARATIVE DIFFERENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99ca8905-b57d-4689-9164-12678eda198b" target="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678">
  <data key="d3">Higher ongoing charges in Option 2 may gradually reduce the account value over time, thereby limiting the extent to which the total death benefit exceeds the base specified amount when combined with account value.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99ca8905-b57d-4689-9164-12678eda198b" target="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6">
  <data key="d3">Higher ongoing charges in Option 2 fund the mechanism enabling the death benefit to grow alongside the account value, making it possible for the benefit to increase over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99ca8905-b57d-4689-9164-12678eda198b" target="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76">
  <data key="d3">The higher ongoing charges associated with Option 2 may influence a policyholder’s decision to switch options, but the ability to switch is independent of the charge levels themselves.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99ca8905-b57d-4689-9164-12678eda198b" target="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647">
  <data key="d3">The statement about higher ongoing charges in Option 2 relates to long-term cost differences between benefit structures but does not influence when policy loans become accessible.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99ca8905-b57d-4689-9164-12678eda198b" target="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25">
  <data key="d3">The higher ongoing charges associated with Option 2 do not influence the requirement for 60 days’ advance notice when changing death benefit options. This procedural rule applies regardless of fee differences.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
