  <data key="d3">Option 2 incurs higher ongoing charges compared to Option 1, but this detail does not affect the fixed 4% interest rate applied to policy loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99ca8905-b57d-4689-9164-12678eda198b" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">The higher ongoing charges of Option 2 do not influence the interest earned by loaned funds, which continues to accumulate at 3% regardless of the chosen option.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99ca8905-b57d-4689-9164-12678eda198b" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">The statement about higher ongoing charges in Option 2 pertains to long-term expense differences between death benefit structures. This detail does not affect or explain the cap on policy loans set at 90% of surrender value.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99ca8905-b57d-4689-9164-12678eda198b" target="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9">
  <data key="d3">The statement about higher ongoing charges in Option 2 relates to long-term cost differences between death benefit structures but does not affect the minimum withdrawal amount requirement.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99ca8905-b57d-4689-9164-12678eda198b" target="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 compares ongoing charges between death benefit options, while fact_sentence_2 describes a separate fee waiver for early partial withdrawals. There is no direct connection between the fee structure of the benefit options and the withdrawal fee policy.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99ca8905-b57d-4689-9164-12678eda198b" target="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009">
  <data key="d3">Higher ongoing charges in Option 2 influence the effective account value over time, which impacts how much can be withdrawn without triggering penalties. This affects the maximum allowable partial withdrawal, constrained by remaining account value after deducting applicable surrender charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99ca8905-b57d-4689-9164-12678eda198b" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">Option 2 incurs higher ongoing charges compared to Option 1, reflecting its different fee structure. This detail is unrelated to the net cost of policy loans, which depends on separate mechanics involving interest rates and investment returns.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="99ca8905-b57d-4689-9164-12678eda198b" target="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for evidence of insurability when increasing coverage relates to why Option 2 has higher ongoing charges, as it involves greater risk and administrative complexity.</data>
