<edge source="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6" target="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906">
  <data key="d3">The dynamic nature of Option 2’s death benefit, which grows with account value, contrasts sharply with the fixed $500,000 benefit offered under Option 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRASTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6" target="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199">
  <data key="d3">Option 2’s growing death benefit contrasts sharply with Option 1's fixed benefit, illustrating a key design difference where flexibility and growth are traded for consistency.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRASTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6" target="f48d18db-916a-4e9a-ad5c-8b176c59da3c">
  <data key="d3">Option 2’s death benefit grows with account value, providing enhanced future payouts, whereas Option 1 maintains a stable level benefit with lower associated charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPARATIVE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6" target="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678">
  <data key="d3">Because the death benefit under Option 2 depends on the growing account value, its increase over time is directly tied to the accumulation within that account.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6" target="99ca8905-b57d-4689-9164-12678eda198b">
  <data key="d3">The growing death benefit under Option 2 justifies the higher ongoing charges, as the increased cost supports sustained accumulation and future payouts.</data>
  <data key="d4">JUSTIFIED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6" target="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit under Option 2 grows with account value, but only if policyholders meet requirements like providing evidence of insurability to increase coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6" target="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76">
  <data key="d3">Option 2 provides an escalating death benefit tied to account performance, offering long-term growth potential. This feature makes it a meaningful choice when evaluating whether to switch options annually.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6" target="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25">
  <data key="d3">Option 2’s death benefit grows with account value, reflecting long-term accumulation benefits. This feature requires careful planning when considering a switch, hence the need for 60 days’ notice before changing options.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6" target="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647">
  <data key="d3">The increase in death benefit under Option 2 depends on account value growth but does not influence when policy loans become accessible.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">Option 2's death benefit expands with account value gains, but this feature does not influence the fixed 4% interest charged on policy loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit under Option 2 grows with account value, reflecting long-term accumulation. The maximum loan amount is capped at 90% of the surrender value, providing access to cash while preserving some policy value.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit under Option 2 rises with account value growth, while any outstanding loans continue accruing interest at 3%, independent of the benefit calculation.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6" target="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit under Option 2 grows with account value, but this growth is independent of the minimum withdrawal threshold set at $500.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6" target="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009">
  <data key="d3">The growing account value in Option 2 determines the maximum allowable partial withdrawal, as it influences the base figure before subtracting surrender charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6" target="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d">
  <data key="d3">Option 2's death benefit rises with account value growth, but this does not affect the fee status of early partial withdrawals, which remain free regardless of benefit level changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">Option 2’s death benefit grows with account value, reflecting long-term investment gains. This growth may prompt some policyholders to take loans against the growing cash value, leading to associated borrowing costs.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6" target="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit under Option 2 grows with account value, but subsequent partial withdrawals beyond the tenth year trigger a $50 fee regardless of this growth dynamic.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">The growing death benefit under Option 2 may be reduced by any outstanding policy loans, meaning the full benefit gain could be offset by debt obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6" target="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225">
  <data key="d3">Option 2's death benefit grows with account value, whereas Option 1’s death benefit is reduced dollar-for-dollar by partial withdrawals. The two statements contrast behavior across different plan types rather than describing an interdependent process.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRASTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6" target="03e4f2e0-8fd5-4268-b333-707b317fcbd9">
  <data key="d3">Option 2's growing death benefit is a product-specific detail unrelated to the company's contact information provided in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6" target="9ac0c7c4-1321-469b-afaa-abe6d54dbd8e">
  <data key="d3">Option 2's growing death benefit is a feature of the policy offered by Horizon Wealth Protection Insurance, but the existence of the company does not affect the mechanism described.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6" target="dc9f1c71-4218-47d3-a2d6-f9dd0a3d8783">
  <data key="d3">Option 2’s increasing death benefit depends on account performance but has no inherent link to the insurer’s website domain. The site is merely a point of access for policy-related communications.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6" target="7c78ce63-cb1f-4b61-bdcd-88d0ce4bcb53">
  <data key="d3">The increase in death benefit under Option 2 depends on account performance but has no relation to the document's execution location in Chicago, Illinois.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6" target="47c97675-2a23-4fd8-af2f-5cf44ebaf17b">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit dynamics under Option 2 depend on account performance and do not involve leadership roles or signing authorities. No link exists between the policy’s financial features and the signatory’s job title.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6" target="79f032d3-1299-41de-85c7-f944c1411556">
  <data key="d3">Option 2’s growing death benefit depends on account performance, a core policy feature unrelated to when the document was signed. The execution date serves only as administrative context.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6" target="ba1c52cb-9fba-4846-9a66-8e0c71e2a754">
  <data key="d3">The increase in death benefit under Option 2 depends on account performance, while the presence of a seal confirms the document’s official nature. These elements serve different purposes—one operational, the other procedural—and do not affect each other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
