<edge source="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76" target="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906">
  <data key="d3">The availability of switching between death benefit options allows a policyholder to move away from the fixed $500,000 level benefit offered by Option 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76" target="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199">
  <data key="d3">The ability to switch death benefit options annually relies on having defined alternatives, such as the Level option described in Sentence 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76" target="f48d18db-916a-4e9a-ad5c-8b176c59da3c">
  <data key="d3">The availability of switching death benefit options annually does not impact or depend on the level of ongoing charges associated with Option 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76" target="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678">
  <data key="d3">The right to switch between death benefit options relies on knowing how each option calculates its payout, including that Option 2 includes an account value component.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFORMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76" target="99ca8905-b57d-4689-9164-12678eda198b">
  <data key="d3">While the possibility of switching allows policyholders to respond to differences in ongoing charges, the availability of switches does not affect the actual fee amounts charged to each option.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76" target="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6">
  <data key="d3">The ability to switch death benefit options annually allows policyholders to adapt their coverage strategy. This includes transitioning into Option 2, where benefits grow with account value.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76" target="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25">
  <data key="d3">Switching death benefit options requires an annual decision on the policy anniversary, but it cannot occur without providing at least 60 days’ prior notification to ensure administrative processing.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES_NOTICE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76" target="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501">
  <data key="d3">Switching to an increased death benefit requires proof of insurability, meaning that while switches are allowed annually, not all transitions are unconditional—they depend on health qualification when raising coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76" target="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647">
  <data key="d3">Switching death benefit options occurs annually on policy anniversaries, regardless of other features like loan eligibility. Loan access begins exactly one year after policy inception, making it a time-bound condition separate from benefit option changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">Switching death benefit options allows policyholders to adjust coverage types but does not affect the calculation of the maximum loan amount, which remains tied solely to the surrender value.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">Switching death benefit options allows policyholders flexibility in coverage selection but does not affect the fixed 4% interest rate charged on policy loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">Switching death benefit options allows policyholders flexibility in coverage selection but has no impact on how loan balances accrue interest in the fixed account.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76" target="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 describes the flexibility to change death benefit options annually. Fact sentence 2 specifies the minimum amount allowed for partial withdrawals. These are separate administrative provisions without mutual influence.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">Switching death benefit options allows policyholders to adjust coverage levels, but does not affect the interest cost associated with borrowing via policy loans, which remains independently calculated.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76" target="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009">
  <data key="d3">Switching death benefit options affects how much can be withdrawn later, since the maximum partial withdrawal depends on the current account value and applicable surrender charges, which might change post-switch.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76" target="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5">
  <data key="d3">Switching death benefit options occurs annually without affecting withdrawal fees. The fee for partial withdrawals is determined solely by the number of withdrawals made, regardless of benefit choice changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76" target="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d">
  <data key="d3">Switching death benefit options allows policyholders to adjust their coverage strategy annually, but this action does not affect the fee structure associated with partial withdrawals, which remain free for the first ten instances regardless of such switches.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76" target="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225">
  <data key="d3">Switching death benefit options allows policyholders to change plans annually, but this action has no direct effect on the reduction of the death benefit caused by partial withdrawals under Option 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">Switching death benefit options allows policyholders to change their coverage type but has no effect on existing loan balances or how those loans affect the final payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76" target="9ac0c7c4-1321-469b-afaa-abe6d54dbd8e">
  <data key="d3">The ability to switch death benefit options annually is a core policy feature detailed in the document, while the identity of the insurer, Horizon Wealth Protection Insurance, serves only as organizational attribution without affecting the functionality described.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76" target="03e4f2e0-8fd5-4268-b333-707b317fcbd9">
  <data key="d3">Switching death benefit options requires administrative action that might involve contacting the insurer, but the provided phone number does not confirm or explain this process.</data>
  <data key="d4">INCIDENTAL_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76" target="dc9f1c71-4218-47d3-a2d6-f9dd0a3d8783">
  <data key="d3">The ability to switch death benefit options is a core policy feature detailed in chunk_summary_1 but has no inherent link to the company's website address mentioned in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76" target="47c97675-2a23-4fd8-af2f-5cf44ebaf17b">
  <data key="d3">The ability to switch death benefit options annually is unrelated to the organizational hierarchy or identity of the signing officer.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
