  <data key="d3">A rule requiring 60 days’ notice before changing death benefit options implies that different types of options exist, including the Level benefit described in Sentence 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="f48d18db-916a-4e9a-ad5c-8b176c59da3c">
  <data key="d3">The need for 60 days’ advance notice to change options does not affect the comparison of ongoing charges between death benefit options.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678">
  <data key="d3">Changing death benefit options requires at least 60 days’ notice, ensuring administrative time for processing. This requirement applies regardless of whether the option being selected uses a level or increasing formula.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="99ca8905-b57d-4689-9164-12678eda198b">
  <data key="d3">The necessity of providing 60 days’ advance notice before switching death benefit options does not affect the level of ongoing charges assessed under each option, including Option 2’s higher fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for 60 days’ advance notice ensures sufficient processing time when altering death benefit options. Since Option 2 offers an increasing benefit tied to account performance, timely notification helps maintain alignment with financial goals.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76">
  <data key="d3">The need for 60 days’ advance notice ensures sufficient time to process changes before the policy anniversary when switches become effective.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_SWITCHING</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">Changing death benefit options requires prior notification, but this does not affect the maximum allowable loan based on surrender value.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501">
  <data key="d3">Changing death benefit options requires at least 60 days’ notice, and if the policyholder seeks to increase coverage beyond current levels, additional documentation proving insurability must be submitted.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES AND CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647">
  <data key="d3">Changing death benefit options requires at least 60 days’ notice, but this does not affect when policy loans become accessible. Loan eligibility depends solely on the policy’s duration since inception.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">Changing death benefit options requires prior notification, but this requirement does not influence or relate to the fixed interest rate applied to policy loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 outlines the requirement for advance notice when modifying death benefits, ensuring procedural compliance. Fact sentence 2 sets a threshold for partial withdrawals, independent of any notification period.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">Changing death benefit options requires prior notification, but this does not affect how borrowed funds grow over time. The requirement for advance notice applies independently of loan earnings dynamics.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009">
  <data key="d3">Changing death benefit options requires prior notification, which ensures proper processing time. This timing rule does not affect how much can be withdrawn, which depends instead on account value and surrender charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">Changing death benefit options requires prior notification, but this requirement does not influence the calculation or outcome of the net cost associated with taking out a policy loan.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d">
  <data key="d3">Changing death benefit options requires prior notification but does not affect the fee status of partial withdrawals. The availability of free withdrawals is independent of the timing requirements for switching benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5">
  <data key="d3">Changing death benefit options requires 60 days’ prior notice, but this does not affect the fee structure for partial withdrawals beyond the tenth transaction.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225">
  <data key="d3">Changing death benefit options requires prior notification, but this does not affect how partial withdrawals impact the death benefit under Option 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">Changing death benefit options requires prior notification, but this requirement has no bearing on how existing loans impact the eventual death benefit amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_EFFECT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e">
  <data key="d3">Changing death benefit options requires 60 days’ notice, which operates within the same timeframe affected by surrender charges lasting up to 12 years. This suggests planning ahead is crucial whether altering benefits or terminating the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_OVERLAP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332">
  <data key="d3">The 60-day notice rule for changing death benefit options may influence when a policyholder decides to exit or modify their plan, potentially affecting whether they incur the 7% surrender charge in Year 4.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_REINFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines timing rules for modifying death benefits, while fact_sentence_2 confirms a specific surrender charge applicable in Year 3, reinforcing the timeline-dependent nature of policy costs discussed in both summaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSISTENT_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines a mandatory waiting period before altering death benefit structures, while fact_sentence_2 states that the highest surrender penalty occurs in Year 1. These two elements together inform strategic decision-making around when to modify benefits versus surrendering the policy early.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633">
  <data key="d3">The 60-day notice rule for changing death benefits interacts with surrender charges like the 6% fee in Year 5, as early changes may incur such penalties depending on timing and policy status.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines a procedural rule requiring advanced notice for changes to death benefits, while fact_sentence_2 specifies a specific surrender charge applicable in Year 2. Together, they reflect distinct yet temporally aligned policy restrictions governing early-year actions.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="84b84dec-45b7-4ca8-ae2f-a68466866f24">
  <data key="d3">The 60-day notice rule for altering death benefit options applies regardless of surrender charges like those in Year 6, meaning switching benefits does not trigger immediate surrender penalties but requires adherence to notification timelines.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca">
  <data key="d3">Changing death benefit options requires advanced notice, and the timing may influence whether surrender charges apply, making the 4% charge in Year 7 relevant to such decisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00">
  <data key="d3">The 60-day notice rule for modifying death benefits operates within the same multi-year timeframe governed by declining surrender charges, including the 2% charge in Year 9, suggesting coordinated policy design across administrative and financial provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75">
  <data key="d3">The 60-day notice rule for altering death benefit options operates independently of surrender charges, but both are part of the same policy’s time-bound structural rules. Knowing the Year 8 surrender charge helps assess financial implications when considering changes late in the policy term.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">The 60-day notice rule for changing death benefits becomes more strategically relevant when considering that surrender charges end in Year 12, allowing greater flexibility in policy adjustments without financial penalties.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">The 60-day notice rule for changing death benefits operates within a policy environment where surrender charges decline over time, including a 1% charge in Year 10, suggesting such changes may be strategically timed near the end of high-charge periods.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for 60 days’ notice to modify death benefits operates independently of the specific surrender charge amount in Year 11, though both reflect temporal restrictions affecting policyholder decisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">Changing death benefit options requires 60 days’ notice, affecting future cash surrender value calculations since surrender charges and loans influence final payout amounts defined in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for 60 days’ advance notice when altering death benefit options aligns with broader policy timelines involving financial adjustments like surrender charges, which are applied over the first 10 years based on premiums paid.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="9d636a77-9852-432c-b8fb-7593d751a2da">
  <data key="d3">The 60-day notice rule ensures proper administrative handling before modifying death benefit terms, which may affect future eligibility for partial withdrawals tied to account value. However, the ability to take up to 10% annual withdrawals does not depend on this notice period.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for 60 days’ notice to modify death benefit options does not conflict with the availability of free partial withdrawals after Year 1; both reflect permitted actions once the policy has been active for over a year.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="9ac0c7c4-1321-469b-afaa-abe6d54dbd8e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for 60 days’ advance notice to modify death benefits is part of the policy terms detailed in the document, but it is unrelated to the identification of the issuing company, Horizon Wealth Protection Insurance.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="03e4f2e0-8fd5-4268-b333-707b317fcbd9">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines administrative procedures for modifying death benefits, while fact_sentence_2 provides a generic contact number for the insurer. There is no interaction between these two pieces of information.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="ba1c52cb-9fba-4846-9a66-8e0c71e2a754">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines a procedural requirement tied to policy changes, while fact_sentence_2 notes a visual authentication feature. The seal lends authority to the rule stated in fact_sentence_1, reinforcing the document’s legitimacy.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_SUPPORT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="dc9f1c71-4218-47d3-a2d6-f9dd0a3d8783">
  <data key="d3">The 60-day notice requirement for altering death benefits is a procedural detail within the policy framework, while the company's website is a separate channel for accessing information. There is no functional interaction between these two pieces of information.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="7c78ce63-cb1f-4b61-bdcd-88d0ce4bcb53">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for 60 days’ advance notice to modify death benefits pertains to internal policy procedures, while the document's execution in Chicago, Illinois, indicates its legal origin but does not influence or depend on that procedural rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="79f032d3-1299-41de-85c7-f944c1411556">
  <data key="d3">The 60-day notice requirement applies to any future modification of death benefits, regardless of when the document was signed. The execution date anchors the timeline but doesn't affect the operational rules described.</data>
  <data key="d4">TEMPORALLY_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25" target="e9cf97a9-cf24-4d3c-adf8-586c6935d0e1">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines a specific policy requirement regarding changes to death benefits, which is governed by the insurer identified in fact_sentence_2. This connection situates the procedural detail within its organizational context.</data>
  <data key="d4">PROVENANCE_OF</data>
