<edge source="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501" target="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906">
  <data key="d3">To increase the death benefit above the default $500,000 level, policyholders must meet specific criteria including providing evidence of insurability, thus making such changes contingent on external validation rather than automatic adjustment.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501" target="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199">
  <data key="d3">Requiring evidence of insurability to increase coverage applies only to the changing nature of benefits under the increasing option, independent of whether Option 1 maintains a static death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501" target="f48d18db-916a-4e9a-ad5c-8b176c59da3c">
  <data key="d3">The necessity of providing evidence of insurability when increasing coverage affects decision-making around plan changes, potentially influencing whether individuals opt into higher-cost plans despite Option 1’s favorable fee structure.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501" target="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678">
  <data key="d3">To access increased death benefits under Option 2—which include additional account value—the policyholder must provide evidence of insurability when raising coverage limits.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_CALCULATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501" target="99ca8905-b57d-4689-9164-12678eda198b">
  <data key="d3">Higher ongoing charges in Option 2 justify the necessity of providing evidence of insurability before increasing coverage, ensuring policyholder eligibility amid increased financial exposure.</data>
  <data key="d4">JUSTIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501" target="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6">
  <data key="d3">To enable future increases in the death benefit tied to account value growth, policyholders must provide evidence of insurability when raising coverage limits.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501" target="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76">
  <data key="d3">The need for evidence of insurability arises specifically when upgrading coverage via a switch, making it a prerequisite for certain types of changes permitted under the annual switch rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501" target="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25">
  <data key="d3">To increase coverage, a policyholder must provide evidence of insurability, but such changes cannot occur without first giving at least 60 days’ advance notice.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for evidence of insurability applies when seeking higher coverage but does not influence the maximum allowable loan amount tied to surrender value.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501" target="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647">
  <data key="d3">Increasing coverage requires proof of insurability, but this does not affect when policy loans become available. Loan eligibility depends solely on the policy’s duration, independent of underwriting requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for evidence of insurability applies when modifying coverage terms but does not affect how loaned funds accrue interest in the fixed account.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501" target="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 outlines a prerequisite condition for modifying coverage terms, specifically requiring proof of health status when seeking higher benefits. Fact sentence 2 sets a minimum threshold for accessing funds via partial withdrawals, unrelated to coverage changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">Evidence of insurability ensures eligibility to raise coverage limits, but does not affect the interest cost associated with taking out a loan. The 1% net cost of borrowing remains independent of whether such evidence was submitted.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501" target="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d">
  <data key="d3">Increasing coverage requires evidence of insurability, but this condition has no direct connection to the fee-free status of early partial withdrawals.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501" target="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for evidence of insurability when increasing coverage does not affect the fee structure for partial withdrawals after the tenth instance.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501" target="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009">
  <data key="d3">Increasing coverage beyond current levels requires proof of insurability, which may affect future liquidity since higher coverage could influence account value dynamics. This does not directly impact the maximum allowable partial withdrawal, which is determined independently by account value and surrender charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">Increasing coverage requires evidence of insurability, but this does not influence how existing loans impact the death benefit. The two facts operate independently regarding death benefit outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501" target="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225">
  <data key="d3">Evidence of insurability applies only when modifying coverage type, not when making withdrawals. The requirement does not influence withdrawal impacts on the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for evidence of insurability applies when upgrading coverage, while the fixed 4% loan rate governs borrowing costs regardless of coverage changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501" target="9ac0c7c4-1321-469b-afaa-abe6d54dbd8e">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines a condition related to modifying coverage, relevant to policyholder actions. Fact_sentence_2 identifies the insurer responsible for administering such policies but adds no new operational detail about eligibility or requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_SOURCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501" target="03e4f2e0-8fd5-4268-b333-707b317fcbd9">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 describes a prerequisite for modifying coverage that requires proof of insurability, while fact_sentence_2 gives the contact number for the issuing company. These pieces of information serve different purposes and do not influence each other logically.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501" target="7c78ce63-cb1f-4b61-bdcd-88d0ce4bcb53">
  <data key="d3">The necessity of providing evidence of insurability for increased coverage is unrelated to the geographic origin of the document’s execution. One concerns internal policy rules, while the other addresses legal or logistical provenance.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501" target="dc9f1c71-4218-47d3-a2d6-f9dd0a3d8783">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for evidence of insurability when increasing coverage is unrelated to the availability of the insurer's website, though both are relevant aspects of the broader policy framework provided by Horizon Wealth Protection Insurance.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501" target="47c97675-2a23-4fd8-af2f-5cf44ebaf17b">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for evidence of insurability when increasing coverage is unrelated to the executive position of the signatory on the document.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501" target="ba1c52cb-9fba-4846-9a66-8e0c71e2a754">
  <data key="d3">The need for evidence of insurability when increasing coverage is a substantive policy condition unrelated to the physical authentication feature of a corporate seal on the document.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
