<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906">
  <data key="d3">The availability of policy loans after one year of policy duration does not impact the predetermined $500,000 death benefit under Option 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199">
  <data key="d3">Loan availability after one year is independent of whether the death benefit is set at a constant amount. It is governed by policy tenure rather than benefit design.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="f48d18db-916a-4e9a-ad5c-8b176c59da3c">
  <data key="d3">Loan eligibility after one year is independent of the fee structure associated with Option 1, meaning it neither influences nor results from its cost characteristics.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678">
  <data key="d3">Loan access becomes possible after one year of policy activity, regardless of whether the death benefit uses a level or increasing formula. This timeline constraint applies uniformly across benefit options.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="99ca8905-b57d-4689-9164-12678eda198b">
  <data key="d3">The availability of policy loans after one year depends on policy duration and is independent of the fee structure associated with either death benefit option.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6">
  <data key="d3">Loan eligibility after one year is independent of how the death benefit evolves under Option 2.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76">
  <data key="d3">Loan availability starts after one full year of policy activity, which is unrelated to the frequency or timing of death benefit switches that occur annually based on policy anniversaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">POSTPONED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25">
  <data key="d3">Policy loans are available only after one year of policy activity, regardless of whether a request to change death benefits is pending or submitted.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501">
  <data key="d3">The availability of policy loans after one year does not impact the need for evidence of insurability when increasing coverage. The two rules operate independently based on separate policy triggers.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">The ability to take a policy loan begins after one year of policy activity, enabling access to funds capped at 90% of the surrender value.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">Once the policy has been active for one year, borrowers gain access to loans, which are subject to a fixed 4% annual interest rate.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">Once policy loans become accessible after one year of policy activity, any borrowed amounts continue to accrue interest at the fixed account rate of 3% annually.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">Loan access begins after one year of policy activity, enabling borrowers to utilize funds. This eligibility enables the application of a 1% net annual cost based on interest differentials between the loan rate and investment earnings.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9">
  <data key="d3">Loan availability begins after one year of policy activity, whereas partial withdrawals require a minimum of $500 regardless of loan status. These are distinct transactional thresholds without mutual influence.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d">
  <data key="d3">Loan eligibility begins after one year of policy activity, but this does not affect the fee structure of initial partial withdrawals, which remain free regardless of loan access.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5">
  <data key="d3">The availability of policy loans after one year does not influence the fee applied to partial withdrawals after the tenth instance. The two financial mechanisms operate independently regarding timing and costs.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009">
  <data key="d3">Loan eligibility begins after one year of policy activity, enabling early access to funds. However, the maximum partial withdrawal is constrained by the current account value less any applicable surrender charge, reflecting ongoing penalty structures that affect accessible equity.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_LIMIT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">Once policy loans are accessible after one year, any borrowed amounts remain outstanding until repaid. These unpaid balances directly decrease the final death benefit paid out when a claim is made.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225">
  <data key="d3">The availability of policy loans after one year does not affect how partial withdrawals impact the death benefit under Option 1. These are independent features governed by separate rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="1d4b712e-5e26-4cf9-a7ad-301c683e58e3">
  <data key="d3">Loan eligibility begins after one year, independently of the cap rate mechanism governing index account earnings.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77">
  <data key="d3">Loan eligibility after one year depends on policy duration, whereas the Floor Rate protects gains/losses regardless of time, making it a separate structural safeguard.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955">
  <data key="d3">Policy loans being accessible after one year do not affect how index gains are calculated via the Participation Rate. Conversely, the Participation Rate’s function remains unchanged regardless of when loans are taken.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3">
  <data key="d3">Loan access becomes possible after one year, aligning with the annual cycle used by the Point-to-Point Method, though the two features function without dependency.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="db06e7c6-2f5b-4dca-9e5a-d5dd96d2c405">
  <data key="d3">Loan availability after one year allows policyholders to draw against accumulated value, potentially influencing decisions about allocating assets into the Fixed Account, where earnings are locked in at 3.0% annually.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="f64306b3-60d7-48b6-82c2-6580397642e1">
  <data key="d3">Policy loans accessible after one year offer withdrawal flexibility, unrelated to the 0% floor that protects the Global Diversified Index Account from negative returns. The floor ensures downside protection regardless of when loans are taken.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="326a19f6-3d06-4cde-a9f0-0b1923801873">
  <data key="d3">Policy loans being accessible after one year provide a funding option unrelated to the return cap on the Global Diversified Index Account. This feature allows cash access based on policy duration rather than investment performance thresholds.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="e56d9b1f-113b-4961-abbd-159d8047aeca">
  <data key="d3">Availability of policy loans after one year depends on accumulated cash value, which is influenced by factors including the participation rate in indexed accounts like the Global Diversified Index Account, though not explicitly tied to it.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="c4dbdf51-a4cd-4a65-8903-f269d529eefd">
  <data key="d3">Loan availability after one year depends on policy tenure, while the fixed account’s 2% guarantee offers consistent returns regardless of loan usage, operating independently of loan timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7">
  <data key="d3">Loan eligibility after one year allows policyholders to draw funds based on accumulated value, whereas the 25% minimum participation rate safeguards index-linked earnings against poor market outcomes. Although both impact long-term value accumulation, they function separately and have no mutual dependence or conflict.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1">
  <data key="d3">The availability of policy loans after one year provides access to cash value, which could indirectly relate to investment strategy involving indexed accounts, though it does not alter or rely on the 4% minimum cap for credited interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">Loan availability after one year provides liquidity that might help offset the impact of the 3.5% premium load, especially if holders need funds without terminating coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">Access to policy loans after one year depends on maintaining sufficient account value, which is influenced by regular COI deductions and premium contributions outlined in the first fact.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="6bfb8452-bcec-4db6-b212-fd25bdcfbc79">
  <data key="d3">Loan eligibility after one year depends on sufficient cash accumulation, which is influenced by ongoing deductions like the $12 monthly administrative charge.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d3">The eligibility for policy loans after one year hinges on the account value being sufficiently maintained, supporting continued premium flexibility and stability.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db">
  <data key="d3">Policy loans becoming available after one year provide liquidity, potentially affecting the account value that underpins the floor protection guarantee described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647" target="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299">
  <data key="d3">Policy loans becoming available after one year provide financial flexibility regardless of the floor protection setting. Even without a protective floor, borrowers can still access cash value, albeit based on current account value—which might be reduced by market volatility.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
