<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount is capped at 90% of the surrender value, regardless of the chosen death benefit option.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan allowed is limited to 90% of the surrender value, regardless of whether the death benefit option is Level or Increasing. This restriction exists independently of how the death benefit is structured.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="f48d18db-916a-4e9a-ad5c-8b176c59da3c">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan limit being 90% of the surrender value does not affect the level of ongoing charges associated with Option 1, as those are governed by separate fee structures.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan allowed depends on the surrender value, which itself influences the total death benefit under Option 2 when combined with the specified amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="99ca8905-b57d-4689-9164-12678eda198b">
  <data key="d3">The rule limiting policy loans to 90% of surrender value defines borrowing capacity regardless of the option chosen. It does not depend on whether Option 1 or Option 2 incurs higher ongoing charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6">
  <data key="d3">The policy allows loans up to 90% of the surrender value, enabling liquidity without affecting the death benefit’s growth path. However, such loans may indirectly impact future benefits if unpaid.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan limit set at 90% of surrender value is independent of whether a policyholder chooses to switch death benefit options annually.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25">
  <data key="d3">The cap on policy loans at 90% of surrender value is independent of the requirement for 60-day notice when switching death benefit options.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501">
  <data key="d3">The cap on policy loans at 90% of surrender value operates independently of whether evidence of insurability is needed to adjust coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647">
  <data key="d3">Once the policy has been active for one year, borrowers may access up to 90% of the surrender value as a loan.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount is capped at 90% of the surrender value, and this borrowed sum accrues interest at a fixed annual rate of 4%, determining the total repayment obligation.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount is capped at 90% of the surrender value, ensuring that any funds withdrawn remain within defined limits. These borrowed funds continue to earn interest at the fixed account rate of 3%, contributing to overall policy performance.</data>
  <data key="d4">LIMITS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan limit of 90% of surrender value sets the basis for calculating the actual cost of borrowing. This constraint determines the scale of the loan, which directly influences the net annual cost derived from the interest differential.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 defines the maximum allowable loan based on surrender value, whereas fact sentence 2 establishes the smallest permissible withdrawal amount. These are independent operational limits governing different types of transactions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan limit tied to surrender value does not influence the fee structure for early partial withdrawals. The information about free withdrawals applies independently of borrowing capacity.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 establishes that loans cannot exceed 90% of surrender value, limiting access to cash. Fact sentence 2 specifies that partial withdrawals are capped by the remaining account value after deducting any applicable surrender charges, reflecting another constraint on fund availability.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan limit tied to surrender value does not influence the fee structure for partial withdrawals. The $50 fee applies independently once the threshold of ten withdrawals is exceeded.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount is capped at 90% of the surrender value, independent of withdrawal impacts. This constraint does not influence how withdrawals modify the death benefit under Option 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">The maximum allowable loan is set at 90% of the surrender value, enabling borrowers to access significant funds. However, any unpaid loans reduce the final death benefit paid out when the policyholder passes away.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="1d4b712e-5e26-4cf9-a7ad-301c683e58e3">
  <data key="d3">Policy loan limits are determined by surrender value percentages and do not depend on or affect the cap rates applied to index account earnings.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77">
  <data key="d3">Policy loan availability up to 90% of surrender value operates independently of the Floor Rate's role in capping downside risk in indexed accounts.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan limit of 90% of surrender value depends on the policy’s accumulated cash value, which includes credits influenced by the Participation Rate.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3">
  <data key="d3">Policy loan availability up to 90% of surrender value depends on accumulated cash value, which may be influenced by the Point-to-Point Method’s annual crediting process, though this link is indirect and conditional on long-term accumulation.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount depends on the surrender value, which itself is reduced by surrender charges applied in the first 12 years, meaning these two facts jointly constrain borrowing capacity during early policy tenure.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount depends on the surrender value, which is reduced by the 10% Year 1 surrender charge, limiting the effective collateral available for loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
