<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount depends on the surrender value, which itself is reduced by surrender charges like the 3% assessed in Year 8. This means the actual usable surrender value—and thus the loan ceiling—is affected by ongoing charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount depends on the surrender value, which itself is reduced by surrender charges like the 2% charge in Year 9. Thus, higher future surrender charges could indirectly constrain effective loan availability.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount depends on the surrender value, which is reduced by surrender charges like the 0.5% in Year 11. Thus, lower surrender charges increase usable surrender value and indirectly support higher allowable loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount relies on the surrender value, which is diminished by surrender charges like the 1% charge in Year 10. Thus, knowing the surrender charge helps determine the true usable portion of the surrender value for borrowing.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
