  <data key="d3">A higher surrender value due to lower COI impact allows greater policy loan capacity, making the loan limit dependent on the ongoing effect of COI deductions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="6bfb8452-bcec-4db6-b212-fd25bdcfbc79">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s maximum loan limit of 90% of surrender value depends on accumulated account value, which is affected by periodic charges such as the $12 monthly administrative fee mentioned earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d3">The ability to skip premium payments hinges on having enough account value, which directly affects the maximum loanable amount based on surrender value.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db">
  <data key="d3">The ability to borrow up to 90% of surrender value provides liquidity without triggering surrender, whereas floor protection shields gains from a 5% drop in the index. Both support long-term stability but function in distinct operational domains.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299">
  <data key="d3">A higher surrender value, influenced by factors like investment performance and premiums paid, increases the maximum loan amount possible, though it does not impact the zero-floor setting established in the first fact.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7">
  <data key="d3">A maximum loan limit of 90% of surrender value reflects financial flexibility, which complements the safety net provided by zero interest credit during market dips, preserving access to funds despite volatility.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
