  <data key="d3">Loan proceeds are charged a fixed 4% interest rate, yet they continue to accumulate earnings at a 3% fixed account rate, creating a net cost differential.</data>
  <data key="d4">FINANCIAL TRADE-OFF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">The 4% fixed interest rate on policy loans results in a net annual cost of only 1% when combined with the 3% return earned in the fixed account, effectively subsidizing part of the borrowing cost.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that policy loans carry a fixed 4% annual interest rate. This detail is unrelated to the minimum threshold for partial withdrawals, which is set at $500 regardless of loan rates.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d">
  <data key="d3">The loan interest rate is set at 4%, but this does not affect the fee structure for partial withdrawals, which remain free for the first ten instances regardless of borrowing activity.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009">
  <data key="d3">The fixed 4% interest rate on loans affects overall policy costs, influencing how much equity remains when making withdrawals. However, the maximum withdrawal limit is determined independently by account value and surrender charges, without requiring knowledge of the loan's interest rate.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5">
  <data key="d3">The fixed 4% interest rate on policy loans does not affect the $50 fee applied to partial withdrawals made after the tenth withdrawal. The two features operate independently within the policy’s financial framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225">
  <data key="d3">The fixed 4% interest rate on policy loans affects borrowing costs but has no bearing on how partial withdrawals impact the death benefit under Option 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">A fixed 4% interest rate on policy loans increases the total debt owed over time, leading to greater reductions in the death benefit when claims are processed due to unpaid balances.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="1d4b712e-5e26-4cf9-a7ad-301c683e58e3">
  <data key="d3">A fixed 4% policy loan rate offers predictable borrowing costs regardless of index performance, making it less sensitive to changes in the Cap Rate, which governs only the upside potential of certain investment accounts.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77">
  <data key="d3">A fixed 4% loan interest rate contrasts with the variable nature of indexed crediting governed by the Floor Rate, which protects against negative returns but does not affect loan costs.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955">
  <data key="d3">While the loan interest rate affects the cost of borrowing against the policy, it does not influence how index gains are calculated or allocated via the Participation Rate. They represent different aspects of policy economics.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3">
  <data key="d3">A fixed 4% loan interest rate operates independently of the annual index-based crediting used in the Point-to-Point Method.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="db06e7c6-2f5b-4dca-9e5a-d5dd96d2c405">
  <data key="d3">Policy loans at 4% interest make the 3.0% return on the Fixed Account insufficient to offset borrowing costs, making the Fixed Account less advantageous when used as collateral for loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">FINANCIAL_CONTRAST</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="f64306b3-60d7-48b6-82c2-6580397642e1">
  <data key="d3">The fixed 4% policy loan rate applies regardless of performance in the indexed accounts, including those with a 0% floor. Thus, the floor protection does not influence or alter the loan's interest terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="326a19f6-3d06-4cde-a9f0-0b1923801873">
  <data key="d3">The fixed 4% policy loan rate influences cash flow and cost of borrowing, whereas the 8.5% cap restricts upside potential in the indexed account. Although both appear in the same product documentation, they do not influence or depend on each other’s parameters.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="e56d9b1f-113b-4961-abbd-159d8047aeca">
  <data key="d3">The fixed 4% policy loan rate does not impact the 100% participation rate in the indexed account, nor is it influenced by its performance or design parameters.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="c4dbdf51-a4cd-4a65-8903-f269d529eefd">
  <data key="d3">Policy loans are charged at 4%, which surpasses the fixed account’s guaranteed 2% return. As such, taking out a loan reduces the overall value of the fixed account unless offset by better-performing investments elsewhere.</data>
  <data key="d4">FINANCIAL_INEFFICIENCY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7">
  <data key="d3">The 4% fixed loan interest rate governs borrowing costs regardless of indexed account performance, which is governed by its own cap, floor, and participation rate rules—including the 25% minimum.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1">
  <data key="d3">The fixed 4% loan interest rate reflects financing terms for policyholder borrowings, unrelated to the 4% minimum cap on indexed credits, which protects upside in equity-linked accounts.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e">
  <data key="d3">The fixed 4% loan interest rate operates independently of surrender charges but contributes to the total cost of borrowing when combined with early surrender risks. Both features affect the effective return and liquidity of the policy’s cash value over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890">
  <data key="d3">The fixed 4% loan interest rate complements the information about declining surrender charges, showing how early policyholder actions like taking loans may affect long-term value compared to lapsing or surrendering.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018">
  <data key="d3">The fixed 4% loan interest rate contributes to the effective cost of borrowing against the policy, which interacts with the 10% surrender charge in Year 1 by influencing whether it's financially prudent to take a loan instead of surrendering the policy early.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332">
  <data key="d3">The fixed 4% loan interest rate complements the overall cost structure of the policy, while the 7% surrender charge in Year 4 reflects an additional penalty for early withdrawal, contributing to the total economic burden of policy access.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633">
  <data key="d3">The fixed 4% interest rate on policy loans complements the understanding of surrender charges like the 6% fee in Year 5 by illustrating different types of financial obligations tied to policy usage.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b">
  <data key="d3">The fixed 4% loan interest rate contributes to long-term policy cost calculations, while the 8% surrender charge in Year 3 reflects penalty structures tied to early withdrawal. Though unrelated in mechanism, both affect total policy value over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_FACTOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca">
  <data key="d3">The 4% fixed loan interest rate complements the understanding of total policy costs, including the 4% surrender charge in Year 7, which reflects another layer of expense when exiting the policy early.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="84b84dec-45b7-4ca8-ae2f-a68466866f24">
  <data key="d3">The fixed 4% loan interest rate complements the overall cost structure outlined in the surrender charge schedule, where higher early-year penalties reflect the insurer's risk management strategy across multiple policy features.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00">
  <data key="d3">The fixed 4% loan interest rate contributes to long-term policy cost considerations, while the Year 9 surrender charge of 2% reflects declining penalty structures over time. Together, they inform total ownership expenses across different phases of the policy lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75">
  <data key="d3">The fixed 4% loan interest rate contributes to the effective cost of borrowing, which interacts with surrender charges like the 3% in Year 8, influencing total policy expenses over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELEVANCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">The 4% fixed loan rate contributes to a net annual cost of 1%, which becomes more relevant in Year 10 when surrender charges drop to 1%, making early surrender less costly relative to borrowing expenses.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">The fixed loan interest rate affects long-term policy affordability, especially when combined with surrender charges that depend on early premium payments, influencing whether borrowers opt for loans versus withdrawals.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">The fixed 4% loan interest rate remains constant regardless of surrender charge phase, but its financial impact lessens over time due to declining surrender charges post-Year 11, allowing greater flexibility in managing policy liquidity without penalty.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">The fixed 4% interest rate on policy loans increases the total debt owed, thereby reducing the cash surrender value when loans remain unpaid. This makes the loan terms financially consequential for the ultimate surrender outcome.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">The 4% fixed loan interest rate remains relevant even in Year 11, where surrender charges drop significantly to 0.5%, reducing barriers to withdrawing funds or repaying loans without substantial penalties.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="9d636a77-9852-432c-b8fb-7593d751a2da">
  <data key="d3">Policy loans incur a fixed 4% interest rate, whereas partial withdrawals allow up to 10% of the account value annually without penalty. While both provide access to funds, withdrawals do not accrue interest like loans, making them more favorable for short-term needs.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b">
  <data key="d3">Policy loans at a fixed 4% rate provide borrowing capacity after Year 1, while free partial withdrawals allow access to funds without surrender charges. These two provisions together enhance post-year-one liquidity, offering complementary pathways for accessing policy value.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">The fixed 4% loan interest rate reflects borrowing costs separate from premium loads; however, higher premiums due to the 3.5% charge may increase overall policy value, indirectly affecting loan availability based on surrender value.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">A fixed 4% loan interest rate increases the cost of borrowing, which could strain the account balance already reduced by recurring COI charges, affecting sustained policy viability.</data>
  <data key="d4">INCREASES_FINANCIAL_PRESSURE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="6bfb8452-bcec-4db6-b212-fd25bdcfbc79">
  <data key="d3">A 4% fixed interest rate on policy loans influences the total cost of accessing cash value, which may offset or compound the impact of ongoing expenses such as the $12 monthly administrative fee.</data>
  <data key="d4">FINANCIAL_CONTEXTUALIZER</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d3">Maintaining sufficient account value to avoid premium payments helps prevent reliance on loans, thereby reducing exposure to the 4% loan interest cost.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_AFFECTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.55</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db">
  <data key="d3">A fixed 4% loan interest rate impacts the economic burden when accessing funds, potentially affecting the ability to maintain sufficient account value needed to activate floor protection during downturns.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_DEPENDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299">
  <data key="d3">The fixed 4% loan interest rate has no bearing on the 0% floor protection level, as it pertains solely to borrowed funds and not to the underlying investment guarantees within the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7">
  <data key="d3">A fixed 4% loan interest rate does not affect the condition under which zero interest is credited during a 5% index drop. The loan term is independent of the index-based crediting rules governing account growth.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="70667dae-ff8c-4bac-bf04-03807ddb6bd7">
  <data key="d3">The fixed 4% loan interest rate supports the overall risk mitigation strategy implied by the absence of principal loss during market declines, enabling borrowers to leverage policy value securely.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="9ac0c7c4-1321-469b-afaa-abe6d54dbd8e">
  <data key="d3">The fixed 4% interest rate on policy loans is a key feature of the insurance product offered by Horizon Wealth Protection Insurance, providing clarity on borrowing costs within the policy’s financial structure.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6" target="03e4f2e0-8fd5-4268-b333-707b317fcbd9">
  <data key="d3">The fixed 4% interest rate on policy loans is part of the financial mechanics described in the document, while the phone number serves as a point of contact for inquiries about such terms. There is no functional interaction between them.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
