<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906">
  <data key="d3">Funds taken via loan continue to earn 3% annually in the fixed account, even though such loans may reduce the final death benefit payment under Option 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199">
  <data key="d3">Funds taken out via loan continue accruing interest at 3%, but this does not affect the stability or structure of the level death benefit defined in Option 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="f48d18db-916a-4e9a-ad5c-8b176c59da3c">
  <data key="d3">Loan earnings at 3% per year occur regardless of whether Option 1 has lower ongoing charges, so the charge level does not influence this feature.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678">
  <data key="d3">Loan balances earn 3% annually in the fixed account, contributing to account value growth, which increases the death benefit under Option 2 since it factors in account value.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRIBUTES_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="99ca8905-b57d-4689-9164-12678eda198b">
  <data key="d3">Loan earnings at 3% per year occur independently of whether Option 1 or Option 2 is selected, so they are unaffected by the differential charging structure between the two plans.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6">
  <data key="d3">Loan balances grow at 3% annually regardless of changes in the death benefit tied to account value under Option 2.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76">
  <data key="d3">Loan balances continue earning 3% annually regardless of changes to the death benefit option selected, meaning the interest mechanism operates independently of benefit choice switches.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25">
  <data key="d3">Loan balances earn interest regardless of whether a policyholder plans to modify their death benefit option, so the timing rule for changes has no impact on accrued returns.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501">
  <data key="d3">Loan proceeds continue to earn 3% annually regardless of whether additional coverage requires evidence of insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647">
  <data key="d3">The ability for loaned funds to earn 3% annually relies on the policy having been active for at least one year, when loans are permitted.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">Funds borrowed against the policy accumulate interest at 3% annually in the fixed account, but such borrowing is restricted to 90% of the surrender value, limiting exposure and risk.</data>
  <data key="d4">EARNED_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">Despite being subject to a 4% interest charge, loaned funds maintain a 3% annual return in the fixed account, reflecting an ongoing financial trade-off.</data>
  <data key="d4">EARNINGS CONTINUITY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">Loan balances accumulate interest at 3% annually within the fixed account, reducing the overall financial burden of borrowing. This positive accrual lowers the actual cost of the loan compared to its stated interest rate.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5">
  <data key="d3">Loan balances grow at a fixed 3% annual rate regardless of withdrawals. The timing or frequency of partial withdrawals does not affect how much interest is credited to outstanding loans.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d">
  <data key="d3">Loan balances grow at a fixed rate of 3%, independent of withdrawal fees. The availability of free early withdrawals does not affect how borrowed amounts accumulate interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 describes how borrowed funds grow at a fixed rate of 3% annually. Fact sentence 2 specifies that any partial withdrawal must be at least $500. These are independent operational rules without mutual influence.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009">
  <data key="d3">Loan balances grow at 3% annually within the fixed account, contributing to overall account value. This increased value may allow larger partial withdrawals, subject to the deduction of any applicable surrender charge.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">Loan balances accumulate interest at 3%, but any unpaid amount reduces the total death benefit when claimed, meaning earned returns do not offset the reduction in benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES REDUCTION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225">
  <data key="d3">Loan balances grow at 3% annually in the fixed account, contributing to future repayment obligations. This does not affect the death benefit until claims settle, unlike withdrawals, which directly decrease it.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="1d4b712e-5e26-4cf9-a7ad-301c683e58e3">
  <data key="d3">Loan proceeds earn a fixed return of 3%, unaffected by index-based caps. Thus, the cap rate does not influence the interest earned on outstanding loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77">
  <data key="d3">Loan proceeds earn a fixed 3% return in the fixed account, unrelated to the Floor Rate's role in capping downside risk in indexed accounts. They serve separate functions within the product design.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955">
  <data key="d3">Loan funds accruing at 3% in the fixed account have no bearing on the Participation Rate used in index-linked calculations, which determine gains based on external indices rather than internal rates.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3">
  <data key="d3">Loan proceeds earn a fixed return of 3% regardless of index performance, which contrasts with the Point-to-Point Method that ties returns to market indices over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e">
  <data key="d3">The presence of surrender charges in the first 12 years contextualizes why taking loans might carry additional effective costs, especially if the policy is surrendered soon after borrowing. Loan activity could compound total losses when combined with surrender fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890">
  <data key="d3">Loan earnings at 3% offset some of the 4% loan cost, contributing to an effective net expense of 1%; however, this does not affect the 9% surrender charge applied in Year 2 when terminating the policy prematurely.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_COST</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018">
  <data key="d3">Loan financing incurs a net annual cost due to the difference between the 4% repayment rate and the 3% earnings on the fixed account, while the 10% surrender charge in Year 1 represents an additional penalty for exiting the policy early, contributing to overall policy expense burden.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332">
  <data key="d3">The fixed earnings rate on loans (3%) interacts with the Year 4 surrender charge (7%), influencing overall policyholder cost when accessing funds early. This helps frame long-term financial trade-offs involving liquidity and penalties.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_SUPPORT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b">
  <data key="d3">Loan earnings at 3% offset part of the 4% loan interest, creating an effective net cost of 1%; this interacts with surrender charges like the 8% in Year 3 when evaluating early withdrawal impacts.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633">
  <data key="d3">The fixed earnings on loans (3%) contrast with the 4% loan interest rate, contributing to an effective cost of 1%; this economic dynamic interacts with long-term policy expenses like the Year 5 surrender charge of 6%, influencing decisions around early withdrawals or lapses.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="84b84dec-45b7-4ca8-ae2f-a68466866f24">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains the effective cost of borrowing due to the difference between the loan interest rate (4%) and the return on the fixed account (3%), leading to a net cost of 1%. This detail contextualizes why surrender charges like those in Year 6 matter when evaluating long-term financing decisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75">
  <data key="d3">Loan interest rates affect net policyholder returns, while surrender charges impact early termination costs; together, they inform total ownership expenses. The 3% return on borrowed funds contrasts with the 3% surrender charge in Year 8, illustrating different layers of financial implications.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00">
  <data key="d3">Loan earnings at 3% affect overall policy economics, while the Year 9 surrender charge of 2% reflects declining penalties over time, influencing long-term holding decisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFORMS_TIMELINE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca">
  <data key="d3">Loan financing incurs a net annual cost due to the difference between the 4% repayment rate and the 3% earned in the fixed account. While the surrender charge in Year 7 is 4%, it does not directly affect the loan’s internal economics but may influence whether a policyholder chooses to liquidate the policy before maturity.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">The 1% surrender charge in Year 10 reduces the financial risk associated with accessing funds, potentially enabling policyholders to manage loan costs more effectively when considering surrenders or withdrawals.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSISTENT_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans reduce the cash surrender value, meaning that borrowing against the policy impacts its eventual liquidation value, even though the loan earns interest at a lower rate than the fixed account.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">The 3% fixed account return on borrowed funds contributes to the effective cost of financing, while the reduced 0.5% surrender charge in Year 11 reflects declining penalties over time, potentially influencing when borrowers might repay loans or surrender policies.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">Loan costs impact account value accumulation, which may influence whether surrender charges become material when exiting the policy. In Year 12 or later, since surrender charges vanish, any remaining loan balance has less consequence on final settlement.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">The fixed-rate earnings on loans described in fact_sentence_1 contribute to the total cost burden when considering surrender charges, which depend on premiums paid. Together, these factors influence long-term policy value retention.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b">
  <data key="d3">Loan proceeds earn a 3% fixed return, enabling continued growth despite borrowing. Free partial withdrawals post-Year 1 allow fund access without penalties, offering flexibility complementary to loan usage.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="9d636a77-9852-432c-b8fb-7593d751a2da">
  <data key="d3">Loan usage earns a return on the borrowed amount via the fixed account, whereas free partial withdrawals allow access to funds without repayment, capped at 10% of the account value annually. Both provide liquidity but operate differently regarding costs and impact on future benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">Loan earnings at 3% do not affect the 3.5% load applied to premium payments. The load is a front-end charge on contributions, while loan returns accrue later based on internal account allocations.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">While loan proceeds earn a 3% annual return in the fixed account, these gains are subject to reduction by monthly COI deductions, meaning the effective benefit depends on whether earnings exceed ongoing insurance costs.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPENSATED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="6bfb8452-bcec-4db6-b212-fd25bdcfbc79">
  <data key="d3">Loan activity, where funds earn 3% in the fixed account, could offset some impact of ongoing expenses like the $12 monthly charge, especially if the loan balance grows faster than costs accumulate. However, the charge itself remains unaffected by loan performance.</data>
  <data key="d4">MINOR_INFLUENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d3">Loan usage reduces account value over time, making it harder to meet minimum thresholds needed to skip premium payments without risking policy lapse, though earned interest mitigates this effect slightly.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db">
  <data key="d3">Loan earnings at 3% occur independently of the 5% floor protection, meaning borrowers still gain interest even if the underlying index falls below the protected level.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299">
  <data key="d3">Loan earnings at 3% in the fixed account partially offset the 4% loan interest, creating a net cost; however, without any floor protection, negative returns on investments increase repayment risks over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPOSES_TO_LOSS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.68</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7">
  <data key="d3">Loan proceeds earn a consistent 3% return in the fixed account, irrespective of whether the index falls by 5% and triggers zero interest credits. This illustrates that loan gains operate outside the variable-indexed account’s performance rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="70667dae-ff8c-4bac-bf04-03807ddb6bd7">
  <data key="d3">Loan proceeds earning a fixed 3% rate support long-term value retention, which indirectly supports the principle that losses from market swings do not affect the insured's principal balance.</data>
  <data key="d4">REINFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="9ac0c7c4-1321-469b-afaa-abe6d54dbd8e">
  <data key="d3">The fixed-rate loan mechanism described in fact_sentence_1 operates independently of the insurer’s identity mentioned in fact_sentence_2. No causal or contextual link exists between the two statements beyond shared document origin.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="03e4f2e0-8fd5-4268-b333-707b317fcbd9">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 describes internal policy financial mechanisms involving loan costs and returns, while fact_sentence_2 offers external contact information for the insurer. There is no interaction between these two pieces of information beyond shared contextual origin.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="7c78ce63-cb1f-4b61-bdcd-88d0ce4bcb53">
  <data key="d3">The statement about earned interest on borrowed funds relates to internal policy finance rules, while the mention of Chicago, Illinois, indicates the document’s place of execution. These elements exist independently without mutual impact.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22" target="ba1c52cb-9fba-4846-9a66-8e0c71e2a754">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a seal on the document confirms its official nature but has no bearing on the loan interest calculations or account earnings detailed in fact_sentence_1.</data>
