<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906">
  <data key="d3">The 1% net annual cost of policy loans stems from the difference between the 4% loan interest and 3% earnings in the fixed account, independent of the $500,000 death benefit specified in Option 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 1% net annual cost for policy loans influences decisions about leveraging the policy's cash value, especially when considering Option 1’s fixed death benefit, since each dollar borrowed reduces the ultimate beneficiary payment proportionally.</data>
  <data key="d4">AFFECTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="f48d18db-916a-4e9a-ad5c-8b176c59da3c">
  <data key="d3">The net annual cost of borrowing via a policy loan is 1%, calculated as the difference between the 4% loan interest and 3% fixed account returns. This figure stands independent of the ongoing charges tied to Option 1’s fee structure.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678">
  <data key="d3">The annual net cost of a policy loan is 1%, derived from the difference between the 4% loan interest and 3% earnings in the fixed account. This does not affect how the death benefit is computed under Option 2.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="99ca8905-b57d-4689-9164-12678eda198b">
  <data key="d3">The net annual cost of a policy loan is 1%, calculated as the difference between the 4% loan interest and the 3% return in the fixed account. This figure does not influence or depend on the comparative ongoing charges between death benefit options.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6">
  <data key="d3">The net annual cost of a policy loan is 1%, which affects overall policy economics. While this does not alter the mechanism of benefit increase under Option 2, it influences whether borrowers might prefer higher-growth options like Option 2 despite added debt burden.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76">
  <data key="d3">The annual net cost of 1% on policy loans exists regardless of whether a policyholder switches death benefit options, making it an independent financial feature.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25">
  <data key="d3">The net annual cost of a policy loan is determined independently of the notice period needed to modify death benefit options, reflecting separate financial and administrative rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501">
  <data key="d3">The 1% annual net cost of policy loans reflects the difference between the 4% loan interest and 3% earnings on the fixed account, regardless of requirements like evidence of insurability needed to increase coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647">
  <data key="d3">A 1% annual net cost arises due to the difference between the 4% loan interest and 3% fixed account returns. This cost only applies once loans are permitted, which requires the policy to have been active for at least one year.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">The net annual cost of 1% arises specifically due to the terms governing the maximum allowable loan—being capped at 90% of surrender value—and reflects the economic trade-off when using that credit facility.</data>
  <data key="d4">DERIVES_FROM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">A net annual borrowing cost of 1% implies that despite a 4% interest charge on loans, the policyholder benefits from a 3% return in the fixed account, lowering the actual financial burden.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">The net annual cost of 1% arises because the loan earns 3% interest in the fixed account while being subject to a 4% charge, creating an offsetting effect that defines the true economic cost.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9">
  <data key="d3">The net cost of borrowing via policy loans is 1% per year, reflecting the difference between interest earned in the fixed account and the loan interest rate. This financial detail stands independently from the minimum withdrawal threshold.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d">
  <data key="d3">Policy loans incur a net annual cost of 1%, but this does not affect the fee structure for partial withdrawals, which remain free for the first ten instances regardless of outstanding loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5">
  <data key="d3">The net cost of borrowing via a policy loan is unrelated to the fee imposed on partial withdrawals after the tenth instance. They represent distinct transaction types with separate financial implications.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009">
  <data key="d3">The net cost of borrowing via a policy loan is determined by the difference between the loan interest rate and returns earned in the fixed account. This figure is unrelated to the limits imposed on partial withdrawals, which depend instead on account value and surrender charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225">
  <data key="d3">Policy loans incur a net annual cost of 1%, but do not directly alter the death benefit unless unpaid. In contrast, partial withdrawals under Option 1 immediately reduce the death benefit by the withdrawal amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">The 1% annual net cost of borrowing reflects the true expense of using a policy loan, which results in a direct reduction of the death benefit when unpaid, linking financing costs to diminished payouts.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="1d4b712e-5e26-4cf9-a7ad-301c683e58e3">
  <data key="d3">A higher cap rate could enhance the value of funds allocated to index accounts, potentially reducing reliance on policy loans. In contrast, the consistent 1% net loan cost remains unaffected by changes in cap rates, offering predictable borrowing expenses irrespective of index performance.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77">
  <data key="d3">While the net cost of borrowing is determined independently by loan rates and internal crediting mechanics, the presence of a 0% Floor Rate ensures that even poor market performance won’t erode the basis used to calculate future earnings relevant to loan repayment capacity.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955">
  <data key="d3">The net cost of borrowing (1%) affects cash flow and policy sustainability, whereas the Participation Rate governs how market gains are allocated to the account. They impact different aspects of policy performance without direct interaction.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3">
  <data key="d3">While the net cost of borrowing is set at 1%, this figure does not influence or rely on the Point-to-Point Method’s calculation logic, which governs return attribution independently.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="db06e7c6-2f5b-4dca-9e5a-d5dd96d2c405">
  <data key="d3">A policy loan incurs a net annual cost of 1%, which is lower than the 3.0% return offered by the Fixed Account, implying strategic use of loans to access higher-yielding assets may be financially advantageous.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES_RETURN</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="f64306b3-60d7-48b6-82c2-6580397642e1">
  <data key="d3">The 1% net cost of policy loans reflects an interest expense tied to accessing cash value, which operates independently of the 0% floor on the indexed account—but borrowers should consider whether such leverage aligns with their exposure to volatile markets protected only by the floor.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="326a19f6-3d06-4cde-a9f0-0b1923801873">
  <data key="d3">The net 1% annual cost of policy loans does not influence the 8.5% cap on the Global Diversified Index Account, as these features operate independently—one governs debt financing costs, the other investment return ceilings.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="e56d9b1f-113b-4961-abbd-159d8047aeca">
  <data key="d3">The net cost of policy loans being 1% annually is unrelated to the 100% participation rate in the indexed account, as it stems from separate components of the contract’s financing structure.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="c4dbdf51-a4cd-4a65-8903-f269d529eefd">
  <data key="d3">The low net cost of policy loans complements the fixed account’s guaranteed returns, allowing users to leverage the account’s stability for affordable borrowing.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7">
  <data key="d3">The 1% net cost of policy loans does not influence the 25% minimum participation rate required for index credits, as these mechanisms serve distinct functions in investment and financing respectively.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1">
  <data key="d3">The 1% net cost of policy loans arises from a 4% loan interest rate offset by 3% earned in the fixed account, reflecting a funding mechanism unrelated to the 4% minimum cap on indexed credits. This cost does not affect or depend on the cap level.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e">
  <data key="d3">The net cost of borrowing reflects an ongoing expense tied to policy usage, while surrender charges represent a penalty for early termination. Both factors influence total policy cost but operate independently—one related to active use (loans), the other to discontinuation (surrender).</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018">
  <data key="d3">The net cost of borrowing reflects ongoing financing expenses tied to policy loans, while the Year 1 surrender charge represents an upfront penalty for terminating the policy early. Both affect overall policy economics but operate independently—one related to debt usage, the other to withdrawal timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_COSTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890">
  <data key="d3">The net cost of borrowing reflects ongoing financing expenses tied to policy loans, while the Year 2 surrender charge represents an exit penalty. Both affect overall policy economics but operate independently—one pertains to sustained use of borrowed funds, the other to premature cancellation.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b">
  <data key="d3">The net cost of borrowing reflects ongoing financing expenses tied to policy loans, while the Year 3 surrender charge represents an exit penalty. Both contribute to overall policyholder costs but operate independently—one related to sustained use of borrowed funds, the other to premature cancellation.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELEVANCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="84b84dec-45b7-4ca8-ae2f-a68466866f24">
  <data key="d3">The net cost of borrowing reflects ongoing financing terms, while the Year 6 surrender charge represents an exit penalty; together, they inform total policyholder expenses over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332">
  <data key="d3">The net cost of borrowing (1%) reflects an ongoing expense tied to policy loans, while the Year 4 surrender charge (7%) represents a front-end penalty for early termination. Both contribute to total policy-related costs but operate independently—one applies when taking out a loan, the other when surrendering the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633">
  <data key="d3">The net cost of borrowing reflects an ongoing expense tied to policy loans, while the Year 5 surrender charge represents a one-time penalty for early termination. Both contribute to total policy-related costs but operate independently—one applies when taking out a loan, the other when surrendering the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca">
  <data key="d3">The net cost of borrowing reflects an ongoing expense tied to policy loans, while the Year 7 surrender charge represents a penalty for terminating the policy early. Both contribute to overall policy expenses but operate independently—one related to debt financing, the other to contract cancellation.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00">
  <data key="d3">The net cost of borrowing (1%) reflects ongoing financing terms, while the Year 9 surrender charge (2%) represents a penalty for early termination. Both contribute to total policy-related costs over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75">
  <data key="d3">The net cost of borrowing (1%) reflects an internal financing mechanism unaffected by surrender charges, though both factors influence total policy expenses over time. The Year 8 surrender charge of 3% adds another layer of cost consideration when evaluating early termination versus holding into later years.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">The low surrender charge in Year 11 reduces the penalty risk associated with accessing funds early, supporting sustained utilization of policy loans without significant loss, thereby reinforcing the feasibility of maintaining the 1% net borrowing cost over extended periods.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">The net cost of borrowing (1%) reflects an ongoing expense tied to policy loans, while the Year 10 surrender charge (1%) represents a one-time penalty for early termination. Both contribute to total policyholder costs but operate independently—one recurring, the other periodic.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">The absence of surrender charges from Year 12 onward makes it financially feasible to maintain policy loans longer, supporting the sustained viability of the 1% net borrowing cost over extended periods.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">The net cost of borrowing through a policy loan (1%) reflects an internal financing calculation unrelated to surrender charges, which depend on premium payments over time. These two elements operate independently within the policy’s financial framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">The net cost of borrowing relies on the deduction of loans from the account value when calculating cash surrender value, making it dependent on the formula defined in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b">
  <data key="d3">The net cost of policy loans being 1% annually complements the availability of free partial withdrawals after Year 1, as both enhance policyholder liquidity without immediate penalties.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="9d636a77-9852-432c-b8fb-7593d751a2da">
  <data key="d3">The net cost of borrowing via a policy loan is 1%, which reflects an expense tied to accessing funds. This contrasts with the ability to take free partial withdrawals up to 10% of the account value annually without repayment obligation, offering alternative access to funds without accruing debt.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">The 1% net cost of borrowing reflects the effective interest rate on policy loans, which depends on internal crediting rates and does not alter the 3.5% load applied per premium payment, though it influences total policy cost over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">While the net cost of borrowing is determined externally based on loan rates and investment returns, it may influence decisions about maintaining sufficient account value to avoid excessive COI deductions due to reduced reserves.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="6bfb8452-bcec-4db6-b212-fd25bdcfbc79">
  <data key="d3">The net 1% annual cost of borrowing reflects the effective interest expense when utilizing policy loans, which operates independently of the flat $12 monthly administrative fee that applies regardless of loan use.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_COST</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d3">Low net borrowing costs enable sustainable use of policy loans, supporting account value maintenance needed to avoid mandatory premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES_FINANCIAL_STABILITY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db">
  <data key="d3">A low net borrowing cost enables strategic use of policy loans, which complements the safety provided by floor protection by allowing flexible fund access without triggering losses due to market volatility.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb" target="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299">
  <data key="d3">A 1% net cost of borrowing makes policy loans highly advantageous, partially offsetting the risk posed by having no floor protection, thus enhancing overall policy resilience.</data>
  <data key="d4">OFFSETTING_RISK</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
