<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906">
  <data key="d3">Fact Sentence 2 sets the minimum allowable amount for partial withdrawals. While withdrawals affect the death benefit under Option 1, this rule itself has no bearing on the base $500,000 death benefit level.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 sets the minimum amount allowed for partial withdrawals. This rule applies regardless of whether the death benefit is level or increasing, making it unrelated to the specific feature described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="f48d18db-916a-4e9a-ad5c-8b176c59da3c">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that partial withdrawals begin at $500 sets a baseline for accessing funds, but it does not influence or relate to the comparative fee levels of Option 1 versus other options.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678">
  <data key="d3">A minimum partial withdrawal of $500 applies regardless of how the death benefit is calculated under Option 2, including when it consists of the specified amount plus account value.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="99ca8905-b57d-4689-9164-12678eda198b">
  <data key="d3">The minimum partial withdrawal amount of $500 sets a procedural limit on cash access, independent of the fee structure associated with either death benefit option.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that partial withdrawals be at least $500 applies regardless of how the death benefit changes over time under Option 2.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 outlines the minimum withdrawal requirement of $500. Fact sentence 1 explains the process for changing death benefit options. Neither action depends on the other, as they govern unrelated transaction types.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 defines the smallest allowable partial withdrawal amount, unrelated to changes in death benefit options. Fact sentence 1 mandates prior notice for such modifications, but does not affect withdrawal rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 defines the smallest allowable amount that can be withdrawn from the policy’s account value without penalty. This rule applies independently of whether additional insurance coverage is being requested, which requires separate documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647">
  <data key="d3">A minimum withdrawal of $500 applies independently of whether policy loans have become available after one year. The timing of loan eligibility does not affect withdrawal limits.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 sets the minimum withdrawal size at $500, separate from fact sentence 1, which governs the cap on policy loans. The two rules operate independently without affecting each other’s conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that partial withdrawals begin at $500 sets a baseline for cash access but has no bearing on the fixed 4% interest charged on policy loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 establishes a minimum withdrawal limit of $500. Fact sentence 1 explains that outstanding loans accumulate interest at 3% per year. The existence of a withdrawal floor does not affect loan interest calculations, and vice versa.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">A minimum partial withdrawal amount of $500 applies when accessing funds early, but this requirement does not affect the calculation or impact of the 1% net cost associated with policy loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009">
  <data key="d3">The minimum withdrawal is set at $500, ensuring small but meaningful access to funds. The maximum allowable withdrawal depends on the current account value adjusted for any applicable surrender charge, capping how much can be withdrawn without triggering penalties.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSTRAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d">
  <data key="d3">The requirement of a $500 minimum withdrawal enables access to fee-free partial withdrawals, making it possible for policyholders to withdraw funds without penalty when meeting the threshold.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5">
  <data key="d3">The requirement of a $500 minimum ensures withdrawals occur meaningfully, enabling the application of subsequent rules like the $50 fee after the tenth withdrawal.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">The minimum withdrawal amount of $500 sets a baseline for accessing funds, though it does not influence how loans impact the death benefit. This rule applies regardless of any existing loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that partial withdrawals must be at least $500 sets the baseline for when the reduction mechanism applies. This ensures only meaningful withdrawals trigger changes to the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">The minimum partial withdrawal amount of $500 sets a floor for cash access, which could affect long-term funding dynamics, potentially influencing whether sufficient reserves remain to cover recurring 3.5% loads on future premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">A minimum partial withdrawal of $500 affects how policyholders manage their account balances, influencing whether sufficient funds remain after COI deductions to support future withdrawals without depleting reserves.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES_ACCOUNT_VALUE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="6bfb8452-bcec-4db6-b212-fd25bdcfbc79">
  <data key="d3">While the $500 minimum partial withdrawal rule governs access to funds, the $12 monthly administrative charge impacts the total account balance that could be withdrawn, influencing long-term withdrawal strategy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES_ACCOUNT_VALUE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d3">The $500 minimum withdrawal requirement depends on having adequate account value to avoid violating conditions needed to skip premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for a minimum $500 partial withdrawal has no bearing on the 5% index decline floor protection, as it concerns fund accessibility rather than performance safeguards.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299">
  <data key="d3">Setting the minimum partial withdrawal at $500 implies users need sufficient account balance to meet this threshold, which becomes increasingly challenging given the lack of floor protection—any decline below zero would eliminate buffer capacity entirely.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPOSES VULNERABILITY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.68</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7">
  <data key="d3">The $500 minimum partial withdrawal limit has no impact on the condition that zero interest is credited when the index falls by 5%; the two rules serve distinct purposes—one controls cash-out flexibility, the other protects capital during losses.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="70667dae-ff8c-4bac-bf04-03807ddb6bd7">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a $500 minimum partial withdrawal threshold implies that policyholders have accessible liquidity only when sufficient funds remain, which is made possible because market losses do not affect principal—a key feature enabling predictable withdrawal availability over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="03e4f2e0-8fd5-4268-b333-707b317fcbd9">
  <data key="d3">The minimum partial withdrawal amount of $500 relates to policyholder actions within the insurance product, while the provided phone number serves as a generic point of contact for customer inquiries unrelated to withdrawal mechanics.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
