<edge source="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009" target="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906">
  <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals cannot exceed the account value less surrender charges, so the ability to access funds affects how much equity remains tied to the original $500,000 death benefit. As withdrawals reduce the account value, they may lower the actual payout unless offset by other factors like investment performance.</data>
  <data key="d4">LIMITED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009" target="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199">
  <data key="d3">The presence of a surrender charge reduces the effective account value available for withdrawal, meaning that even though Option 1 has a stable death benefit, actual withdrawable amounts depend on penalty adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009" target="f48d18db-916a-4e9a-ad5c-8b176c59da3c">
  <data key="d3">The cap on partial withdrawals—account value minus surrender charge—is constrained by structural costs such as surrender charges, which aligns with the higher relative expense profile of alternative options, making Option 1's lower ongoing charges particularly advantageous.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODULATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.68</data>
</edge>
<edge source="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009" target="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678">
  <data key="d3">The maximum partial withdrawal is constrained by the account value after accounting for surrender charges, which ties back to the calculation basis used in determining the death benefit under Option 2.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009" target="99ca8905-b57d-4689-9164-12678eda198b">
  <data key="d3">The limit on partial withdrawals—account value minus surrender charge—is influenced by the overall cost structure of the option, including higher ongoing charges in Option 2, which erode account value more quickly and thus indirectly restrict withdrawal capacity.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009" target="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6">
  <data key="d3">The cap on partial withdrawals reflects the current account value’s growth, which is central to how Option 2's death benefit expands over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009" target="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76">
  <data key="d3">The availability of larger partial withdrawals, limited by account value and surrender charges, influences the flexibility of choosing different death benefit options, especially when considering long-term financial planning.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009" target="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25">
  <data key="d3">The maximum allowable partial withdrawal is limited by the account value less any applicable surrender charge. This restriction operates independently of the need for advance notice when switching death benefit options.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009" target="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501">
  <data key="d3">The maximum partial withdrawal is limited by the account value less any applicable surrender charge, meaning that high surrender charges might restrict withdrawable amounts. This restriction has no direct bearing on whether evidence of insurability is needed to increase coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009" target="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647">
  <data key="d3">The cap on partial withdrawals reflects the balance between account value and surrender charges, limiting how much can be taken without triggering additional costs. This restriction operates independently of loan availability, though both features relate to withdrawing accumulated value over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 indicates that partial withdrawals depend on the account value less surrender charges, setting an upper bound on accessible funds. This contrasts with fact sentence 1, where the maximum loan is tied solely to 90% of surrender value, independent of other deductions.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">The cap on partial withdrawals—based on account value less surrender charges—is unaffected by the 4% loan interest rate. This limitation governs access to funds regardless of borrowing costs.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">The maximum partial withdrawal is constrained by the account value less the surrender charge. Since loan earnings increase the account value over time, they indirectly support higher possible withdrawals, including those involving funded loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES POTENTIAL</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">The maximum allowable partial withdrawal depends on the current account value less any applicable surrender charge. This cap has no bearing on the net annual cost of using a policy loan, which remains fixed at 1%.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009" target="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9">
  <data key="d3">The maximum withdrawal is constrained by the account value less the surrender charge, meaning it cannot exceed what remains after accounting for early termination costs. This cap ensures that even large withdrawals respect policy terms tied to surrender fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">DETERMINES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009" target="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d">
  <data key="d3">The maximum partial withdrawal is determined by subtracting the surrender charge from the account value, regardless of whether fees apply. This rule stands independently of the number or frequency of withdrawals.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009" target="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5">
  <data key="d3">The maximum allowable partial withdrawal is determined by subtracting the surrender charge from the account value. After the tenth withdrawal, a $50 fee applies regardless of the amount withdrawn.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009" target="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225">
  <data key="d3">The maximum withdrawable amount is constrained by the account value less any applicable surrender charge, which limits how large a withdrawal can be made. This capped amount directly reduces the death benefit when withdrawn under Option 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_LIMITS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">The maximum partial withdrawal is constrained by the account value and surrender charge, influencing cash availability, but does not directly impact the death benefit reduction caused by outstanding loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ee6e471a-ab68-4fbc-ada5-7d93519deee3" target="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">determines_maximum_withdrawal_limit</data>
</edge>
