  <data key="d3">Free partial withdrawals for the first ten transactions occur independently of the 4% fixed interest charged on policy loans, meaning one feature has no bearing on the other.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">Free partial withdrawals (up to ten) have no associated costs, but this has no bearing on whether outstanding loans earn interest at 3%.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">The absence of fees on the first ten partial withdrawals has no bearing on the net cost of borrowing via policy loans, which remains consistently at 1% per year.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d" target="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9">
  <data key="d3">Fee-free status applies only to withdrawals that meet or exceed the $500 minimum, ensuring that smaller amounts do not qualify for the exemption.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d" target="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009">
  <data key="d3">The absence of fees for the first ten partial withdrawals applies uniformly across all eligible withdrawals, irrespective of how much is withdrawn relative to the account value and surrender charge.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d" target="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5">
  <data key="d3">The first ten partial withdrawals are exempt from fees, establishing a threshold before additional costs apply. After exceeding this limit, each withdrawal triggers a $50 charge.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d" target="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225">
  <data key="d3">The first ten partial withdrawals being fee-free means policyholders can access funds without additional costs early on, though each withdrawal still reduces the death benefit under Option 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">While the first ten partial withdrawals are free, any outstanding policy loans still reduce the death benefit paid out when a claim is made.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">Fee-free partial withdrawals allow policyholders to access cash without immediate cost, contrasting with the upfront 3.5% load on premiums, which raises entry costs. They represent separate mechanisms affecting long-term affordability differently.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals reduce the account value, which affects future COI calculations since COI is typically based on current account balances. Free withdrawals allow flexibility without immediate penalty, though COI continues to accrue monthly regardless.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d" target="6bfb8452-bcec-4db6-b212-fd25bdcfbc79">
  <data key="d3">Free partial withdrawals allow policyholders to access cash without immediate penalties, but these benefits are offset by persistent $12 monthly administrative charges that cumulatively reduce the account’s value and limit future withdrawal capacity.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUBJECT_TO_FEE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d3">Maintaining adequate account value to avoid premium shortfalls supports financial stability necessary to take advantage of free partial withdrawals without risking lapses due to insufficient balances.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_SUPPORT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d" target="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db">
  <data key="d3">Fee-free partial withdrawals offer flexible access to funds, which complements the floor protection mechanism by letting users withdraw money without additional costs—even if the underlying index falls, preserving some control over assets.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d" target="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299">
  <data key="d3">Although partial withdrawals are initially free, the absence of any floor protection exposes the underlying account value to full market volatility, possibly reducing funds available for future withdrawals.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d" target="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7">
  <data key="d3">Free partial withdrawals allow policyholders to access cash without immediate penalties, supporting long-term planning that aligns with the safety net provided by zero interest credits during significant market drops.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d" target="70667dae-ff8c-4bac-bf04-03807ddb6bd7">
  <data key="d3">Fee-free partial withdrawals allow access to funds without penalty initially, supporting liquidity needs regardless of whether market fluctuations erode principal—a concern mitigated separately by the policy's built-in protections.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d" target="9ac0c7c4-1321-469b-afaa-abe6d54dbd8e">
  <data key="d3">The fee-free partial withdrawal rule applies within policies offered by Horizon Wealth Protection Insurance, establishing a condition tied to the insurer’s product design.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d" target="dc9f1c71-4218-47d3-a2d6-f9dd0a3d8783">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines financial conditions related to policyholder withdrawals, which could potentially be accessed or managed via the company’s website mentioned in fact_sentence_2, though no explicit link exists between them.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
