  <data key="d3">The $50 fee per partial withdrawal beyond the tenth occurrence applies regardless of the option chosen, including Option 1, which still carries lower ongoing charges than alternatives.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5" target="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678">
  <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals beyond the tenth trigger a $50 fee, regardless of how the death benefit is computed under Option 2.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5" target="99ca8905-b57d-4689-9164-12678eda198b">
  <data key="d3">A $50 fee applied to partial withdrawals beyond the tenth year pertains to fund access transactions, independent of the ongoing charge levels between Option 1 and Option 2, which affect total premium allocation rather than withdrawal activity.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5" target="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6">
  <data key="d3">While partial withdrawals after the tenth year carry a $50 fee, such transactions do not affect the underlying rule that the death benefit increases alongside account value growth under Option 2.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5" target="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76">
  <data key="d3">Partial withdrawal fees depend only on how many withdrawals have been taken, not on whether the death benefit option has been changed.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5" target="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25">
  <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals exceeding ten incur a $50 fee regardless of whether a change in death benefit option was previously initiated.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5" target="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501">
  <data key="d3">A $50 fee on partial withdrawals after the tenth does not impact the need for evidence of insurability when increasing coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5" target="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647">
  <data key="d3">The imposition of a $50 fee on partial withdrawals after the tenth does not affect when policy loans become accessible. Loan eligibility depends solely on the policy's duration, not withdrawal frequency.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">The imposition of a $50 fee after the tenth partial withdrawal has no bearing on the calculation or availability of policy loans, which are determined solely by surrender value.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">The $50 fee charged per partial withdrawal after the tenth has no bearing on the 4% fixed interest rate applicable to policy loans. Each feature is governed by separate terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals exceeding ten incur a $50 fee, independent of any loan activity. Whether funds were borrowed or not has no bearing on whether such fees apply.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">A $50 fee applied to partial withdrawals after the tenth does not affect the net annual cost of policy loans, which remains independent of withdrawal frequency or timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5" target="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9">
  <data key="d3">A $50 fee applies per withdrawal after the tenth instance, contingent on prior adherence to the $500 minimum withdrawal rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5" target="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009">
  <data key="d3">A $50 fee is charged per partial withdrawal occurring after the tenth such transaction. This fee does not affect how much can be withdrawn, only the cost associated with exceeding ten withdrawals.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5" target="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d">
  <data key="d3">After the initial ten free withdrawals, every additional withdrawal incurs a $50 fee, reflecting a cumulative restriction tied to prior actions.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals exceeding ten incur a $50 fee, but this does not influence the reduction of the death benefit due to outstanding loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5" target="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225">
  <data key="d3">After the tenth partial withdrawal, a $50 fee applies. Under Option 1, each withdrawal reduces the death benefit dollar-for-dollar.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">The $50 fee on partial withdrawals after year ten reflects a separate operational charge unrelated to the 3.5% load on premium payments. While both affect account value over time, they operate independently across different stages of policy usage.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals incur fees after the tenth, reducing the account value used to pay the monthly Cost of Insurance, thereby possibly impacting long-term affordability of coverage unless premiums remain sufficient.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_AFFECTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.55</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5" target="6bfb8452-bcec-4db6-b212-fd25bdcfbc79">
  <data key="d3">The $50 fee for subsequent partial withdrawals has no bearing on the $12 monthly administrative charge, which is consistently applied regardless of withdrawal activity. These fees operate on separate mechanisms within the policy’s financial framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d3">Insufficient account value due to missed premium payments—or failure to maintain adequate reserves—could trigger reliance on partial withdrawals, which incur fees after the tenth instance, thereby compounding financial strain.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRIBUTES_TO_RISK</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5" target="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db">
  <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals incur fees after the tenth instance, impacting cash flow flexibility, while the floor protection shields gains from market drops. The two mechanisms serve distinct purposes without overlapping functionality.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5" target="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299">
  <data key="d3">A $50 fee on partial withdrawals after the tenth year increases the cost of accessing funds, compounding the risk posed by zero floor protection, potentially eroding the account faster than intended.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXACERBATES_VULNERABILITY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5" target="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7">
  <data key="d3">A $50 fee for withdrawals after the tenth occurrence has no impact on whether interest is credited when the index falls by 5%.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5" target="70667dae-ff8c-4bac-bf04-03807ddb6bd7">
  <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals after the tenth trigger a $50 fee, reducing the account balance; however, since market declines don’t affect principal, these withdrawals occur from a stable base, preserving the integrity of the guaranteed protection regardless of such transactions.</data>
  <data key="d4">NEUTRAL_SUPPORT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5" target="03e4f2e0-8fd5-4268-b333-707b317fcbd9">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines a specific fee associated with frequent partial withdrawals, while fact_sentence_2 gives general contact information for the insurer. No interaction exists between these two pieces of information.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5" target="9ac0c7c4-1321-469b-afaa-abe6d54dbd8e">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines a specific fee structure tied to policyholder actions, while fact_sentence_2 names the insurer responsible for administering those rules. The latter provides organizational context but does not influence the meaning or application of the former.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_SOURCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5" target="dc9f1c71-4218-47d3-a2d6-f9dd0a3d8783">
  <data key="d3">The $50 fee for additional partial withdrawals relates to policy terms detailed in the document, while the website address identifies the issuing company but does not affect or explain that fee structure.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
