<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans decrease the death benefit paid out upon claim, meaning the $500,000 guaranteed benefit under Option 1 may be lowered depending on loan balances.</data>
  <data key="d4">REDUCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199">
  <data key="d3">Any outstanding policy loan reduces the final death benefit payment, regardless of whether the chosen option is Level or Increasing.</data>
  <data key="d4">REDUCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="f48d18db-916a-4e9a-ad5c-8b176c59da3c">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans decrease the death benefit regardless of whether Option 1 has lower ongoing charges. This effect is separate from the cost implications of choosing Option 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans reduce the death benefit, meaning even if Option 2 calculates a higher base benefit via account value, the loan balance reduces it accordingly.</data>
  <data key="d4">REDUCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="99ca8905-b57d-4689-9164-12678eda198b">
  <data key="d3">The reduction of the death benefit due to outstanding loans does not depend on whether Option 1 or Option 2 has higher ongoing charges. This consequence arises solely from loan activity, regardless of fee levels.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans lower the final death benefit amount, potentially diminishing the advantage gained from an increasing benefit tied to account value growth.</data>
  <data key="d4">REDUCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans reduce the death benefit regardless of whether the policyholder switches death benefit options, meaning this reduction occurs independently of such changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25">
  <data key="d3">The presence of unpaid loans reduces the death benefit, independent of whether a policyholder plans to switch benefit options, which requires separate advance notice.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_EFFECT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans reduce the death benefit regardless of whether evidence of insurability was required to increase coverage. The requirement for such evidence does not alter loan impacts on payouts.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is reduced by any outstanding policy loans, but such loans only become possible once the policy has been active for one year, making timing essential for this effect.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans decrease the death benefit payable upon claim, meaning higher loan balances result in lower payouts. Since loans cannot exceed 90% of the surrender value, this sets an upper bound on how much can be borrowed and thus potentially deducted from the benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">REDUCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">The presence of outstanding policy loans reduces the death benefit, which stems from the accumulated cost of borrowing at a fixed 4% annual interest rate.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">The presence of an outstanding loan decreases the death benefit, despite the loan continuing to earn 3% interest in the fixed account, showing that accrual does not prevent benefit erosion.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES BENEFIT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans lower the death benefit because each dollar borrowed increases the liability against the policy’s cash value, thereby reducing what remains for beneficiaries—a process driven by the 1% net cost of such borrowings.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans reduce the death benefit when claimed, irrespective of whether a $500 minimum withdrawal has occurred. The presence of loans affects the payout independently of withdrawal thresholds.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans directly lower the death benefit paid out, regardless of withdrawal limits tied to account value and surrender charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans decrease the death benefit paid out upon claim, independent of any fees charged for partial withdrawals.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans reduce the death benefit when a claim is made. This effect operates separately from partial withdrawals, which also reduce the death benefit but through different financial mechanics.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY REDUCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d">
  <data key="d3">Although outstanding loans decrease the death benefit, this does not impact the fee status of initial partial withdrawals, which remain free regardless.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="1d4b712e-5e26-4cf9-a7ad-301c683e58e3">
  <data key="d3">Policy loans reduce the death benefit regardless of the cap rate applied to index account gains, meaning the credit limit has no bearing on loan-related deductions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77">
  <data key="d3">Policy loans reduce the final death benefit regardless of whether the Floor Rate protects against market declines, meaning the credit protection offered by the Floor Rate doesn’t mitigate loan-related deductions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans reduce the death benefit regardless of how interest is calculated via methods like Point-to-Point, meaning the crediting approach doesn't alter the impact of debt on payouts.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans decrease the death benefit paid out, whereas the Participation Rate affects how much of an index’s increase contributes to the account balance. Since lower account values due to loans could result in smaller participation credits over time, there is a weak indirect link where loan activity may modestly limit the base used for calculating participation-based gains.</data>
  <data key="d4">WEAKLY_DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="db06e7c6-2f5b-4dca-9e5a-d5dd96d2c405">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans decrease the death benefit, potentially reducing the amount that could have been supported by the Fixed Account’s guaranteed 3.0% yield over time, thus diminishing the effective long-term value derived from the fixed return component.</data>
  <data key="d4">REDUCES_EFFECTIVE_VALUE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.55</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="f64306b3-60d7-48b6-82c2-6580397642e1">
  <data key="d3">Policy loans reduce the death benefit, potentially impacting the total value transferred even when the indexed account maintains its 0% floor protection during market drops.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="326a19f6-3d06-4cde-a9f0-0b1923801873">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans decrease the death benefit, potentially reducing the overall value of the account where the 8.5% cap applies, though the cap itself remains unaffected by borrowing activity.</data>
  <data key="d4">NEUTRAL_INFLUENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="e56d9b1f-113b-4961-abbd-159d8047aeca">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans decrease the death benefit, even though the Global Diversified Index Account offers full participation in market gains, meaning higher account values do not fully offset loan impacts.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="c4dbdf51-a4cd-4a65-8903-f269d529eefd">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans decrease the death benefit, whereas the fixed account maintains a minimum 2% return regardless of such liabilities. This means loan effects do not alter the fixed account’s guarantee, though cumulative debt could indirectly affect total account balance over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7">
  <data key="d3">Policy loans decrease the death benefit regardless of the 25% minimum participation rate applied to index-linked gains. The presence of such loans has no bearing on the guarantee of participation rates.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans decrease the death benefit paid out on claim, reducing the ultimate payoff despite any positive credits earned from indexed accounts. Even though the indexed accounts have a 4% minimum cap guarantee, loan balances erode the total benefit, meaning investors may receive less than expected based solely on credited returns.</data>
  <data key="d4">REDUCES_OUTCOME</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans reduce the death benefit, compounding the financial impact of high early-year surrender charges like the 10% in Year 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPOUNDS_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 confirms the surrender charge level in Year 2, supporting the gradual decline pattern referenced in chunk_summary_1’s explanation of surrender charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans decrease the death benefit, while surrender charges reduce the cash surrender value when exiting early—both mechanisms impact final payouts but operate independently.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans reduce the death benefit, and while unrelated directly, the presence of surrender charges in Year 4 reflects part of the same policy’s financial framework affecting long-term value.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_SUPPORT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans reduce the death benefit, while the surrender charge in Year 3 affects the cash surrender value; these factors independently influence policy outcomes but do not directly interact.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans decrease the final death benefit, while the Year 5 surrender charge reduces the cash surrender value; together, they represent two distinct financial deductions that affect overall policy returns.</data>
  <data key="d4">RELATED_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="84b84dec-45b7-4ca8-ae2f-a68466866f24">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans reduce the death benefit, and this effect interacts with surrender charges like the 5% fee in Year 6, which further reduces the cash surrender value when exiting early.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPOUNDS_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans reduce the death benefit, and while the surrender charge in Year 7 is specified separately, it contributes to overall policy value erosion alongside loans when assessing total benefit impact.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELEVANCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans reduce the death benefit, and knowing the low surrender charge in Year 11 helps assess whether maintaining such loans remains financially viable over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans reduce the death benefit, while the surrender charge in Year 8 being 3% reflects the declining schedule outlined in the policy terms. These elements operate independently within the same framework but do not directly influence each other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans decrease the death benefit, while the surrender charge in Year 9 affects the cash surrender value; these factors independently shape the policyholder’s financial outcome upon termination or death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans reduce the death benefit, while the surrender charge in Year 10 being low (1%) reflects reduced penalties later in the policy term, indirectly supporting longer-term retention without significant penalty.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans reduce the death benefit regardless of surrender charges, but once surrender charges end in Year 12+, policyholders gain more freedom to manage those loans without additional penalties.</data>
  <data key="d4">NEUTRAL_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans decrease the death benefit, consistent with their role in reducing the cash surrender value as defined in the second statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans decrease the final death benefit, while surrender charges depend on early premium payments; together, they represent distinct ways policy value erodes before maturity or withdrawal.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans reduce the death benefit, and since free partial withdrawals after Year 1 lower the account value, they could increase reliance on loans or amplify the reduction effect over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="9d636a77-9852-432c-b8fb-7593d751a2da">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans decrease the death benefit by reducing the net amount payable, which complements the effect of partial withdrawals that also lower the payout by drawing down the account value. Together, these features illustrate ways the policy’s death benefit may be diminished over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans decrease the death benefit, making it more impactful that a 3.5% load is added to every premium payment, thereby reducing effective fund growth over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">REDUCES_EFFECTIVENESS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans lower the death benefit, which may necessitate higher COI payments later due to reduced account value, thereby intensifying the impact of ongoing monthly COI deductions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INCREASES_IMPACT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="6bfb8452-bcec-4db6-b212-fd25bdcfbc79">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans decrease the death benefit, and such debt accumulation may exacerbate the financial burden caused by ongoing administrative charges like the $12 monthly fee.</data>
  <data key="d4">INCREASES_FINANCIAL_PRESSURE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.55</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d3">High levels of unpaid loans decrease the account value, which may prevent the account from being large enough to cover monthly deductions and thus hinder the ability to skip premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">IMPACTED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db">
  <data key="d3">While the floor protection shields against market losses, any outstanding policy loans decrease the death benefit, which means the insured might receive less than expected despite the safety net.</data>
  <data key="d4">REDUCES EFFECTIVENESS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans decrease the death benefit, so having zero floor protection exacerbates financial risk because market losses cannot be offset, accelerating depletion of assets needed to cover debt obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">INCREASED_VULNERABILITY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans decrease the death benefit, potentially undermining the protection offered by the 5% buffer mechanism, especially if loan balances grow over time despite stagnant account gains.</data>
  <data key="d4">WEAKENS_PROTECTION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="70667dae-ff8c-4bac-bf04-03807ddb6bd7">
  <data key="d3">Although policy loans reduce the death benefit, this effect operates separately from market-related losses, meaning the absence of principal loss does not offset the reduction caused by borrowed funds.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="9ac0c7c4-1321-469b-afaa-abe6d54dbd8e">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans reduce the death benefit, a feature detailed in a document issued by Horizon Wealth Protection Insurance, linking the operational rule to its source entity.</data>
  <data key="d4">PROVENANCE_LINK</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
