</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans reduce the death benefit regardless of payment status, while failure to pay premiums leads to policy lapse. The former affects claims only if the policy remains active; the latter terminates coverage entirely before any claim can occur.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="e27b0a94-4088-4246-ba72-d6793b6cd04d">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans reduce the final death benefit, which may become more likely if a lapse occurs during the grace period due to non-payment, indirectly linking loan exposure to late premium scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="b080d9ad-b053-459f-8150-83b862b99de1">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans decrease the death benefit amount paid out, while capped rates ensure minimum returns but do not affect loan deductions. These elements function separately within different components of the policy’s financial structure.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="15cc61a2-a432-4cb5-8906-a25d63f7e7f6">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans decrease the death benefit if the insured dies, but if the policy lapses instead, those loans may still need repayment from the surrendered value, affecting what the policyholder receives.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans decrease the final death benefit, while the absence of losses from negative index performance provides a separate layer of financial safety against investment downturns.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a" target="af34274c-dfee-4fb4-a491-3e2e93de0364">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding policy loans reduce the death benefit, and while the fixed account’s return affects loan cost, the guaranteed minimum rate protects against downward volatility in earnings, indirectly supporting stable loan financing over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
