<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges apply in the early years of the policy, and Year 2's specific charge of 9% reflects the declining schedule beginning at 10% in Year 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges apply during the first 12 years, and the highest charge—10%—is assessed in the first year. This reflects the maximum penalty tied to early termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges apply in the first 12 years, and by Year 4, the charge is specifically set at 7%, reflecting an annual decrease from 10% down to 0%.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b">
  <data key="d3">Sentence 1 states that surrender charges apply in the first 12 years, providing context for when such fees occur. Sentence 2 gives a concrete example by specifying that the charge in Year 3 is 8%, illustrating how the general rule applies at a particular point in time.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="84b84dec-45b7-4ca8-ae2f-a68466866f24">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges apply throughout the first 12 years, and in Year 6, they are set at 5%, reflecting an annual decrease from 10% down to 0%.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 states that surrender charges apply in the first 12 years, providing context for when such fees occur. Fact_sentence_2 gives a specific example by stating the charge in Year 5 is 6%, illustrating how the general rule applies at a particular point in time.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges apply throughout the first 12 years, and in Year 8, they are set at 3%, reflecting an annual decrease from 10% down to 0%.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca">
  <data key="d3">Sentence 1 states that surrender charges apply in the first 12 years, providing context for when such fees occur. Sentence 2 gives a concrete example by specifying that the charge in Year 7 is 4%, illustrating how the general rule applies at a particular point in time.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges apply in the first 12 years, and by Year 9, the charge has decreased to 2%, consistent with an annual decline from 10% down to 0%.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges decline over time, beginning at 10% in Year 1 and reducing each year until they reach 0% by Year 12. In Year 10, the charge is specifically set at 1%, consistent with this declining pattern.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the condition under which surrender charges exist—within the first 12 years—while fact_sentence_2 gives a concrete example by specifying the charge rate at Year 11, illustrating how the general rule applies at a particular point in time.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges apply only during the initial 12-year period, and by definition, they drop to zero at the start of Year 12. Therefore, the absence of charges in Year 12 logically follows from the rule stated in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="9d636a77-9852-432c-b8fb-7593d751a2da">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges apply when a policy is terminated early, specifically within the first 12 years. This feature relates to exiting the policy prematurely rather than accessing funds incrementally.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">The applicability of surrender charges during the initial 12-year period depends on the calculation method tied to premiums paid in the first ten years. This establishes a conditional framework where the existence of charges relies on historical payment data.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">The presence of surrender charges during the first 12 years determines the amount subtracted from the account value to compute the cash surrender value. Without knowing whether surrender charges apply, the exact cash surrender value cannot be determined.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="59735a62-be54-4b86-a006-cd569871d4ef">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges relate to early termination fees when canceling the policy before year 12. This does not affect the operation or maintenance of a non-elected no-lapse guarantee rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="628900ad-3981-4384-be18-2669a41ba276">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges apply when a policy is terminated early, affecting financial outcomes upon withdrawal. This contrasts with the availability of a separate optional rider designed to prevent lapses under certain conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges apply when policies are terminated early, but exceptions exist for certain transactions like partial withdrawals. Free partial withdrawals allow access to funds without incurring surrender fees after the first year.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCEPTION_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="d4b10129-f843-43a5-8362-ff505e1fb13b">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges apply when a policy is terminated early, regardless of whether additional riders like the No Lapse Guarantee were chosen. This statement stands independently of rider selection.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges penalize early policy cancellation within 12 years, whereas the No Lapse Guarantee Rider protects against policy lapse regardless of account value. These are independent safeguards addressing distinct risks—early withdrawal costs versus long-term sustainability.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges apply if the policy is terminated early, but this condition doesn’t influence whether the insurer notifies the holder about insufficient funds for monthly deductions. The second sentence describes an administrative step prior to lapse based on account balance, independent of surrender charge rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges apply when a policy is terminated early, but they are unrelated to the grace period used to reinstate a delinquent policy. One concerns withdrawal penalties; the other concerns renewal timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="ae3f8271-673d-4549-8f9b-46011b263dfc">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges apply upon early withdrawal of funds, but do not directly affect whether a policy lapses due to missed payments. The existence of surrender charges does not influence the grace period outcome described here.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder surrenders within the first 12 years, they face surrender charges, reducing the amount returned. After a policy lapses due to non-payment, any residual surrender value—including what remains after deductions—is permanently forfeited.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="1c5eba0f-2f29-43d1-b13a-bc342d4f4ae4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 introduces surrender charges that impact liquidity and cost of exiting the policy early. This has no bearing on how interest is credited via index performance described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="1d4b712e-5e26-4cf9-a7ad-301c683e58e3">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges penalize early policy cancellation, whereas the Cap Rate restricts return rates on investments. Although both impact final gains, they function in separate domains—one related to timing of withdrawal, the other to investment performance cap.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges reflect the cost of exiting the policy early, which may affect whether a holder benefits from long-term guarantees like the Floor Rate. However, the Floor Rate does not impact the application or amount of these fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges impact the net amount received when exiting the policy, potentially reducing the benefit derived from high Participation Rates over time, especially if the policy is terminated early.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODULATED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges affect the net payout upon early policy cancellation, potentially reducing the benefit derived from any interest credited via the point-to-point method, especially in early years.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="e6aa2762-a82e-4371-9d8e-da19a25dd6d1">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges during the initial 12 years create a disincentive to exit the policy prematurely, potentially impacting the decision to utilize the S&amp;P 500 Index Account over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="492399d4-a4a8-470a-b04c-a4e38ca316d2">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges impact the liquidity and timing of fund access, regardless of the S&amp;P 500's capped returns. The presence of a cap does not alter the charge schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="faf66c9e-da0e-4813-9561-2d1480419596">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges that persist for the first 12 years create a disincentive for early exit, which may affect policyholders' decisions regarding long-term use of the 100% participation benefit tied to the S&amp;P 500 account.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="a4c6faf8-57d8-4d84-affb-d94570b3ae60">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges in the first 12 years could discourage early exit, potentially making the guaranteed 0% floor more valuable over time, though the two features operate independently.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="a0671d34-e31b-4b17-8ed5-6a9d495c5148">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges applied within the first 12 years may reduce the net benefit derived from the S&amp;P 500 Index Account's credited returns, especially if the policyholder exits before realizing full compounding effects under the 1-year crediting cycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="62714aed-4640-40fa-9927-1e7eaaddb24c">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges affect the liquidity and net benefit of holding any index account—including the NASDAQ-100—for fewer than 12 years, impacting returns tied to those indices.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="4144da65-9775-496c-b601-6cbcd31e5849">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges impact when a policyholder may exit the contract without penalty, whereas the cap determines maximum return potential on the NASDAQ-100 Index Account. Together, they shape risk-return trade-offs but do not directly affect each other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="32909f74-b806-4169-8ab1-602ea158ef9f">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges that apply within the first 12 years could reduce the effective gain from the 100% participation rate in the NASDAQ-100 Index Account if the policy is terminated early.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_AFFECTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="bce094ed-5c85-40d1-800b-e0894835715b">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges impact the net amount received upon policy cancellation, potentially reducing the benefit even when the account has positive value despite the 0% floor on index gains.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="b0213eb9-bcd3-41f0-9381-ae8e81ac0f24">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges lasting up to 12 years create an incentive to hold the policy beyond the initial crediting periods, potentially impacting whether gains from the 1-year credit cycle are retained.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSIDERED_IN</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="de64be79-d83e-496d-97f6-5d2e80705c21">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges during the initial 12 years do not influence which index accounts are available, such as the Global Diversified Index Account.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="13cdba53-929e-487b-9dac-c7e31bdd92a0">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges over 12 years may deter early withdrawal, potentially influencing a policyholder’s decision to stay invested even when capped returns limit upside in the Global Diversified Index Account.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="22fdc352-4139-456b-bd73-2207bfdefc4e">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges reduce the net payout upon early exit, potentially diminishing returns even when the account has strong growth potential via a 100% participation rate.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="a5cf74c6-3010-4b87-83b5-452662af8369">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges influence when and how policyholders may withdraw money without penalty, whereas the 0% floor safeguards account value from losses. Though related to overall policy economics, they do not directly affect each other’s functionality.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges during the initial 12 years create a disincentive to terminate the policy early, reinforcing the importance of consistent premium payments—including those meeting the $100 minimum—to maintain long-term benefits without penalty.</data>
  <data key="d4">REINFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges discourage early withdrawal, reinforcing the importance of consistent premium payments like the $100 minimum required to keep the policy active.</data>
  <data key="d4">REINFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2">
  <data key="d3">High annual premiums approaching the $50,000 limit significantly increase the base upon which surrender charges are calculated, affecting potential losses at surrender.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="0d35c1ce-d96d-4562-80f8-0654abe126d2">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges reduce the net return upon early cancellation, making high-premium strategies less attractive unless long-term retention is planned, thus indirectly shaping adherence to the $50,000 tax-aligned cap.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSTRAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">Early surrender within 12 years incurs fees based on prior premiums paid, making it financially disadvantageous to terminate a policy unless sufficient funds have been contributed under the recommended premium schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges diminish the return on invested premiums, making the upfront 3.5% load more impactful over shorter holding periods due to reduced effective accumulation.</data>
  <data key="d4">AMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges affect the net amount received at policy cancellation, potentially reducing funds available to cover future COI expenses if the policy is terminated prematurely.</data>
  <data key="d4">AFFECTED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="6bfb8452-bcec-4db6-b212-fd25bdcfbc79">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges reduce the net payout upon early termination, potentially making it less financially viable to exit the policy despite paying consistent administrative fees like the $12 monthly charge.</data>
  <data key="d4">FINANCIAL_INFLUENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="0b7e0a06-5166-489d-a873-3b798f915e2c">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges diminish the cash surrender value, meaning less money remains after deducting them—even though total monthly charges already reduce the account balance incrementally.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="1b6d4d68-07ed-4c80-987c-ddf958d36f08">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges depend on the timing of withdrawal and reduce the cash surrender value, potentially offsetting gains accumulated despite consistent monthly charge deductions described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges apply for the first 12 years, meaning any action like switching death benefit options—even with proper notice—could result in financial loss if done too soon, especially near the beginning of the term.</data>
  <data key="d4">TEMPORAL_CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges impact the surrender value, which determines the upper limit of allowable policy loans, thus influencing the applicability and magnitude of the 90% loan rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges during the first 12 years influence the net value accessible via withdrawal or surrender, potentially impacting whether taking out a 4% interest loan remains financially viable before the charge schedule expires.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges during the first 12 years affect the overall economic outcome of holding a policy, which includes the long-term cost of maintaining loans that earn only 3% despite being charged 4%.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges impact the liquidity and final payout when exiting the policy early, whereas the net cost of borrowing relates to financing needs during ownership. Though distinct, both affect the economic viability of holding the policy beyond short terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges apply over the first 12 years and lower the cash surrender value, indirectly influencing outcomes related to loans and death benefits, though they do not alter the mechanism by which loans reduce the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="9ac0c7c4-1321-469b-afaa-abe6d54dbd8e">
  <data key="d3">The presence of surrender charges described in fact_sentence_1 applies within policies issued by Horizon Wealth Protection Insurance, establishing that these fees are part of the company's product offerings.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="7c78ce63-cb1f-4b61-bdcd-88d0ce4bcb53">
  <data key="d3">The existence of surrender charges described in fact_sentence_1 does not depend on or relate to the geographical origin stated in fact_sentence_2. The latter only indicates where the document was signed, which has no bearing on the policy's financial rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="79f032d3-1299-41de-85c7-f944c1411556">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge rule applies throughout the initial 12-year term regardless of when the document was issued. This factual statement about policy fees stands independently of the document’s publication date.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e" target="ba1c52cb-9fba-4846-9a66-8e0c71e2a754">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a seal on the document suggests formal authentication, which could imply that the policy details—including surrender charge rules—are officially recorded. However, the seal itself has no bearing on the application or computation of those fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
