<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">The 10% surrender charge in Year 1 reduces the surrender value, thereby lowering the upper bound of the 90% loan limit derived from that value.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES_LIMIT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">The 10% surrender charge in Year 1 impacts decisions about policy cancellation, indirectly affecting the attractiveness of taking a loan at 4%, as high surrender fees may discourage liquidation even if low-cost loans are available.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">The 10% surrender charge in Year 1 reflects a significant early exit cost, which interacts with the loan mechanism described in fact_sentence_1 where borrowing leads to a net 1% annual cost, compounding total financial impact when combining withdrawal and loan strategies.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">The 10% surrender charge in Year 1 impacts the effective value returned upon policy cancellation, whereas the 1% net loan cost affects those who borrow against the policy’s value. These two figures represent distinct financial mechanisms influencing long-term policy outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_COSTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">The 10% surrender charge in Year 1 reflects an early penalty that, combined with existing loans, reduces the net amount available to beneficiaries, amplifying the reduction caused by outstanding loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPOUNDS_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="9ac0c7c4-1321-469b-afaa-abe6d54dbd8e">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge detail applies within policies offered by Horizon Wealth Protection Insurance, linking the financial term to its originating institution.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_LINK</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="7c78ce63-cb1f-4b61-bdcd-88d0ce4bcb53">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge detail in Year 1 is unrelated to the document’s place of execution in Chicago, Illinois. No contextual link connects the financial term to the geographical origin of the document.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="79f032d3-1299-41de-85c7-f944c1411556">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge rate described in fact_sentence_1 is part of the policy terms that could be referenced in a document dated October 3, 2024, but the date itself has no bearing on the charge amount.</data>
