<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e">
  <data key="d3">The 9% surrender charge in Year 2 exemplifies the broader rule that charges decline annually over the first 12 years, starting from 10%.</data>
  <data key="d4">PART_OF_SEQUENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge drops from 10% in Year 1 to 9% in Year 2, reflecting the scheduled annual reduction outlined in the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b">
  <data key="d3">Year 2's surrender charge of 9% logically precedes and sets the stage for Year 3’s reduced rate of 8%, reflecting an ongoing annual reduction schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633">
  <data key="d3">Year 2's surrender charge of 9% occurs before Year 5’s 6%, reflecting the gradual annual decrease described in the chunk summary. This progression shows how surrender charges diminish predictably over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332">
  <data key="d3">Year 2 has a surrender charge of 9%, which is higher than the 7% charge in Year 4, reflecting the gradual reduction in fees over time as stated in the chunk summary.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75">
  <data key="d3">Year 2 has a higher surrender charge than Year 8, reflecting the declining nature of charges over time as stated in the chunk summary.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES AND DECREASES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="84b84dec-45b7-4ca8-ae2f-a68466866f24">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states the surrender charge in Year 2 is 9%, setting an early point in the declining schedule. Fact sentence 2 continues this trend by specifying that by Year 6, the charge has decreased further to 5%, illustrating the annual reduction over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states the surrender charge in Year 2 is 9%, which aligns with the initial high rate that decreases each subsequent year. Fact sentence 2 shows the charge has reduced to 4% by Year 7, reflecting the ongoing downward trend established in the earlier year.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES AND DECREASES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">Year 2's surrender charge of 9% sets an early point in the declining sequence that continues through subsequent years, culminating in a minimal 0.5% charge by Year 11.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">Year 2 has a surrender charge of 9%, reflecting an early stage in the declining schedule. By Year 10, the charge reduces further to 1%, demonstrating the ongoing downward trend established earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00">
  <data key="d3">Year 2 has a surrender charge of 9%, reflecting the initial phase of the declining schedule. By Year 9, the charge has decreased further to 2%, illustrating the ongoing reduction trend within the 12-year window.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 2 being 9% aligns with the rule that charges decline annually based on premiums paid within the first ten years. This reflects the mechanism by which the charge is determined.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 2 is set at 9%, which is applied when calculating the cash surrender value. This specific rate serves as an input into the formula that determines the final cash surrender value.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRIBUTES_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">Year 2 has a surrender charge of 9%, reflecting an ongoing reduction from the initial 10% rate. By Year 12, the cumulative decrease brings the charge down to 0%, completing the scheduled phase-out.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="9d636a77-9852-432c-b8fb-7593d751a2da">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 2 being 9% reflects the declining fee schedule applied when terminating the policy early. This does not affect the ability to take annual partial withdrawals, which remain independent of surrender charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="628900ad-3981-4384-be18-2669a41ba276">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 2 is specified at 9%, reflecting the declining schedule outlined in the policy terms. This detail stands independently of whether riders like the no-lapse guarantee are offered.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge being 9% in Year 2 reflects the declining schedule within the first decade, while the ability to take free partial withdrawals after Year 1 ensures policyholders can access funds without triggering these charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSISTENT WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 2 is specified at 9%, reflecting the declining scale over the initial 12-year period. This detail is unrelated to the non-elected No Lapse Guarantee Rider, whose protective benefit does not activate under current conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 2 reflects penalty rates applied if the policy is terminated early, while the second statement describes a warning system triggered by inadequate account balances that could lead to lapse. These are independent operational conditions affecting policy outcomes differently.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="d4b10129-f843-43a5-8362-ff505e1fb13b">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 2 is set at 9%, reflecting the scheduled reduction from the initial 10% rate. This detail stands independently of whether the No Lapse Guarantee Rider was chosen.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 2 is set at 9%, reflecting the declining schedule. After a policy lapses due to non-payment, any residual surrender value is lost entirely.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="ae3f8271-673d-4549-8f9b-46011b263dfc">
  <data key="d3">Year 2 surrender charge reflects the declining penalty schedule applied when withdrawing funds early. This does not directly influence whether a policy lapses due to missed payments beyond the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="59735a62-be54-4b86-a006-cd569871d4ef">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 2 is part of the declining fee schedule applied within the first 12 years. This detail is unrelated to the No Lapse Guarantee Rider, which was not selected and thus has no operational effect on current policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">NOT RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 2 being 9% reflects the declining penalty schedule applied when canceling the policy early. This detail does not influence or depend on the 61-day grace period allowed for reinstating a lapsed policy due to non-payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="1c5eba0f-2f29-43d1-b13a-bc342d4f4ae4">
  <data key="d3">The Year 2 surrender charge impacts the net amount received upon policy termination, potentially reducing returns that could otherwise benefit from index-linked gains described in the Index Account definition.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="1d4b712e-5e26-4cf9-a7ad-301c683e58e3">
  <data key="d3">A higher cap could increase long-term account value, potentially reducing the relative impact of surrender charges over time. However, the Cap Rate does not influence the fixed 9% surrender charge in Year 2, which remains unchanged regardless of index performance.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77">
  <data key="d3">A 9% surrender charge in Year 2 reflects a cost associated with exiting the policy early, which may influence decisions about whether to rely on the Floor Rate's protection over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges affect the net amount received upon withdrawal, whereas the Participation Rate influences how much returns are credited based on index performance. Though related to overall policy value, these elements do not directly influence or depend on each other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
