  <data key="d3">The 8% surrender charge in Year 3 affects the total payout upon withdrawal, possibly reducing the effective return despite consistent deduction of smaller fees like the $12 monthly charge.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_COST</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="0b7e0a06-5166-489d-a873-3b798f915e2c">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges in Year 3 impact the final payout if the policyholder terminates the contract, reducing the effective return on accumulated funds that were already subject to monthly charges such as COI and administration fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES_ACCOUNT_VALUE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="1b6d4d68-07ed-4c80-987c-ddf958d36f08">
  <data key="d3">A high surrender charge in Year 3 may discourage early withdrawal despite consistent monthly deductions reducing the account balance gradually over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 identifies a concrete surrender charge amount in Year 3, which supports understanding the financial implications referenced when switching death benefit options under the 60-day rule outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSISTENT_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">The 8% surrender charge in Year 3 reduces the surrender value, thereby lowering the upper limit of the 90% loan amount that can be taken against it.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">The 8% surrender charge in Year 3 impacts the effective value of funds withdrawn or surrendered, whereas the 4% loan interest rate affects borrowers’ out-of-pocket expenses. Both elements shape the economic viability of holding versus accessing policy benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_FACTOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">The 8% surrender charge in Year 3 influences decisions about taking loans or withdrawing funds, especially considering that such actions may trigger higher out-of-pocket costs due to the net 1% loan expense.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">The Year 3 surrender charge affects the amount received upon withdrawal or surrender, whereas the 1% net loan cost impacts long-term borrowing efficiency. Though distinct, both influence total policy economics and should be considered together when evaluating financial trade-offs.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELEVANCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">The Year 3 surrender charge influences the cash surrender value, which may affect loan availability and repayment capacity, indirectly shaping the impact of outstanding loans on the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
