<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e">
  <data key="d3">The 7% surrender charge in Year 4 exemplifies the broader rule that surrender charges decline annually over the initial 12-year period.</data>
  <data key="d4">PART_OF_SEQUENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge drops from 10% in Year 1 to 7% in Year 4, demonstrating a consistent downward trend over time as part of the defined fee structure.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 4 is lower than in Year 2, aligning with the declining schedule that starts at 10% and reduces each year until it reaches zero by Year 12.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b">
  <data key="d3">The 8% surrender charge in Year 3 precedes and sets the context for the subsequent drop to 7% in Year 4, demonstrating the progressive nature of the fee reduction plan.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="84b84dec-45b7-4ca8-ae2f-a68466866f24">
  <data key="d3">Year 4 has a higher surrender charge than Year 6, reflecting the gradual reduction in charges over time as specified in the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES AND DECREASES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca">
  <data key="d3">Year 4's surrender charge of 7% precedes and logically leads into Year 7’s reduced rate of 4%, reflecting the annual decline pattern described in the summary.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633">
  <data key="d3">Year 4's surrender charge of 7% sets the stage for the subsequent reduction to 6% in Year 5, reflecting the scheduled annual decline in fees throughout the initial 12-year period.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00">
  <data key="d3">Year 4 has a higher surrender charge (7%) than Year 9 (2%), reflecting the gradual annual decrease in charges over the first 12 years.</data>
  <data key="d4">DECREASES TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">Year 4's surrender charge of 7% fits the expected downward trend from the initial 10% rate, suggesting it precedes later reductions like the 1% charge in Year 10.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states the surrender charge in Year 4 is 7%, which aligns with the declining trend established by the chunk summary. Fact sentence 2 follows this by stating the lower charge in Year 8, continuing that same downward progression.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES AND DECREASES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 4 being 7% is used in calculating the cash surrender value by subtracting it from the account value along with any outstanding loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">USED_IN_CALCULATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">Year 4 has a surrender charge of 7%, reflecting an intermediate stage in the declining schedule before it reaches 0% in Year 12. This demonstrates the gradual reduction pattern outlined in the summary.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 4 being 7% aligns with the annual decrease pattern described in the summary, where charges start at 10% and decline each year. Since the calculation depends on premiums paid within the first ten years, this specific rate fits the established method.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">Year 4’s surrender charge of 7% fits into a declining annual trend that continues through Year 11, where it further reduces to 0.5%. This illustrates progression toward zero by the end of the 12-year window.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="628900ad-3981-4384-be18-2669a41ba276">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 4 is specified at 7%, reflecting the declining schedule over the initial 12-year period. This detail does not relate to the availability of the no-lapse guarantee rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="9d636a77-9852-432c-b8fb-7593d751a2da">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 4 being 7% reflects the annual reduction in penalties applied when terminating the policy early. This does not affect the ability to make tax-free partial withdrawals, which remain independent of surrender charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 4 is set at 7%, reflecting the declining annual scale applied during the initial policy term. This specific charge level has no bearing on the eligibility or cost of partial withdrawals permitted after Year 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="d4b10129-f843-43a5-8362-ff505e1fb13b">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 4 is set at 7%, reflecting the declining schedule over the first 12 years. This detail stands independently of whether the No Lapse Guarantee Rider was chosen.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 4 is part of the standard penalty schedule based on premium payments, unrelated to any optional riders. The absence of an active No Lapse Guarantee Rider means the policy remains vulnerable to lapse if premiums are not sustained.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="ae3f8271-673d-4549-8f9b-46011b263dfc">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 4 indicates ongoing financial penalties if the policyholder terminates coverage early, but it does not affect whether the policy lapses due to missed payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 4 reflects penalty rates applied when withdrawing funds early, while the notice about insufficient account value pertains to impending policy lapse due to non-payment. These events occur under different conditions and involve separate triggers.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="59735a62-be54-4b86-a006-cd569871d4ef">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 4 depends on the policy’s surrender charge schedule, independent of any riders. Since the No Lapse Guarantee Rider was not elected, its terms do not affect the calculation or application of surrender charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">NOT APPLICABLE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 4 reflects penalty rates applied when withdrawing funds early, while the 61-day grace period allows policyholders extra time to pay overdue premiums without lapsing coverage. These are independent features related to financial penalties and renewal flexibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 4 reduces the potential surrender value, meaning less money would remain upon withdrawal. If the policy later lapses, any residual surrender value—including what's left after deducting the charge—is forfeited.</data>
  <data key="d4">AFFECTS VALUE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
