<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="1c5eba0f-2f29-43d1-b13a-bc342d4f4ae4">
  <data key="d3">A 7% surrender charge in Year 4 could impact the net benefit derived from an index account’s performance, especially if the policyholder exits before realizing full gains.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="1d4b712e-5e26-4cf9-a7ad-301c683e58e3">
  <data key="d3">While the surrender charge in Year 4 is set at 7%, this fee operates independently of the Cap Rate’s impact on account growth, meaning high-indexed returns cannot offset the penalty when withdrawing early.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77">
  <data key="d3">A 7% surrender charge in Year 4 reflects a penalty for early termination, unrelated to the 0% Floor Rate, which protects against market downturns in crediting rates.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955">
  <data key="d3">The Year 4 surrender charge affects the net payout upon withdrawal, whereas the Participation Rate influences how much of the index’s gain increases the account balance. Neither directly impacts nor depends on the other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges in Year 4 are part of the penalty structure for early withdrawal, unrelated to how interest is calculated via the Point-to-Point Method, though both influence overall policy value over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
