  <data key="d3">A 7% surrender charge in Year 4 reduces the net proceeds when withdrawing funds, potentially diminishing the benefits gained from investing in the S&amp;P 500 Index Account under the point-to-point method.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODERATED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="492399d4-a4a8-470a-b04c-a4e38ca316d2">
  <data key="d3">The Year 4 surrender charge impacts liquidity and withdrawal decisions, whereas the S&amp;P 500 cap sets return ceilings. No causal or conditional link exists between them.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
