  <data key="d3">A 7% surrender charge in Year 4 impacts the net benefit of accessing funds, regardless of whether the Global Diversified Index Account’s 8.5% cap has been reached. This penalty may discourage early access even if high returns were possible.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="22fdc352-4139-456b-bd73-2207bfdefc4e">
  <data key="d3">A 7% surrender charge in Year 4 may reduce effective returns even when the 100% participation rate delivers strong index-linked growth, potentially diminishing investor benefit if withdrawn early.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332" target="a5cf74c6-3010-4b87-83b5-452662af8369">
  <data key="d3">A 7% surrender charge in Year 4 reflects a contractual penalty for early withdrawal, whereas the 0% floor ensures that even under poor market conditions, the account balance won’t drop below its prior level. Together, they represent complementary protections: one limits downside risk in growth, the other incentivizes long-term retention.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
