  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 5 reflects a penalty for terminating the policy early, which may influence decisions about when to access funds. This contrasts with the Cap Rate, which restricts how much interest can be earned, affecting long-term accumulation rather than liquidity timing.</data>
