  <data key="d3">A 6% surrender charge in Year 5 impacts the cost of exiting the policy early, whereas the 8.5% cap restricts gains on the Global Diversified Index Account. Although both factors shape overall policy value, they function in separate domains: one relates to access timing, the other to return ceilings.</data>
