  <data key="d4">IS_INFLUENCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">A 6% surrender charge in Year 5 underscores the importance of meeting the $6,000 annual premium recommendation to ensure continued coverage beyond this point without premature termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">The 6% surrender charge in Year 5 reflects a penalty for early withdrawal, which may reduce net returns despite consistent application of the 3.5% premium load.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">A 6% surrender charge in Year 5 reduces the effective payout if the policyholder surrenders the contract, potentially offsetting gains lost due to cumulative COI deductions made throughout the policy's term.</data>
  <data key="d4">REDUCES_NET_PAYOUT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633" target="6bfb8452-bcec-4db6-b212-fd25bdcfbc79">
  <data key="d3">A 6% surrender charge in Year 5 may reduce the net proceeds upon withdrawal, making ongoing fees like the $12 monthly admin charge more impactful on long-term value retention.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633" target="0b7e0a06-5166-489d-a873-3b798f915e2c">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges in Year 5 reflect a penalty applied at policy termination, which depends on accumulated premiums and may impact the effective cost of maintaining coverage—this ties back to long-term expense considerations that also involve consistent monthly charges such as those mentioned in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633" target="1b6d4d68-07ed-4c80-987c-ddf958d36f08">
  <data key="d3">A 6% surrender charge in Year 5 reflects long-term penalty structures that may affect overall account balance, influencing the impact of ongoing monthly deductions described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633" target="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25">
  <data key="d3">The Year 5 surrender charge of 6% reinforces the importance of planning ahead when modifying death benefit options, especially given the need for 60 days’ notice before any change.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFORMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">The 6% surrender charge in Year 5 reduces the surrender value, thereby lowering the upper bound of the 90% loan limit derived from that value.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES_LIMIT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">The 6% surrender charge in Year 5 contextualizes the long-term cost implications of accessing funds, which interacts with the 4% loan interest rate as part of broader policy expense considerations.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">The Year 5 surrender charge of 6% reflects the declining penalty schedule over time, which contextualizes why borrowers may face higher total costs when combining loan usage with early termination, especially given the 3% fixed account returns on loaned amounts.</data>
  <data key="d4">RELATED_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">The Year 5 surrender charge affects the amount received upon policy cancellation, whereas the 1% net loan cost impacts borrowers who use policy loans. Though distinct in mechanism, both influence the effective cost of holding or accessing policy value over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">The Year 5 surrender charge affects the cash surrender value, whereas outstanding loans directly lower the death benefit—both mechanisms impact policy value differently but contribute to reduced financial gains for the policyholder.</data>
  <data key="d4">RELATED_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633" target="7c78ce63-cb1f-4b61-bdcd-88d0ce4bcb53">
