<edge source="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca" target="492399d4-a4a8-470a-b04c-a4e38ca316d2">
  <data key="d3">A 4% surrender charge in Year 7 reflects the penalty for exiting the policy early, whereas the 10.5% cap on the S&amp;P 500 Index Account defines the upper limit of annual gains. Though both relate to financial outcomes under the policy, they function in separate domains: one impacts access to funds, the other influences earnings potential.</data>
