  <data key="d3">A 4% surrender charge in Year 7 reflects a penalty for early withdrawal, whereas the 0% floor ensures that index-linked gains cannot go below zero. These elements serve distinct purposes—one governs exit fees, the other safeguards downside exposure.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca" target="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176">
  <data key="d3">A 4% surrender charge in Year 7 implies that policies with lower-than-recommended premiums may still incur fees upon cancellation, underscoring why meeting the $100 minimum payment threshold matters for long-term financial planning.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca" target="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa">
  <data key="d3">A higher initial investment due to meeting the $100 minimum helps build account value over time, reducing the risk of losing significant equity upon surrender—even though the 4% charge in Year 7 remains fixed regardless of individual payment size.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_FACTOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca" target="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2">
  <data key="d3">The 4% surrender charge in Year 7 reflects a penalty for early termination based on prior premium payments, which could influence whether a policyholder chooses to invest up to the $50,000 annual limit.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca" target="0d35c1ce-d96d-4562-80f8-0654abe126d2">
  <data key="d3">The 4% surrender charge in Year 7 depends on prior premium payments, which are capped at $50,000 annually—a key factor determining the financial impact of exiting the policy early.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">A 4% surrender charge in Year 7 underscores the importance of sustaining regular premiums, such as the recommended $6,000 per year, to prevent policy lapse and associated financial penalties.</data>
  <data key="d4">REINFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">The 4% surrender charge in Year 7 reflects a penalty tied to early termination, which interacts with the cumulative effect of the 3.5% premium load—both reducing net gains and influencing whether surrendering the policy is financially viable.</data>
  <data key="d4">IMPACTED_BY_LOAD</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
