  <data key="d3">A 4% surrender charge in Year 7 reduces the cash surrender value, indirectly impacting how much remains after accounting for prior COI deductions that have already reduced the account balance.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca" target="6bfb8452-bcec-4db6-b212-fd25bdcfbc79">
  <data key="d3">A 4% surrender charge in Year 7 reflects a significant exit penalty that could affect long-term planning, though it does not directly impact the fixed $12 monthly administrative fee.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_COST</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca" target="0b7e0a06-5166-489d-a873-3b798f915e2c">
  <data key="d3">A higher surrender charge in Year 7 may reflect accumulated costs such as initial loads and monthly fees that have already been deducted from the account value, meaning prior charges impact the effective surrender outcome.</data>
