<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e">
  <data key="d3">The 2% surrender charge in Year 9 exemplifies the broader rule that surrender charges decrease annually over the initial 12-year period.</data>
  <data key="d4">PART_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018">
  <data key="d3">A surrender charge of 2% in Year 9 implies that earlier years had higher charges, such as the 10% rate in Year 1, demonstrating a progressive reduction over time within the 12-year window.</data>
  <data key="d4">INCREASED FROM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 9 is 2%, which follows from the gradual annual drop beginning at 10% in Year 1. Since Year 2 had a charge of 9%, it marks an earlier stage in the same downward trajectory.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b">
  <data key="d3">The 2% surrender charge in Year 9 logically follows from the earlier 8% charge in Year 3, reflecting an ongoing annual decrease in surrender fees across the initial term.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge decreases each year, so the lower charge in Year 9 (2%) logically follows from the higher charge in Year 4 (7%).</data>
  <data key="d4">INCREASES FROM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633">
  <data key="d3">Year 9’s lower surrender charge compared to Year 5 illustrates the ongoing reduction pattern established early in the policy lifecycle, where charges diminish steadily each year.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="84b84dec-45b7-4ca8-ae2f-a68466866f24">
  <data key="d3">Since the surrender charge decreases every year, the lower rate in Year 9 logically follows from the higher rate observed in Year 6, maintaining continuity in the fee structure.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca">
  <data key="d3">Year 9's lower surrender charge (2%) follows logically from the declining trend established in Year 7 (4%), demonstrating a sequential drop in fees over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75">
  <data key="d3">Year 9’s reduced surrender charge of 2% builds upon the prior year’s higher charge of 3%, demonstrating an ongoing downward trend per the plan.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">Year 9's surrender charge of 2% precedes and sets context for the lower charge in Year 11, illustrating the ongoing decline in fees across the initial term.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">Year 9 has a remaining surrender charge of 2%, reflecting its position before the final reduction to zero at Year 12. This indicates progression toward full elimination of charges by the end of the 12-year window.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">The 2% surrender charge in Year 9 is determined by applying the annual percentage rule to the total premiums paid within the initial ten-year window, consistent with the stated calculation basis.</data>
  <data key="d4">DERIVED_FROM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">Year 9's surrender charge of 2% logically precedes and leads into Year 10’s lower charge of 1%, reflecting the annual decline in surrender fees over time within the policy term.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 9 being 2% is used as an input when calculating the cash surrender value. This specific rate affects the final value derived by subtracting it from the account value along with any outstanding loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">INPUT_DEPENDENCY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="9d636a77-9852-432c-b8fb-7593d751a2da">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 9 being 2% reflects the annual reduction in fees applied when terminating the policy early. This detail is independent of the ability to make periodic partial withdrawals without penalty.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="628900ad-3981-4384-be18-2669a41ba276">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 9 is specified at 2%, reflecting the declining schedule outlined in the summary. This detail stands independently of any information about optional riders like the no-lapse guarantee.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 9 being 2% reflects the declining penalty schedule, but it does not impact the ability to take free partial withdrawals after Year 1, which remain unrestricted by surrender charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 9 is part of the standard policy terms related to early termination fees. However, since the No Lapse Guarantee Rider was not elected, it has no impact on current surrender charges or policy continuation under normal conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="59735a62-be54-4b86-a006-cd569871d4ef">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 9 is specified at 2%, reflecting the declining schedule over the initial 12-year period. This detail is unrelated to the No Lapse Guarantee Rider since the rider was not selected and thus cannot influence any aspect of the policy’s current state.</data>
  <data key="d4">NOT APPLICABLE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872">
  <data key="d3">Year 9's 2% surrender charge reflects an annual reduction in penalties for early withdrawal, unrelated to ongoing premium coverage or lapses due to low account value.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="d4b10129-f843-43a5-8362-ff505e1fb13b">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 9 is determined by the declining schedule set for the first 12 years, independent of rider selection.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 9 being 2% reflects the gradual reduction schedule applied during the initial policy term. This detail does not influence nor relate directly to the length of the grace period offered upon missed payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a">
  <data key="d3">A surrender charge of 2% in Year 9 reduces the account value available upon withdrawal or surrender. This reduction increases the likelihood that the remaining surrender value may be zero or negative if the policy lapses without sufficient funds.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="ae3f8271-673d-4549-8f9b-46011b263dfc">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 9 being 2% reflects the annual reduction schedule applied before full elimination at Year 12. This detail pertains to withdrawal costs, while the second sentence discusses consequences of missed payments beyond the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="1c5eba0f-2f29-43d1-b13a-bc342d4f4ae4">
  <data key="d3">A higher potential return from an Index Account may offset the impact of the Year 9 surrender charge, making it more favorable to hold the policy longer despite the fee.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="1d4b712e-5e26-4cf9-a7ad-301c683e58e3">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 9 reflects a contractual penalty for withdrawing funds before maturity, which operates independently of the Cap Rate’s role in limiting return growth on index accounts.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77">
  <data key="d3">A 2% surrender charge applies in Year 9, reflecting the penalty for withdrawing funds before maturity. While unrelated to the Floor Rate's function, this fee impacts liquidity planning and could prompt policyholders to consider guaranteed minimum returns when evaluating long-term strategy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955">
  <data key="d3">A 2% surrender charge in Year 9 indicates a cost associated with accessing funds, whereas the Participation Rate dictates how index-linked returns are allocated to the account. Neither directly influences nor depends on the other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3">
  <data key="d3">A surrender charge in Year 9 indicates potential costs associated with exiting the policy, whereas the Point-to-Point Method governs how returns are computed annually. No causal or complementary link exists between them.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="e6aa2762-a82e-4371-9d8e-da19a25dd6d1">
  <data key="d3">A 2% surrender charge in Year 9 may discourage early withdrawal, potentially influencing whether policyholders benefit fully from the S&amp;P 500 Index Account’s compounded gains over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">IMPACTED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="492399d4-a4a8-470a-b04c-a4e38ca316d2">
  <data key="d3">The Year 9 surrender charge reflects a contractual fee for exiting the policy early, whereas the S&amp;P 500 cap governs upside potential based on index performance. No functional overlap exists between these two provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="faf66c9e-da0e-4813-9561-2d1480419596">
  <data key="d3">A 2% surrender charge in Year 9 affects the net benefit when withdrawing funds, potentially reducing gains that could otherwise result from the 100% participation rate on the S&amp;P 500 Index Account.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELEVANCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="a4c6faf8-57d8-4d84-affb-d94570b3ae60">
  <data key="d3">A 2% surrender charge in Year 9 reflects the cost of exiting the policy early, irrespective of index performance. Even with a 0% floor safeguarding against market downturns, policyholders still face fees if they withdraw funds before maturity.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="a0671d34-e31b-4b17-8ed5-6a9d495c5148">
  <data key="d3">A 2% surrender charge in Year 9 reflects ongoing fees tied to policy duration, whereas the one-year crediting period determines how gains accumulate annually via the index. These elements jointly shape net benefits depending on whether the holder exits before or after full crediting periods.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="62714aed-4640-40fa-9927-1e7eaaddb24c">
  <data key="d3">A 2% surrender charge applies in Year 9, separate from the mechanics of index accounts such as the NASDAQ-100's point-to-point calculation. This fee impacts liquidity but does not affect how index gains are computed.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="4144da65-9775-496c-b601-6cbcd31e5849">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge applicable in Year 9 reflects a contractual cost associated with exiting the policy, whereas the NASDAQ-100 cap defines the upper limit on gains linked to that index. Neither directly influences nor depends on the other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="32909f74-b806-4169-8ab1-602ea158ef9f">
  <data key="d3">A 2% surrender charge in Year 9 may discourage premature withdrawal despite favorable participation rates, such as the 100% rate on the NASDAQ-100 account, potentially affecting strategy alignment.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="bce094ed-5c85-40d1-800b-e0894835715b">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges in Year 9 reduce the net payout upon early termination, potentially affecting how much benefit accrues from positive index performance, such as that enabled by the 0% floor on the NASDAQ-100 Index.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="b0213eb9-bcd3-41f0-9381-ae8e81ac0f24">
  <data key="d3">The Year 9 surrender charge of 2% occurs during the policy's lifecycle when the NASDAQ-100 Index Account is still active under its annual crediting mechanism, though there is no direct impact on how credits are applied.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="de64be79-d83e-496d-97f6-5d2e80705c21">
  <data key="d3">The Year 9 surrender charge applies regardless of which index account (including the Global Diversified Index Account) holds the policy’s assets, impacting liquidity choices related to those investments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="13cdba53-929e-487b-9dac-c7e31bdd92a0">
  <data key="d3">A 2% surrender charge applies in Year 9 regardless of the index account’s performance cap, meaning even strong returns capped at 8.5% may still incur exit fees when withdrawing early.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="22fdc352-4139-456b-bd73-2207bfdefc4e">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 9 (2%) applies regardless of the participation rate, so even though the Global Diversified Index Account offers 100% participation, withdrawing funds would still incur a fee based on premium history.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="a5cf74c6-3010-4b87-83b5-452662af8369">
  <data key="d3">A 2% surrender charge applies in Year 9 regardless of the index account’s performance, including its 0% floor. This fee impacts liquidity but does not affect the floor mechanism protecting against losses.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176">
  <data key="d3">A $100 minimum premium enables sustained policy ownership through Year 9, ensuring eligibility for surrender charges only if the policyholder chooses to withdraw early rather than let it mature.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa">
  <data key="d3">A 2% surrender charge in Year 9 implies that withdrawing funds before maturity may incur costs, reinforcing the importance of meeting minimum premium payments to build adequate account value despite such penalties.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2">
  <data key="d3">A 2% surrender charge in Year 9 reflects the ongoing penalty for terminating the policy early, regardless of whether the full $50,000 premium was paid. It operates independently of the premium amount limits, focusing instead on contract duration and payout timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="0d35c1ce-d96d-4562-80f8-0654abe126d2">
  <data key="d3">A 2% surrender charge in Year 9 reflects ongoing fees affecting policy liquidity, which could impact whether contributors stay within the $50,000 tax-advantaged limit.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_DEPENDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">A 2% surrender charge in Year 9 underscores why meeting the $6,000 annual recommendation is crucial—to minimize erosion of accumulated value upon early termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">REINFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">The 2% surrender charge in Year 9 reflects a penalty tied to accumulated premiums, making it more costly to terminate the policy late in its term; however, since the 3.5% load already diminishes the effective premium contribution, the impact of the surrender charge is partially influenced by prior deductions.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODERATED_BY_LOAD</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">A 2% surrender charge in Year 9 impacts the final payout if the policyholder exits early, especially considering ongoing COI deductions have already lowered the account value over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="6bfb8452-bcec-4db6-b212-fd25bdcfbc79">
  <data key="d3">A 2% surrender charge in Year 9 may impact the effective return on contributions, indirectly influencing whether higher payments (like those suggested at $6,000/year) justify long-term retention despite ongoing fees such as the $12 monthly charge.</data>
  <data key="d4">FINANCIAL_IMPACT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="0b7e0a06-5166-489d-a873-3b798f915e2c">
  <data key="d3">A surrender charge in Year 9 impacts the final payout if the policyholder terminates it at that stage, meaning any accumulated funds less the surrender charge may reflect prior reductions due to monthly charges such as COI and administration fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODULATED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="1b6d4d68-07ed-4c80-987c-ddf958d36f08">
  <data key="d3">The Year 9 surrender charge impacts decisions about withdrawing funds, potentially discouraging early access, whereas periodic monthly deductions continuously erode the account balance regardless of withdrawal intent.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_AFFECTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25">
  <data key="d3">The Year 9 surrender charge of 2% reflects the ongoing decline in penalties throughout the policy’s early years, consistent with the conditions enabling changes like switching death benefit options, which require prior notification.</data>
  <data key="d4">RELATED_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">A 2% surrender charge in Year 9 affects the net surrender value, thereby influencing the upper limit of possible policy loans, since loans cannot exceed 90% of the adjusted surrender value.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES_LIMIT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">The Year 9 surrender charge of 2% indicates an advanced stage in the policy’s early term where penalties have significantly reduced, making it more favorable to access funds. This contrasts with the ongoing 4% loan interest cost, which remains constant regardless of timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">The Year 9 surrender charge of 2% fits into the broader timeline of diminishing fees, which impacts when borrowers might repay loans without significant penalty, especially considering loan interest accrual.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUALIZES_COST</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">The Year 9 surrender charge (2%) impacts the effective return on investment, indirectly influencing the overall cost-effectiveness of taking out a loan, especially if the policy is surrendered before maturity.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">The Year 9 surrender charge of 2% influences the cash surrender value, which may affect whether loans are repaid or remain outstanding, thereby indirectly impacting the death benefit reduction due to unpaid loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="9ac0c7c4-1321-469b-afaa-abe6d54dbd8e">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge detail in Year 9 is part of a policy governed by Horizon Wealth Protection Insurance, whose authority and authenticity are affirmed through documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">SOURCE_OF_POLICY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
