<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 identifies the surrender charge in Year 11 as 0.5%, which exemplifies the broader principle outlined in fact_sentence_1 that such charges apply throughout the initial 12-year period and decrease over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">IS_PART_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018">
  <data key="d3">The low surrender charge of 0.5% in Year 11 implies it resulted from a consistent annual reduction beginning at 10% in Year 1, demonstrating a progressive decline over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">INCREASED_FROM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890">
  <data key="d3">The low surrender charge of 0.5% in Year 11 indicates the final stage of a gradual reduction process initiated earlier, such as the 9% charge observed in Year 2.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b">
  <data key="d3">The 0.5% surrender charge in Year 11 reflects the final stages of the diminishing charge schedule, showing how the rate has decreased progressively from earlier years like Year 3.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332">
  <data key="d3">The 0.5% surrender charge in Year 11 follows logically from earlier reductions, such as the 7% charge in Year 4, showing an ongoing downward trajectory in fees over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633">
  <data key="d3">Year 11’s lower surrender charge of 0.5% follows logically from the gradual reduction described in the chunk summary, making it consistent with the downward trend initiated in Year 5.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="84b84dec-45b7-4ca8-ae2f-a68466866f24">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 reports a surrender charge of 0.5% in Year 11, part of the annual decrease leading toward zero. This follows logically from fact sentence 1’s higher charge in Year 6, illustrating the progressive nature of the fee schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 reports a surrender charge of 0.5% in Year 11, reflecting the final stages of the diminishing charge schedule. This follows logically from fact sentence 1’s higher charge in Year 7, illustrating how charges progressively reduce across the initial 12-year period.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75">
  <data key="d3">Year 11’s surrender charge of 0.5% follows logically from Year 8’s 3%, reflecting an ongoing annual decrease consistent with the stated schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00">
  <data key="d3">The reduced surrender charge of 0.5% in Year 11 follows logically from the earlier 2% charge in Year 9, reflecting the scheduled annual decrease toward zero by Year 12.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">A lower surrender charge in Year 11 compared to Year 10 demonstrates the gradual decline in fees as the policy ages beyond its initial years.</data>
  <data key="d4">INCREASES FROM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge decreases to zero in Year 12, continuing the annual decline described in Year 11’s 0.5% rate.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 11 being 0.5% is determined by applying the annual reduction formula based on premiums paid within the initial ten-year window, consistent with the general calculation principle stated.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 11 is specified at 0.5%, which is used as an input when calculating the cash surrender value. This specific charge value enables accurate computation of the final payout upon surrender.</data>
  <data key="d4">USED_IN_CALCULATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="9d636a77-9852-432c-b8fb-7593d751a2da">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 11 is low at 0.5%, reflecting its gradual decline over time. This minimal fee has no impact on the ability to take an annual 10% partial withdrawal, which remains unaffected by surrender charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="628900ad-3981-4384-be18-2669a41ba276">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 11 being 0.5% reflects the annual decline in fees over time, while the mention of the no-lapse guarantee rider highlights an optional feature unrelated to surrender charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 11 is very low at 0.5%, reflecting its gradual decline toward zero by Year 12. This minimal charge aligns with the availability of free partial withdrawals after Year 1, enabling policyholders to access funds without fees despite earlier high charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="d4b10129-f843-43a5-8362-ff505e1fb13b">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 11 is set at 0.5%, reflecting its gradual reduction over time. This rate stands independently of whether the no-lapse guarantee rider was chosen.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 11 is specified at 0.5%, reflecting the declining schedule within the first 12 years. This detail is independent of the No Lapse Guarantee Rider, which was not elected and thus has no bearing on current surrender terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">NOT APPLICABLE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="59735a62-be54-4b86-a006-cd569871d4ef">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 11 is a fee applied when withdrawing funds early, based on the policy's surrender charge schedule. This detail has no bearing on the No Lapse Guarantee Rider since the rider was not selected.</data>
  <data key="d4">NOT APPLICABLE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311">
  <data key="d3">Year 11 has a surrender charge of 0.5%, reflecting the gradual reduction in penalties over time. This does not affect the 61-day grace period granted if premiums are missed.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872">
  <data key="d3">Year 11's low surrender charge reflects declining penalties over time, while the notice about impending lapse applies when payments fail despite ongoing costs. These describe separate risk pathways leading to policy loss.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELEVANCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="ae3f8271-673d-4549-8f9b-46011b263dfc">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 11 reflects the ongoing reduction schedule of penalties for early withdrawal, independent of payment compliance. This does not influence whether the policy lapses due to missed payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a">
  <data key="d3">A high surrender charge in Year 11 reduces the net surrender value, meaning less or nothing may remain when the policy eventually lapses, leading to potential forfeiture.</data>
  <data key="d4">IMPACTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="1c5eba0f-2f29-43d1-b13a-bc342d4f4ae4">
  <data key="d3">A high surrender charge in Year 11 may discourage premature withdrawal despite favorable index performance, affecting whether policyholders benefit fully from the Indexed Account's growth potential.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="1d4b712e-5e26-4cf9-a7ad-301c683e58e3">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges impact the net payout upon withdrawal, particularly relevant in later years such as Year 11. This does not influence the cap rate mechanism, which controls how much interest can be credited regardless of surrender timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77">
  <data key="d3">While the surrender charge impacts the cost of accessing funds later in the policy term, it has no bearing on the guaranteed minimum interest rate provided by the Floor Rate, which protects against negative returns regardless of withdrawal timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955">
  <data key="d3">The Year 11 surrender charge indicates a declining fee schedule over time, whereas the Participation Rate dictates how indexed gains are applied. Though both influence overall policy value, they do so through separate mechanisms without mutual impact.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3">
  <data key="d3">A low surrender charge in Year 11 (0.5%) indicates reduced penalty for early termination at that stage, potentially reflecting the cumulative impact of interest credited via the point-to-point method over prior years, thus aligning with longer-term investment behavior supported by consistent return calculations.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="e6aa2762-a82e-4371-9d8e-da19a25dd6d1">
  <data key="d3">A 0.5% surrender charge in Year 11 reduces the net proceeds from withdrawing funds, potentially diminishing gains accrued through the S&amp;P 500 Index Account.</data>
  <data key="d4">IMPACTED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="492399d4-a4a8-470a-b04c-a4e38ca316d2">
  <data key="d3">The Year 11 surrender charge impacts the net proceeds upon withdrawal, whereas the S&amp;P 500 cap determines the maximum credited interest based on market performance. Though both relate to financial outcomes, they function in separate dimensions: one governs access costs, the other growth ceilings.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="faf66c9e-da0e-4813-9561-2d1480419596">
  <data key="d3">A 0.5% surrender charge in Year 11 implies that withdrawing funds at that stage incurs a small fee, which may slightly offset returns generated by the 100% participation rate in the S&amp;P 500 Index Account.</data>
