<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="b0213eb9-bcd3-41f0-9381-ae8e81ac0f24">
  <data key="d3">The Year 11 surrender charge of 0.5% indicates continued cost exposure late in the policy’s life, whereas the one-year crediting period ensures annual reset of index-based gains. Though temporally distinct, both features influence overall policy value over time without directly affecting each other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="de64be79-d83e-496d-97f6-5d2e80705c21">
  <data key="d3">The Year 11 surrender charge reflects a contractual fee on policy withdrawals, whereas the Global Diversified Index Account defines one of several investment options available under the policy. There is no functional overlap or mutual influence between them.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
