  <data key="d3">A minimal surrender charge in Year 11 reflects mature policy status, where flexibility increases; however, it has no bearing on the mandatory $100 minimum premium per payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa">
  <data key="d3">A 0.5% surrender charge in Year 11 underscores the importance of sustained premium payments, such as the $100 minimum, to prevent premature policy cancellation and associated financial losses.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2">
  <data key="d3">The low 0.5% surrender charge in Year 11 reflects the diminishing penalty schedule applied after ten years, making it less costly to exit the policy at that stage regardless of whether high premiums were paid earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="0d35c1ce-d96d-4562-80f8-0654abe126d2">
  <data key="d3">A 0.5% surrender charge in Year 11 reflects the diminishing penalties over time, allowing flexibility for high-premium contributors who may have reached the $50,000 annual cap under tax-qualified terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPRTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">A reduced surrender charge of 0.5% in Year 11 makes it financially less risky to exit the policy late in its term, supporting the feasibility of meeting the $6,000 annual premium goal without fear of high penalties.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES_FEASIBILITY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">While the 0.5% surrender charge in Year 11 reflects a penalty for exiting early, it operates independently of the 3.5% premium load, though both contribute to total outlays that reduce accumulated cash value.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY_COSTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">A 0.5% surrender charge in Year 11 reflects the diminishing penalty structure, suggesting long-term retention incentives. This does not directly affect the monthly COI deduction but influences overall policy economics, especially if one considers future liquidity needs versus sustained coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
