  <data key="d3">The 0% surrender charge in Year 12 reflects the culmination of a gradual annual reduction initiated earlier—such as the 8% charge in Year 3—which was part of the same phased-decline pattern.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332">
  <data key="d3">A 0% surrender charge in Year 12 or later indicates the completion of the annual decline from earlier years, including Year 4’s 7% charge, confirming the full expiration of surrender fees post-Year 12.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633">
  <data key="d3">By Year 12, surrender charges have fully diminished to 0%, completing the annual reduction cycle initiated earlier, including Year 5’s 6% charge.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="84b84dec-45b7-4ca8-ae2f-a68466866f24">
  <data key="d3">A 0% surrender charge in Year 12 or later indicates the completion of the declining schedule initiated in earlier years, including Year 6’s 5% charge.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca">
  <data key="d3">By Year 12 or later, surrender charges reach 0%, completing the scheduled phase-out that began at 10% in Year 1 and decreased each subsequent year through Year 7’s 4%.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75">
  <data key="d3">By Year 12, surrender charges have been reduced to zero, meaning any earlier year—like Year 8—is part of the phase when charges still exist and are higher than zero.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00">
  <data key="d3">By Year 12 or later, surrender charges have fully expired, meaning any earlier charges—like the 2% in Year 9—are no longer applicable due to the annual decline culminating in zero.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">A zero surrender charge in Year 12 or later implies that prior years—like Year 10—still carry a non-zero charge, such as 1%, maintaining consistency with the gradual decline described.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">Year 11 has a non-zero surrender charge of 0.5%, setting the stage for its elimination in Year 12, marking the end of the charging period.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">The fact that surrender charges reach 0% in Year 12 or later depends on them being based on premiums paid within the initial ten-year window, ensuring they decline systematically.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">When surrender charges reach 0% in Year 12 or later, they do not reduce the account value when calculating the cash surrender value. This makes the formula in fact_sentence_2 simpler, as only outstanding loans remain as deductions.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b">
  <data key="d3">The absence of surrender charges in Year 12 does not affect the availability of fee-free partial withdrawals beginning in Year 1. These are independent features governed by separate rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges expire by Year 12, eliminating penalties on early termination. This does not affect whether the policy remains active despite low account balances.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="9d636a77-9852-432c-b8fb-7593d751a2da">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges expire entirely by Year 12, removing financial penalties if the policy is surrendered late. This does not affect the availability of annual partial withdrawals, which remain permitted independently based on account value.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="628900ad-3981-4384-be18-2669a41ba276">
  <data key="d3">The statement about zero surrender charges in Year 12 or later describes the termination of fees tied to early policy cancellation. This information does not relate to the availability of the no-lapse guarantee rider, which is a separate feature offered optionally.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="59735a62-be54-4b86-a006-cd569871d4ef">
  <data key="d3">The statement about zero surrender charges in Year 12 or later describes fee structures related to policy termination. This does not relate directly to the condition required for maintaining a no-lapse guarantee rider's activity.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872">
  <data key="d3">The absence of surrender charges in Year 12 does not influence the timing or conditions under which insurers notify about impending lapses due to insufficient account value.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="d4b10129-f843-43a5-8362-ff505e1fb13b">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge being 0% in Year 12 or later reflects the scheduled reduction over time, independent of rider selection. This fact stands separately from whether the no-lapse guarantee rider was chosen.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311">
  <data key="d3">The statement about zero surrender charges in Year 12 or later pertains to withdrawal costs when terminating the policy early. This does not influence or relate directly to the 61-day grace period offered for missed premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="ae3f8271-673d-4549-8f9b-46011b263dfc">
  <data key="d3">The statement about zero surrender charges in Year 12 or later relates to withdrawal penalties based on policy duration. It does not influence nor depend on whether a premium was paid within the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a">
  <data key="d3">When surrender charges become 0% in Year 12 or later, it means policyholders may withdraw full account value without penalties—but only if the policy hasn’t lapsed. After lapse, regardless of surrender charge status, any remaining surrender value is forfeited.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="1c5eba0f-2f29-43d1-b13a-bc342d4f4ae4">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges being waived after Year 12 do not influence how interest is credited to index accounts, which depend solely on index performance and contractual rates.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="1d4b712e-5e26-4cf9-a7ad-301c683e58e3">
  <data key="d3">No surrender charges after Year 12 enable policyholders to withdraw funds freely, potentially maximizing benefits from capped index returns over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges being waived after Year 12 means policyholders gain full access to funds without penalty at that stage. This has no bearing on the Floor Rate’s function, which protects against negative returns irrespective of surrender timelines.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955">
  <data key="d3">No surrender charges after Year 12 enable unhindered access to account value, potentially maximizing returns driven by the Participation Rate over time. However, the Participation Rate itself does not impact when or whether surrender fees are waived.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3">
  <data key="d3">The removal of surrender charges in Year 12 enables policyholders to hold onto policies longer, increasing the likelihood of benefiting from multiple cycles of the point-to-point interest crediting method.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="e6aa2762-a82e-4371-9d8e-da19a25dd6d1">
  <data key="d3">The absence of surrender charges after Year 12 has no impact on the features or operation of the S&amp;P 500 Index Account, which functions based on its own indexing rules regardless of withdrawal fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="492399d4-a4a8-470a-b04c-a4e38ca316d2">
  <data key="d3">No surrender charges after Year 12 allow policyholders to fully benefit from any gains accrued under the S&amp;P 500’s 10.5% cap, removing financial barriers to withdrawing capital once the lock-in period ends.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="faf66c9e-da0e-4813-9561-2d1480419596">
  <data key="d3">The removal of surrender charges after Year 12 supports strategic holding of the S&amp;P 500 account, maximizing benefit from its 100% participation rate over time without early withdrawal penalties.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="a4c6faf8-57d8-4d84-affb-d94570b3ae60">
  <data key="d3">No surrender charge after Year 12 enables unrestricted access to funds, which complements the stable performance guarantees provided by the 0% floor on the S&amp;P 500 Index Account. Together, they enhance long-term flexibility and risk mitigation within the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="a0671d34-e31b-4b17-8ed5-6a9d495c5148">
  <data key="d3">After 12 years, when surrender charges vanish, the annual crediting mechanism ensures that gains earned via the S&amp;P 500’s performance are retained entirely upon withdrawal, maximizing the return potential tied to the 1-year crediting cycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="62714aed-4640-40fa-9927-1e7eaaddb24c">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges being waived after Year 12 do not affect the availability or operation of the NASDAQ-100 Index Account, which remains active regardless of withdrawal fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="4144da65-9775-496c-b601-6cbcd31e5849">
  <data key="d3">No surrender charge after Year 12 enables unrestricted access to the account's growth, including any returns capped at 9.0% via the NASDAQ-100 Index Account. This timing aligns with the benefit of capping upside exposure.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="32909f74-b806-4169-8ab1-602ea158ef9f">
  <data key="d3">The elimination of surrender charges after Year 12 enhances the value of maintaining exposure to the NASDAQ-100 account’s 100% participation rate, allowing long-term retention of gains without penalty.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="bce094ed-5c85-40d1-800b-e0894835715b">
  <data key="d3">The absence of surrender charges after Year 12 means policyholders can access funds without penalty late in the contract term. This temporal benefit has no bearing on the fixed 0% floor applied to the NASDAQ-100 Index Account’s return calculations.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="b0213eb9-bcd3-41f0-9381-ae8e81ac0f24">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges being waived after Year 12 allow policyholders to access accumulated value freely, making longer holding periods more attractive. This complements the annual crediting mechanism of the NASDAQ-100 Index Account, encouraging sustained investment to maximize compounded returns.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="de64be79-d83e-496d-97f6-5d2e80705c21">
  <data key="d3">The absence of surrender charges after Year 12 supports longer-term retention of funds tied to index accounts like the Global Diversified Index Account, enhancing their appeal over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES_VALUE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="13cdba53-929e-487b-9dac-c7e31bdd92a0">
  <data key="d3">No surrender charges after Year 12 enable policyholders to withdraw or surrender the policy freely, potentially maximizing benefits from capped growth in the Global Diversified Index Account over extended periods.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="22fdc352-4139-456b-bd73-2207bfdefc4e">
  <data key="d3">The absence of surrender charges after Year 12 enables policyholders to exit the contract without cost, making the 100% participation rate more valuable over extended holding periods.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES_VALUE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="a5cf74c6-3010-4b87-83b5-452662af8369">
  <data key="d3">A zero surrender charge from Year 12 onward enables full liquidity without fee penalties, whereas the 0% floor on the Global Diversified Index Account protects against negative index returns. Neither condition influences the other’s functionality within the policy framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176">
  <data key="d3">The elimination of surrender charges after Year 12 enhances the incentive to maintain regular premium payments—even minimal ones like $100—since policyholders gain full access to accumulated value without penalties upon withdrawal or surrender.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa">
  <data key="d3">No surrender charge after Year 12 allows policyholders who maintain minimum premiums like $100 to withdraw funds freely, reinforcing the importance of consistent contributions.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2">
  <data key="d3">The removal of surrender charges after Year 12 incentivizes sustained premium payments up to the $50,000 ceiling, ensuring long-term retention benefits align with higher contributions.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="0d35c1ce-d96d-4562-80f8-0654abe126d2">
  <data key="d3">The removal of surrender charges in Year 12 or later enhances the attractiveness of contributing up to the $50,000 annual cap, ensuring funds remain accessible without penalties once the policy matures financially.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">The elimination of surrender charges after Year 12 makes it more feasible to meet the $6,000 annual premium requirement, as policyholders have greater flexibility and security in retaining accumulated value.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES_FEASIBILITY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">While the 3.5% load reduces the net amount added per premium, its impact diminishes over time due to compounding returns. By Year 12, when surrender charges vanish, the cumulative effect of these loads may still affect overall policy performance unless offset by strong gains.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">After Year 12, there are no surrender charges, allowing full access to the account value unaffected by fees. This makes consistent COI deductions less impactful on final payout potential since no additional penalties apply at withdrawal.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="6bfb8452-bcec-4db6-b212-fd25bdcfbc79">
  <data key="d3">While the $12 monthly administrative charge continues indefinitely, its impact diminishes relative to total account value once surrender charges expire at Year 12, allowing greater net access to accumulated funds without additional penalties.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="0b7e0a06-5166-489d-a873-3b798f915e2c">
  <data key="d3">After Year 12, no surrender charges apply, allowing full access to accumulated funds without penalty. This reduces the risk associated with continuing to pay monthly charges, especially since those charges persist throughout the policy term unless offset by growth.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES_VIABILITY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="1b6d4d68-07ed-4c80-987c-ddf958d36f08">
  <data key="d3">After Year 12, there are no surrender charges, so the effect of monthly deductions becomes more predictable and cumulative without additional penalties, allowing greater flexibility in accessing funds despite prior reductions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25">
  <data key="d3">Knowing that surrender charges vanish after Year 12 enhances the practicality of exercising the 60-day window to modify death benefit options, especially for those planning long-term policy changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES_FEASIBILITY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">After Year 12, the elimination of surrender charges enables full utilization of the 90% loan cap tied to surrender value, removing penalties associated with accessing policy funds.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">While the 4% loan interest rate applies consistently throughout the policy term, it becomes more financially favorable in Years 12+ where zero surrender charges allow full access to accumulated value without additional penalties, reducing overall cost burden.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">After Year 12, surrender charges cease entirely, reducing pressure to repay loans quickly. Even though loans incur a net 1% annual cost, the absence of surrender charges makes holding them longer financially feasible without penalty.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_RELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">Knowing the net cost of borrowing is only 1% annually helps justify retaining the policy past Year 12 when surrender charges expire, especially if borrowers rely on access to cash value without triggering early termination costs.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES_VIABILITY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">While surrender charges cease in Year 12+, any outstanding loans still reduce the final death benefit payment, meaning post-Year 12 access does not eliminate prior loan liabilities.</data>
  <data key="d4">NEUTRAL_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="9ac0c7c4-1321-469b-afaa-abe6d54dbd8e">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge provision applies to policies issued under Horizon Wealth Protection Insurance, grounding its operational rules within the framework of this specific insurer’s product offerings.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_LINK</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="7c78ce63-cb1f-4b61-bdcd-88d0ce4bcb53">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge details in Year 12+ do not relate to the geographical execution site of the document. One concerns internal policy terms, while the other specifies legal or procedural documentation origin.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="ba1c52cb-9fba-4846-9a66-8e0c71e2a754">
  <data key="d3">The absence of surrender charges in Year 12 does not affect the document's physical or legal authentication indicated by the seal.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73" target="79f032d3-1299-41de-85c7-f944c1411556">
  <data key="d3">The statement that surrender charges drop to 0% in Year 12 or later is consistent with standard policy timelines, and its validity could depend on being documented around or after October 3, 2024, though no explicit link exists.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUALIZES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
