<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e">
  <data key="d3">The ability to take free partial withdrawals after Year 1 indicates that some forms of fund access do not trigger surrender charges, even though such charges still apply upon full surrender within the initial 12 years.</data>
  <data key="d4">APPLIES_WHEN</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018">
  <data key="d3">After Year 1, the elimination of surrender charges permits unrestricted partial withdrawals, making it possible to access funds freely—this directly follows from the expiration of the initial 10% surrender charge.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS FROM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890">
  <data key="d3">The allowance of free partial withdrawals after Year 1 means that even if a surrender charge like 9% remains in Year 2, such withdrawals avoid penalty, maintaining flexibility despite existing charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPTS FROM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b">
  <data key="d3">Tax-free partial withdrawals are permitted annually after Year 1 without triggering surrender charges, independent of the declining surrender charge schedule. Therefore, even though Year 3 carries an 8% surrender charge, it doesn’t restrict the right to withdraw funds freely.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332">
  <data key="d3">After Year 1, policyholders may take tax-free partial withdrawals up to 10% of the account value annually without paying surrender charges. This provision remains active even when surrender charges like the 7% in Year 4 still apply.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633">
  <data key="d3">After Year 1, policyholders may take tax-free partial withdrawals without paying surrender charges. This feature remains consistent even when the surrender charge is still active, such as in Year 5, where it stands at 6%.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="84b84dec-45b7-4ca8-ae2f-a68466866f24">
  <data key="d3">Free partial withdrawals after Year 1 are permitted without surrender charges, meaning even though the surrender charge remains at 5% in Year 6, such withdrawals remain penalty-free under the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca">
  <data key="d3">Even though surrender charges persist into Year 7 (at 4%), the availability of free partial withdrawals ensures policyholders can access funds without penalty, maintaining flexibility despite existing charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">UNAFFECTED BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75">
  <data key="d3">Free partial withdrawals are allowed annually after Year 1 without triggering surrender charges, regardless of the 3% surrender fee applicable in Year 8.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00">
  <data key="d3">Free partial withdrawals after Year 1 are permitted without triggering surrender charges, so even though the charge remains at 2% in Year 9, such withdrawals avoid penalties entirely due to the policy’s exception clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals are permitted tax-free and without surrender charge starting in Year 2, independent of the specific surrender charge amount in Year 10, which remains part of a separate fee schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">After Year 1, policyholders may take tax-free partial withdrawals up to 10% of the account value annually without paying surrender charges. This provision becomes increasingly relevant as surrender charges diminish over time, culminating in a near-zero charge by Year 11.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">Fee-free partial withdrawals starting in Year 1 do not influence whether surrender charges remain at 0% in Year 12. Each rule operates independently based on distinct conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">Tax-free partial withdrawals being permitted post-Year 1 reduce the impact of surrender charges, making them less relevant for small, periodic distributions.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">Since partial withdrawals after Year 1 are exempt from surrender charges, the calculation of Cash Surrender Value remains unaffected by these transactions, preserving its integrity under the stated formula.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="9d636a77-9852-432c-b8fb-7593d751a2da">
  <data key="d3">After the first year, policyholders gain the right to make tax-free partial withdrawals up to 10% of the account value annually, exempt from surrender charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="628900ad-3981-4384-be18-2669a41ba276">
  <data key="d3">Free partial withdrawals after Year 1 allow policyholders to access funds without penalty. This feature operates independently of whether the No Lapse Guarantee Rider is selected.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="d4b10129-f843-43a5-8362-ff505e1fb13b">
  <data key="d3">Free partial withdrawals are permitted after Year 1 regardless of rider selection. The absence of the No Lapse Guarantee Rider does not affect withdrawal privileges.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="59735a62-be54-4b86-a006-cd569871d4ef">
  <data key="d3">Free partial withdrawals after Year 1 allow policyholders flexibility in accessing funds without penalty. This feature operates independently of whether the No Lapse Guarantee Rider is elected or maintained.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0">
  <data key="d3">Free partial withdrawals allow policyholders to access funds without penalties after Year 1, enhancing financial flexibility. This benefit complements the No Lapse Guarantee Rider by providing additional control over funds while maintaining coverage regardless of account value fluctuations.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311">
  <data key="d3">Free partial withdrawals allow policyholders access to funds post-Year 1 without penalty, independent of the grace period used when premiums are late.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a">
  <data key="d3">Free partial withdrawals are permitted after Year 1 only if the policy remains active; otherwise, they become unavailable upon lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872">
  <data key="d3">Free partial withdrawals after Year 1 allow policyholders flexibility in accessing funds, but if the account value drops too low due to such withdrawals, it may lead to insufficient funds for ongoing deductions, triggering potential lapses. This creates an indirect link where excessive withdrawals could contribute to conditions leading to lapse notifications.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY CONTRIBUTES TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="ae3f8271-673d-4549-8f9b-46011b263dfc">
  <data key="d3">Partial withdrawals are permitted tax-free after the first year without triggering surrender charges, independent of premium payment timelines. This benefit does not affect the risk of policy lapse due to missed payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1">
  <data key="d3">Free partial withdrawals after Year 1 offer flexibility in accessing funds, whereas the 4% minimum cap safeguards against underperformance in indexed accounts. Neither feature affects the functionality or terms of the other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7">
  <data key="d3">Free partial withdrawals after Year 1 provide investors with accessible liquidity, whereas the 25% minimum participation rate safeguards against underperformance in indexed accounts. Though unrelated in function, both contribute to overall investor protection and benefit design.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="c4dbdf51-a4cd-4a65-8903-f269d529eefd">
  <data key="d3">The option for free partial withdrawals after Year 1 enhances fund accessibility, allowing investors to utilize accumulated value generated by the fixed account’s guaranteed 2% interest rate without penalty.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25">
  <data key="d3">Free partial withdrawals after Year 1 do not affect the need for 60 days’ notice when switching death benefit options, as these are distinct administrative procedures governed separately.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">Free partial withdrawals after Year 1 align with the loan provision allowing up to 90% of surrender value, suggesting coordinated design for early policyholder liquidity, though via distinct financial instruments.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">Free partial withdrawals after Year 1 enable fund access without penalty, supporting financial flexibility alongside the option to take policy loans at a fixed 4% interest rate, creating multiple non-redundant avenues for policyholder liquidity.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">Free partial withdrawals after Year 1 provide accessible liquidity without surrender charges, supporting long-term use alongside loan mechanisms where borrowed amounts grow at 3%.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">Free partial withdrawals after Year 1 support the practical use of the policy’s funds, indirectly reinforcing why low-cost borrowing (at 1%) may remain an attractive alternative when accessing cash.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">Free partial withdrawals after Year 1 reduce the account value, potentially leading to higher outstanding loans, which in turn decrease the final death benefit payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="9ac0c7c4-1321-469b-afaa-abe6d54dbd8e">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 describes a specific policy feature regarding early withdrawals, while fact_sentence_2 identifies the issuing company. The latter adds institutional context but does not alter or depend on the former’s content.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="7c78ce63-cb1f-4b61-bdcd-88d0ce4bcb53">
  <data key="d3">The availability of free partial withdrawals after Year 1 relates to policyholder benefits under the contract, while the document’s execution in Chicago, Illinois, indicates its legal origin. These elements exist independently—one describes a feature of the policy, the other specifies where it was formally signed.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="79f032d3-1299-41de-85c7-f944c1411556">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines post-Year-1 withdrawal privileges under a policy, while fact_sentence_2 establishes that this information was formally documented on October 3, 2024, providing a timestamp for its validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">TIMING_CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b" target="ba1c52cb-9fba-4846-9a66-8e0c71e2a754">
  <data key="d3">The availability of free partial withdrawals after Year 1 pertains to policyholder benefits, while the presence of a seal indicates formal documentation. These elements exist independently—one concerns contractual rights, the other administrative authentication.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
