  <data key="d3">An optional no-lapse guarantee rider exists to help maintain coverage without premium payments, independent of the annual surrender charges that reduce over time until Year 12.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="628900ad-3981-4384-be18-2669a41ba276" target="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00">
  <data key="d3">The no-lapse guarantee rider is offered as an optional feature, though it was not selected by the policyholder. This statement does not depend on or relate to the level of surrender charges in Year 9.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="628900ad-3981-4384-be18-2669a41ba276" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">The no-lapse guarantee rider is offered as an option, though it was not selected by the policyholder. Its existence is unrelated to the specific surrender charge amount in Year 10.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="628900ad-3981-4384-be18-2669a41ba276" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">The availability of the no-lapse guarantee rider indicates an additional protection option, whereas the Year 11 surrender charge specifies fee details tied to early termination, independent of rider selection.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="628900ad-3981-4384-be18-2669a41ba276" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">The availability of the no-lapse guarantee rider refers to an optional benefit that protects against policy lapse due to insufficient funds. This has no bearing on when surrender charges expire or how they are calculated over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="628900ad-3981-4384-be18-2669a41ba276" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">The availability of a no-lapse guarantee rider does not affect how surrender charges are calculated, which rely solely on premium payments in the initial ten years.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="628900ad-3981-4384-be18-2669a41ba276" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">The availability of a no-lapse guarantee rider does not affect how cash surrender value is computed, which relies solely on account value, surrender charges, and loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="628900ad-3981-4384-be18-2669a41ba276" target="9d636a77-9852-432c-b8fb-7593d751a2da">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a no-lapse guarantee rider has no bearing on the rules governing tax-free partial withdrawals. One feature does not modify or enable the other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="628900ad-3981-4384-be18-2669a41ba276" target="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b">
  <data key="d3">The No Lapse Guarantee Rider is offered as an option to prevent policy lapse under certain conditions. Its availability does not affect the terms of free partial withdrawals.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="628900ad-3981-4384-be18-2669a41ba276" target="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0">
  <data key="d3">The No Lapse Guarantee Rider, when selected, ensures continuous coverage regardless of the account value dropping to zero.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="628900ad-3981-4384-be18-2669a41ba276" target="d4b10129-f843-43a5-8362-ff505e1fb13b">
  <data key="d3">The No Lapse Guarantee Rider exists as an optional feature within the policy framework. However, it was explicitly not elected by the policyholder.</data>
  <data key="d4">AVAILABLE_BUT_NOT_CHOSEN</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="628900ad-3981-4384-be18-2669a41ba276" target="59735a62-be54-4b86-a006-cd569871d4ef">
  <data key="d3">The availability of the No Lapse Guarantee Rider implies it can be added to a policy, but its ongoing effectiveness requires consistent payment of minimum guaranteed premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_AVAILABILITY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="628900ad-3981-4384-be18-2669a41ba276" target="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a no-lapse guarantee rider does not influence the length of the grace period for premium payment. The grace period remains independent of whether such a rider is selected.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="628900ad-3981-4384-be18-2669a41ba276" target="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a no-lapse guarantee rider indicates an option to prevent lapses due to insufficient funds, though it was not selected. This contrasts with the actual procedural notice given by insurers if the account value fails to meet deduction requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">NOT RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="628900ad-3981-4384-be18-2669a41ba276" target="ae3f8271-673d-4549-8f9b-46011b263dfc">
  <data key="d3">The existence of the No Lapse Guarantee Rider as an option doesn't affect the outcome when premiums are missed beyond the grace period, since the rider was not elected.</data>
  <data key="d4">NOT APPLICABLE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="628900ad-3981-4384-be18-2669a41ba276" target="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a no-lapse guarantee rider offers protection against policy lapse due to insufficient funds, though it was not selected. This contrasts with the outcome described in fact_sentence_2, where lapsing leads to forfeiture of any remaining surrender value.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="628900ad-3981-4384-be18-2669a41ba276" target="9ac0c7c4-1321-469b-afaa-abe6d54dbd8e">
  <data key="d3">The presence of the no-lapse guarantee rider is relevant to policies offered by Horizon Wealth Protection Insurance, implying that such riders may be part of the company’s product suite.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_LINK</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="628900ad-3981-4384-be18-2669a41ba276" target="79f032d3-1299-41de-85c7-f944c1411556">
  <data key="d3">The mention of the No Lapse Guarantee Rider being available aligns with the timing of the document's execution on October 3, 2024, which formalizes its inclusion in current policy offerings.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="628900ad-3981-4384-be18-2669a41ba276" target="7c78ce63-cb1f-4b61-bdcd-88d0ce4bcb53">
  <data key="d3">The presence of a no-lapse guarantee rider option does not influence or depend on the document being executed in Chicago, Illinois. These details serve different purposes: one relates to policy design, the other to legal or procedural documentation.</data>
