<edge source="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0" target="0ced7bd1-f54b-4593-bd8e-211c6a77ddb9">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0" target="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e">
  <data key="d3">The No Lapse Guarantee Rider ensures continued coverage even at zero account value, contrasting with surrender charges that impose fees for exiting the policy early. One relates to retention incentives, the other to exit penalties.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0" target="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018">
  <data key="d3">The No Lapse Guarantee Rider would prevent policy lapse even if the account value reaches zero, ensuring continued coverage. However, since this rider was not elected, its benefits do not affect the surrender charge structure described in Year 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">NOT APPLICABLE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0" target="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890">
  <data key="d3">The absence of an elected No Lapse Guarantee Rider means the policy remains vulnerable to lapsing if premiums are not sustained, despite the 9% surrender charge in Year 2 being part of the early withdrawal cost structure.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0" target="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b">
  <data key="d3">The absence of an active no-lapse guarantee means the policy remains vulnerable to lapse if premiums are unpaid, regardless of surrender charges in Year 3.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0" target="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332">
  <data key="d3">Even though the No Lapse Guarantee Rider would prevent lapse under certain conditions, it was not elected, so it has no effect on the surrender charge applied in Year 4.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0" target="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633">
  <data key="d3">Even though the No Lapse Guarantee Rider would prevent lapse under low-value conditions, its absence means the policy could still lapse if premiums are unpaid—unrelated to the Year 5 surrender charge level.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0" target="84b84dec-45b7-4ca8-ae2f-a68466866f24">
  <data key="d3">The No Lapse Guarantee Rider would prevent policy lapse even at zero account value, but since it was not elected, its protections do not apply. As such, it bears no direct relation to the surrender charge amount in Year 6.</data>
  <data key="d4">NOT APPLICABLE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0" target="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca">
  <data key="d3">The No Lapse Guarantee Rider would prevent policy lapse despite low account values, but since it was not elected, its protections do not apply. As such, it bears no influence on the calculation or existence of surrender charges like those in Year 7.</data>
  <data key="d4">NOT APPLICABLE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0" target="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75">
  <data key="d3">The No Lapse Guarantee Rider would prevent policy lapse due to insufficient funds, but since it was not elected, its protective mechanism does not apply. As such, the absence of this rider means the policy remains vulnerable to lapse if premiums are not sustained, regardless of the Year 8 surrender charge level.</data>
  <data key="d4">NOT APPLICABLE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0" target="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00">
  <data key="d3">The absence of an active No Lapse Guarantee Rider means the policy remains subject to lapsing if premiums are not maintained, independent of the surrender charge applied in Year 9.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">The No Lapse Guarantee Rider would prevent policy lapse despite low account values, but since it was not elected, it does not influence any aspects of surrender charges or premium obligations discussed in relation to Year 10.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">The No Lapse Guarantee Rider would prevent policy lapse despite low account values, but since it was not elected, its protections do not apply. This makes the existence of a surrender charge in Year 11 irrelevant to the rider’s functionality.</data>
  <data key="d4">NOT APPLICABLE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">A No Lapse Guarantee Rider ensures continued coverage even if the account value reaches zero. It operates independently of surrender charge schedules.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">A no-lapse guarantee rider ensures continuous coverage even when account value reaches zero, independent of surrender charge calculations tied to early premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">A no-lapse guarantee ensures continued coverage even if the account value reaches zero. This feature has no impact on how cash surrender value is computed, which depends solely on account value, surrender charges, and loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0" target="9d636a77-9852-432c-b8fb-7593d751a2da">
  <data key="d3">The No Lapse Guarantee Rider protects against policy termination despite declining account values, independent of the ability to make annual partial withdrawals, which are governed by different terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0" target="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b">
  <data key="d3">The No Lapse Guarantee Rider ensures continuous coverage even if the account value reaches zero, offering security against lapses. This stability supports the ability to take advantage of free partial withdrawals without fear of losing coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0" target="628900ad-3981-4384-be18-2669a41ba276">
  <data key="d3">The availability of the No Lapse Guarantee Rider allows policyholders to maintain coverage under adverse financial conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0" target="59735a62-be54-4b86-a006-cd569871d4ef">
  <data key="d3">The No Lapse Guarantee Rider ensures continued coverage despite a zero account value, but only if minimum guaranteed premiums are consistently paid.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_DEPENDENCY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0" target="d4b10129-f843-43a5-8362-ff505e1fb13b">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains what the No Lapse Guarantee Rider would do if elected, but Fact_sentence_2 clarifies it was not selected, rendering the rider’s benefits irrelevant to this policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">NOT ELEC TED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0" target="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a no-lapse guarantee rider would prevent lapses due to low account value, making pre-lapse notifications unnecessary. However, since the rider was not elected, such protections do not apply, leading to reliance on standard lapse warnings.</data>
  <data key="d4">NOT APPLICABLE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0" target="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311">
  <data key="d3">The No Lapse Guarantee Rider prevents policy termination despite insufficient funds, whereas the 61-day grace period allows time to restore coverage after missing a payment. These mechanisms serve distinct purposes within policy maintenance.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0" target="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a">
  <data key="d3">The No Lapse Guarantee Rider prevents policy termination due to low account value, but since it wasn’t selected, this protection doesn’t apply. After a policy lapses without such protection, any residual surrender value is forfeited.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRASTS_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0" target="ae3f8271-673d-4549-8f9b-46011b263dfc">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a no-lapse guarantee rider would prevent policy lapse despite low account values, but since it wasn’t selected, its protective effect doesn’t apply. Therefore, the risk of lapse due to missed payments remains active.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRADICTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
