<edge source="d4b10129-f843-43a5-8362-ff505e1fb13b" target="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75">
  <data key="d3">The decision not to elect the No Lapse Guarantee Rider affects long-term policy stability but has no bearing on the surrender charge applied in Year 8, which follows a fixed reduction schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d4b10129-f843-43a5-8362-ff505e1fb13b" target="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00">
  <data key="d3">The decision not to select the No Lapse Guarantee Rider has no impact on the surrender charge amount in Year 9, which depends solely on the premium payment history and time elapsed since issuance.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d4b10129-f843-43a5-8362-ff505e1fb13b" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">The decision not to select the No Lapse Guarantee Rider has no impact on the surrender charge schedule, including its level in Year 10.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d4b10129-f843-43a5-8362-ff505e1fb13b" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">The decision not to select the no-lapse guarantee rider means the policy lacks automatic protection against lapsing due to insufficient premium payments. However, this choice has no impact on the surrender charge schedule, including the 0.5% fee in Year 11.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d4b10129-f843-43a5-8362-ff505e1fb13b" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">The decision not to select the no-lapse guarantee rider has no impact on the calculation or timing of surrender charges, including their elimination in Year 12.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d4b10129-f843-43a5-8362-ff505e1fb13b" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">The absence of the no-lapse guarantee rider does not affect how surrender charges are calculated, which remain tied to early premium payments regardless of rider selection.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d4b10129-f843-43a5-8362-ff505e1fb13b" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">The decision not to elect a no-lapse guarantee rider affects policy longevity risk but has no bearing on how cash surrender value is computed based on account value, surrender charges, and loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d4b10129-f843-43a5-8362-ff505e1fb13b" target="9d636a77-9852-432c-b8fb-7593d751a2da">
  <data key="d3">Not selecting the No Lapse Guarantee Rider has no impact on the availability of free partial withdrawals up to 10% of the account value per year.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d4b10129-f843-43a5-8362-ff505e1fb13b" target="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b">
  <data key="d3">The lack of a No Lapse Guarantee Rider means the policy may lapse if premiums are not maintained, though this has no bearing on the availability of free partial withdrawals post-Year 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d4b10129-f843-43a5-8362-ff505e1fb13b" target="628900ad-3981-4384-be18-2669a41ba276">
  <data key="d3">Although the No Lapse Guarantee Rider is offered as an add-on benefit, the policyholder chose not to include it in their coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">NOT_SELECTED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d4b10129-f843-43a5-8362-ff505e1fb13b" target="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 indicates the No Lapse Guarantee Rider was not chosen, so the protective function described in Fact_sentence_1 does not apply to this specific policy instance.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO EFFECT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d4b10129-f843-43a5-8362-ff505e1fb13b" target="59735a62-be54-4b86-a006-cd569871d4ef">
  <data key="d3">Since the No Lapse Guarantee Rider was not selected, the condition about maintaining coverage through premium payments has no applicability to this policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">NOT APPLICABLE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d4b10129-f843-43a5-8362-ff505e1fb13b" target="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872">
  <data key="d3">Since the No Lapse Guarantee Rider was not elected, the policyholder bears greater risk if the account value declines. This increases the importance of timely notifications when the account may fail to cover deductions, ensuring the holder has time to act.</data>
  <data key="d4">INCREASES RISK</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d4b10129-f843-43a5-8362-ff505e1fb13b" target="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311">
  <data key="d3">The lack of a No Lapse Guarantee Rider means the policyholder has no guaranteed protection against lapse due to missed payments, increasing dependence on external safeguards like the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL SUPPORT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d4b10129-f843-43a5-8362-ff505e1fb13b" target="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a">
  <data key="d3">The absence of the No Lapse Guarantee Rider increases the likelihood of policy lapse, leading to the potential loss of the surrender value upon termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">INCREASES RISK OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d4b10129-f843-43a5-8362-ff505e1fb13b" target="ae3f8271-673d-4549-8f9b-46011b263dfc">
  <data key="d3">The absence of the No Lapse Guarantee Rider means the policy has no built-in protection against termination if premiums are not sustained. This increases the chance that the policy will lapse if payments are delayed beyond the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">INCREASES RISK OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d4b10129-f843-43a5-8362-ff505e1fb13b" target="ba1c52cb-9fba-4846-9a66-8e0c71e2a754">
  <data key="d3">The lack of a no-lapse guarantee rider pertains to policy coverage details, while the presence of a seal indicates formal documentation integrity. These elements coexist without mutual influence.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d4b10129-f843-43a5-8362-ff505e1fb13b" target="7c78ce63-cb1f-4b61-bdcd-88d0ce4bcb53">
  <data key="d3">The lack of a no-lapse guarantee rider pertains to policy benefits and financial protections, while the document's execution in Chicago reflects its legal or administrative origin. These elements exist independently within the broader context of the policy documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
