<edge source="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872" target="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e">
  <data key="d3">The insurer’s notice regarding inadequate account value for monthly payments occurs independently of surrender charge applicability. This warning mechanism relates to ongoing premium payment obligations, whereas surrender charges pertain only to voluntary withdrawal decisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872" target="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018">
  <data key="d3">A lack of sufficient account value may lead to policy lapse, prompting a pre-lapse notification. While surrender charges reduce account value early on, they are not directly tied to the specific trigger described here.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872" target="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890">
  <data key="d3">A notice about impending lapse due to low account value highlights one path to policy termination, whereas the surrender charge in Year 2 applies specifically to voluntary cancellations during the initial phase. Neither condition depends on the other.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872" target="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b">
  <data key="d3">A warning about impending policy lapse due to inadequate account value precedes potential loss of coverage, whereas the first fact specifies annual surrender charges that reduce payout upon early exit. Both relate to financial risk outcomes but stem from distinct causes.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO DIRECT RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872" target="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332">
  <data key="d3">A warning about potential policy lapse due to inadequate account value precedes termination risks unrelated to surrender charges. This alert focuses on payment obligations rather than withdrawal penalties tied to surrender timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872" target="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633">
  <data key="d3">A notice about impending policy lapse occurs when account value cannot sustain monthly deductions, independent of surrender charges. This event does not depend on the specific surrender fee amount in Year 5.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872" target="84b84dec-45b7-4ca8-ae2f-a68466866f24">
  <data key="d3">A notice prior to lapse occurs if the account value fails to meet deduction requirements, regardless of surrender charges. The level of surrender charge in Year 6 has no bearing on this trigger condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872" target="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca">
  <data key="d3">A notice about insufficient funds triggering a lapse is unrelated to the specific surrender charge rate in Year 7, though both concern policy sustainability under financial stress.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872" target="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75">
  <data key="d3">When the account value falls short of covering required monthly deductions, the insurer notifies the policyholder at least 30 days prior to potential lapse. This scenario is independent of the specific surrender charge amount in Year 8.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872" target="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00">
  <data key="d3">Insufficient account value triggering a pre-lapse notification occurs independently of surrender charge schedules, focusing on payment adequacy rather than withdrawal costs.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">Insurers issue warnings at least 30 days prior to policy lapse if the account value cannot meet monthly deductions. This procedural step operates independently of the specific surrender charge amount applicable in Year 10.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">A warning before lapse occurs if account value cannot meet deductions highlights financial sustainability concerns, whereas the Year 11 surrender charge indicates penalty levels tied to early exit timing. Both concern policy termination but through distinct mechanisms.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELEVANCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">Insurers notifying policyholders prior to lapse based on inadequate account value has no bearing on whether surrender charges are applied in Year 12 or beyond.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">The insurer's notice prior to lapse due to low account value does not rely on surrender charge calculations, though both concern policy termination risks.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">When the account value cannot sustain monthly deductions, the insurer notifies the policyholder prior to lapse, regardless of how the cash surrender value was previously computed.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872" target="9d636a77-9852-432c-b8fb-7593d751a2da">
  <data key="d3">Notification of possible lapse due to inadequate account value could result from reduced funds caused by prior withdrawals, including those allowed under the partial withdrawal provision. This reflects a potential downstream effect on financial sustainability.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872" target="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b">
  <data key="d3">When the account value cannot meet monthly deductions, the insurer notifies the policyholder ahead of time, giving opportunity to take corrective action—including potentially making partial withdrawals—to avoid lapse. However, since withdrawals are already permitted post-Year 1, they represent one possible response to such warnings.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESPONSE TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872" target="628900ad-3981-4384-be18-2669a41ba276">
  <data key="d3">Insurers issue warnings prior to policy lapse when account balances fall short, ensuring policyholders have time to act. However, this does not imply that a no-lapse guarantee rider was active or utilized.</data>
  <data key="d4">NOT RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872" target="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0">
  <data key="d3">Without an active no-lapse guarantee rider, the insurer issues advance notice before lapping a policy due to insufficient funds, ensuring transparency despite lack of automatic protection against lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">NOT APPLICABLE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872" target="59735a62-be54-4b86-a006-cd569871d4ef">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence outlines the insurer's notice procedure before policy lapse due to insufficient funds. This scenario is unrelated to the no-lapse guarantee rider since it was not elected, making the first sentence irrelevant to this event.</data>
  <data key="d4">NOT RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872" target="d4b10129-f843-43a5-8362-ff505e1fb13b">
  <data key="d3">The insurer's obligation to provide advance notice before lapse only becomes significant because the No Lapse Guarantee Rider was not chosen, leaving the policy vulnerable to termination without additional safeguards.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPOSES VULNERABILITY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872" target="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311">
  <data key="d3">When the account value falls short of covering monthly deductions, the insurer notifies the policyholder at least 30 days prior to lapse, initiating a process that leads into the 61-day grace period where reinstatement remains possible.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872" target="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a">
  <data key="d3">When the account value cannot meet monthly deductions, the insurer notifies the policyholder ahead of time. If no action is taken, the policy may lapse, resulting in complete loss of any remaining surrender value.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872" target="ae3f8271-673d-4549-8f9b-46011b263dfc">
  <data key="d3">When the account value falls short of covering monthly deductions, the insurer notifies the policyholder at least 30 days prior to lapse, providing time to act. This pre-lapse notification precedes the final outcome described in fact_sentence_2, where non-payment during the grace period triggers actual policy lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
