<edge source="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311" target="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e">
  <data key="d3">A 61-day grace period allows reinstatement after missed premiums, independent of whether surrender charges would apply upon earlier cancellation. The existence of one does not affect the conditions of the other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311" target="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018">
  <data key="d3">A 61-day grace period allows policyholders time to pay overdue premiums before the policy lapses. This timeframe is independent of the annual surrender charge schedule beginning at 10% in Year 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311" target="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890">
  <data key="d3">The 61-day grace period allows policyholders time to pay overdue premiums without immediate lapse, independent of any surrender charges assessed if the policy were surrendered earlier. It has no bearing on the specific rate of the Year 2 surrender charge.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311" target="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b">
  <data key="d3">A 61-day grace period allows time to pay overdue premiums without immediate policy lapse, independent of any surrender charges assessed during earlier policy years like Year 3.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311" target="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332">
  <data key="d3">A 61-day grace period enables reinstatement of a lapsed policy due to missed payments, whereas the Year 4 surrender charge applies specifically to withdrawals made before the end of the 12-year window. Both relate to policy maintenance but operate under distinct conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311" target="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633">
  <data key="d3">A 61-day grace period allows reinstatement after missing a premium payment, independent of any surrender charges that may apply if the policyholder withdraws money before Year 12.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311" target="84b84dec-45b7-4ca8-ae2f-a68466866f24">
  <data key="d3">A 61-day grace period allows policyholders to reinstate coverage after missing a premium payment. This provision operates independently of the annual surrender charge reduction schedule described in Year 6.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311" target="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca">
  <data key="d3">A 61-day grace period allows time to pay overdue premiums without immediate policy lapse. This provision operates independently of the surrender charge schedule used when terminating the policy before maturity.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311" target="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75">
  <data key="d3">A 61-day grace period enables policyholders to restore coverage after missing payments, whereas the Year 8 surrender charge applies if the policyholder withdraws funds prematurely. These mechanisms serve distinct purposes in policy lifecycle management.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311" target="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00">
  <data key="d3">A 61-day grace period allows policyholders time to pay overdue premiums before the policy lapses. This provision operates independently of the surrender charge structure outlined earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">The 61-day grace period allows policyholders to avoid lapsing due to late payments, independent of any surrender charges that may apply later. It does not influence or relate directly to the calculation or existence of surrender charges in Year 10.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">A 61-day grace period allows policyholders to reinstate their policy after missing a premium payment. This timeline is independent of the surrender charge applicable in Year 11.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 61-day grace period allows policyholders time to catch up on overdue premiums without immediate lapse. This timing feature has no bearing on whether surrender charges remain active beyond Year 12.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">The 61-day grace period allows policyholders to reinstate coverage if they miss a payment, regardless of whether surrender charges apply. It operates independently of how those charges are calculated.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">A 61-day grace period enables reinstating a lapsed policy due to missed premiums, separate from how cash surrender value is computed based on account value and deductions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311" target="9d636a77-9852-432c-b8fb-7593d751a2da">
  <data key="d3">The 61-day grace period for reinstatement has no direct connection to the rules governing partial withdrawals.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311" target="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b">
  <data key="d3">A 61-day grace period enables reinstatement if premiums are unpaid, separate from withdrawal privileges that operate independently once the policy is active.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311" target="628900ad-3981-4384-be18-2669a41ba276">
  <data key="d3">A 61-day grace period allows time to pay overdue premiums without lapsing the policy, regardless of whether a no-lapse guarantee rider was elected.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311" target="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0">
  <data key="d3">A 61-day grace period enables reinstatement after a missed premium, independent of whether the No Lapse Guarantee Rider was selected. This provision applies regardless of riders chosen.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311" target="59735a62-be54-4b86-a006-cd569871d4ef">
  <data key="d3">A 61-day grace period allows policyholders to pay a sufficient premium to restore a lapsed policy, independent of whether the No Lapse Guarantee Rider was previously elected.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311" target="d4b10129-f843-43a5-8362-ff505e1fb13b">
  <data key="d3">The availability of a 61-day grace period compensates for the absence of a No Lapse Guarantee Rider by providing temporary relief to avoid policy termination when premiums are late.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY SAFETY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311" target="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872">
  <data key="d3">The 61-day grace period allows time to address payment issues, including cases where insufficient account value triggers a pre-lapse notification sent at least 30 days earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311" target="ae3f8271-673d-4549-8f9b-46011b263dfc">
  <data key="d3">A 61-day grace period allows policyholders time to pay overdue premiums. Failure to do so results in the policy lapsing.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311" target="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a">
  <data key="d3">If the 61-day grace period expires without payment, the policy lapses, leading to the forfeiture of any remaining surrender value.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
