</edge>
<edge source="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a" target="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e">
  <data key="d3">A policy lapse leads to forfeiture of the surrender value, meaning even if surrender charges were applicable earlier, those charges cannot be recovered post-lapse. This outcome underscores why timely surrender before lapse matters.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREVENTS_RECOVERY_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a" target="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses, any remaining surrender value—including amounts reduced by prior charges such as the 10% fee in Year 1—is completely forfeited, highlighting how early charges amplify financial loss upon termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a" target="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890">
  <data key="d3">Any remaining surrender value is forfeited upon policy lapse, regardless of prior surrender charges like the 9% fee in Year 2.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a" target="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses, any residual surrender value would have been diminished by prior-year surrender charges like the one applicable in Year 3, making it unlikely to recover significant funds.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES_LAPSE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a" target="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses, the holder loses any remaining surrender value, including amounts affected by prior-year charges like the one in Year 4.</data>
  <data key="d4">REDUCES VALUE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a" target="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses, any remaining surrender value—already diminished by prior surrender charges like the one in Year 5—is completely forfeited, making earlier charges consequential.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a" target="84b84dec-45b7-4ca8-ae2f-a68466866f24">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses, any remaining surrender value—including what would have been affected by a 5% charge—is forfeited, making prior surrender charges relevant to final payout outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a" target="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses, any residual surrender value—already diminished by the applicable surrender charge—is forfeited, making the prior existence of such charges relevant to the final payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES VALUE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a" target="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses, any remaining surrender value—including what would have been affected by prior surrender charges like the 3% in Year 8—is forfeited entirely.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a" target="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses, any residual surrender value—already diminished by prior surrender charges like the 2% in Year 9—is completely forfeited, meaning earlier charges contribute to eliminating potential payouts.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses, any residual surrender value is forfeited regardless of prior surrender charges. Even if the charge was small in Year 10, such as 1%, the entire account balance may still be lost unless withdrawn earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses due to unpaid premiums, any residual surrender value—affected by prior-year charges like those in Year 11—is completely forfeited.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses, its benefits—including any accumulated surrender value—are lost, even though surrender charges have already been reduced to 0% by Year 12. Thus, maintaining premium payments ensures access to the full account value post-Year 12.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">The forfeiture of surrender value after lapse underscores why understanding how surrender charges are applied matters—they determine what remains at risk when a policy terminates.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses, the previously computed Cash Surrender Value is lost entirely. This outcome directly follows from the definition that accounts for surrender charges and loans when determining the value.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a" target="9d636a77-9852-432c-b8fb-7593d751a2da">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses, any unused surrender value is lost, meaning prior partial withdrawals—though permissible—are subject to final loss if the policy fails to stay current.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a" target="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b">
  <data key="d3">The forfeiture of surrender value after policy lapse negates the ability to access funds via free partial withdrawals, making such withdrawals impossible post-lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a" target="628900ad-3981-4384-be18-2669a41ba276">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses without a no-lapse guarantee rider being active, the holder loses any accumulated surrender value. Since the rider was not elected, this scenario applies, making its absence relevant to the final loss.</data>
  <data key="d4">NOT_ELECTED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a" target="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses—especially when no No Lapse Guarantee Rider is active—the policyholder loses access to any remaining surrender value. This outcome contrasts with what would happen under an active rider, which would prevent lapse regardless of account balance.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON_RIDER</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a" target="59735a62-be54-4b86-a006-cd569871d4ef">
  <data key="d3">The forfeiture of surrender value upon policy lapse implies that maintaining coverage through riders like the No Lapse Guarantee is essential to preserve financial benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES_FORFEITURE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a" target="d4b10129-f843-43a5-8362-ff505e1fb13b">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses—especially without a No Lapse Guarantee Rider—the surrender value is forfeited, highlighting the consequence of not selecting such protection.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a" target="f693b3ab-ce04-4645-b10b-f2a647d0f872">
  <data key="d3">A policy lapse occurs if payments or account balances fail to sustain coverage. After such lapse, any residual surrender value is permanently lost, even if earlier warnings were issued.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a" target="12268e1c-c5d6-4433-beca-c792fd3b6311">
  <data key="d3">A 61-day grace period exists specifically to prevent policy lapse, thereby preserving the surrender value if premiums are paid within that window.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a" target="ae3f8271-673d-4549-8f9b-46011b263dfc">
  <data key="d3">The forfeiture of the remaining surrender value occurs only after the policy has lapsed due to non-payment beyond the grace period. This outcome depends on the prior event of policy lapse caused by missed payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a" target="e27b0a94-4088-4246-ba72-d6793b6cd04d">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 61-day grace period prevents immediate forfeiture of the surrender value upon late payment, allowing policyholders time to restore the policy before lapsing occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a" target="15cc61a2-a432-4cb5-8906-a25d63f7e7f6">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 asserts that a lapsed policy results in loss of surrender value, while fact_sentence_2 claims it is paid out—creating a direct conflict on post-lapse financial outcome.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONFLICTS_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a" target="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b">
  <data key="d3">The forfeiture of surrender value occurs when a policy lapses due to unpaid premiums beyond the grace period, making the outcome in fact_sentence_1 contingent on the event described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="95a26d1b-74dc-4dec-892b-da3110b604f2" target="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
