<edge source="c929a946-29b9-4878-9e8b-1320d6fdb4af" target="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 offers no relevant context about the grace period or payment timeline; thus, it cannot explain or relate to the lapsed status described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c929a946-29b9-4878-9e8b-1320d6fdb4af" target="15cc61a2-a432-4cb5-8906-a25d63f7e7f6">
  <data key="d3">The policy lapses immediately upon failure to pay, triggering the release of any remaining surrender value to the holder.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c929a946-29b9-4878-9e8b-1320d6fdb4af" target="e27b0a94-4088-4246-ba72-d6793b6cd04d">
  <data key="d3">The statement that the policy lapses 0 days before lapse indicates immediate termination, leaving no room for action. This contrasts with the grace period provision, which would allow reinstatement only if the lapse were imminent but not yet final.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRADICTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c929a946-29b9-4878-9e8b-1320d6fdb4af" target="f059bbb2-2661-4ab8-9504-a5a0a25687f5">
  <data key="d3">The policy's immediate lapse upon non-payment sets the stage for potential claims during active coverage, but this particular scenario does not affect the outcome described in fact_sentence_2 regarding suicide-related payouts.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c929a946-29b9-4878-9e8b-1320d6fdb4af" target="d95da1e8-f071-414b-b0ad-9b56d2f0e759">
  <data key="d3">The statement about the policy lapsing immediately lacks connection to the explanation regarding index participation and stock ownership. The first concerns administrative consequences of non-payment; the second explains structural features of indexed components.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c929a946-29b9-4878-9e8b-1320d6fdb4af" target="6e42de55-cde0-435f-b499-10c6b12172e2">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence discusses the timeline for policy lapse, though its wording is self-contradictory and semantically invalid. This has no bearing on whether the policy qualifies as a securities product.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c929a946-29b9-4878-9e8b-1320d6fdb4af" target="66d61507-a301-4354-ad15-acfad1eafccb">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s immediate lapse prevents any possibility of reinstatement, rendering the suicide benefit provision ineffective because reinstatement cannot occur.</data>
  <data key="d4">INVALIDATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c929a946-29b9-4878-9e8b-1320d6fdb4af" target="2ec53e58-1461-418f-af0f-33f4dab5f971">
  <data key="d3">The statement about the policy lapsing immediately after missing payment relates to administrative consequences of nonpayment, whereas the explanation about index participation highlights how returns are calculated without actual fund ownership. The two do not influence each other logically.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c929a946-29b9-4878-9e8b-1320d6fdb4af" target="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3">
  <data key="d3">The statement about the policy lapsing 0 days before lapse describes a procedural timeline issue but does not relate to how dividend calculations affect index performance.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c929a946-29b9-4878-9e8b-1320d6fdb4af" target="1fb961d9-6574-4554-b263-906d75b3f515">
  <data key="d3">The statement about the policy lapsing immediately highlights enforcement of non-renewal due to unpaid premiums, while the second sentence outlines a separate regulatory safeguard against fraudulent applications within the initial two-year window. The two facts pertain to unrelated triggers for policy invalidation.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c929a946-29b9-4878-9e8b-1320d6fdb4af" target="a6b58496-e890-407d-99f3-f8e86cce69dd">
  <data key="d3">The statement about the policy lapsing 0 days before lapse appears to describe a technical timing issue without connection to how cap rates might change annually.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c929a946-29b9-4878-9e8b-1320d6fdb4af" target="b080d9ad-b053-459f-8150-83b862b99de1">
  <data key="d3">The claim about the policy lapsing "0 days before lapse" appears self-referential and semantically unclear, offering no meaningful connection to the technical assurance regarding minimum guaranteed cap rates.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c929a946-29b9-4878-9e8b-1320d6fdb4af" target="09f59f75-d8f5-4cf9-b763-8e9b77770ca0">
  <data key="d3">The statement about the policy lapsing 0 days before lapse contradicts the established 61-day grace period, suggesting immediate termination despite available recovery time. This does not relate to how fixed account rates might change annually.</data>
