<edge source="e27b0a94-4088-4246-ba72-d6793b6cd04d" target="c929a946-29b9-4878-9e8b-1320d6fdb4af">
  <data key="d3">The 61-day grace period enables reinstatement after a missed payment, assuming the policy hasn't fully lapsed. However, since the policy has already lapsed with no grace period remaining, this option is no longer available.</data>
  <data key="d4">IRRELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e27b0a94-4088-4246-ba72-d6793b6cd04d" target="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b">
  <data key="d3">A 61-day grace period provides opportunity to restore coverage through premium payment; failure to do so results in policy lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e27b0a94-4088-4246-ba72-d6793b6cd04d" target="f059bbb2-2661-4ab8-9504-a5a0a25687f5">
  <data key="d3">The grace period provides time to restore coverage post-payment default, while the suicide exclusion defines benefits upon death during the initial two-year period regardless of reinstatement status.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e27b0a94-4088-4246-ba72-d6793b6cd04d" target="6e42de55-cde0-435f-b499-10c6b12172e2">
  <data key="d3">The grace period provision enables reinstatement of coverage upon late payment, independent of whether the policy qualifies as a securities product.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e27b0a94-4088-4246-ba72-d6793b6cd04d" target="15cc61a2-a432-4cb5-8906-a25d63f7e7f6">
  <data key="d3">If the policyholder pays the required premium within the 61-day grace period, the policy remains active. However, failure to make such a payment results in lapse, triggering the release of the surrender value.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e27b0a94-4088-4246-ba72-d6793b6cd04d" target="1fb961d9-6574-4554-b263-906d75b3f515">
  <data key="d3">The grace period provides time to restore coverage post-payment default, but it does not influence the insurer’s ability to challenge claims based on misrepresentation during the initial two-year contestability period.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e27b0a94-4088-4246-ba72-d6793b6cd04d" target="66d61507-a301-4354-ad15-acfad1eafccb">
  <data key="d3">The grace period provides a window to reinstate the policy, making reinstatement possible; once reinstated, the suicide exclusion becomes active, limiting benefits if suicide occurs within two years.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e27b0a94-4088-4246-ba72-d6793b6cd04d" target="d95da1e8-f071-414b-b0ad-9b56d2f0e759">
  <data key="d3">The grace period enables reinstatement via timely payment but has no bearing on how index-linked features function. This sentence explains administrative flexibility in maintaining coverage, unrelated to investment structure.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
