  <data key="d3">Without timely payment during the 61-day grace period, the policy lapses, resulting in the complete forfeiture of any remaining surrender value.</data>
  <data key="d4">LEADS_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e27b0a94-4088-4246-ba72-d6793b6cd04d" target="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225">
  <data key="d3">The 61-day grace period enables reinstatement after missed premiums, preserving policy validity; this contrasts with partial withdrawals under Option 1, which permanently reduce the death benefit regardless of reinstatement actions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e27b0a94-4088-4246-ba72-d6793b6cd04d" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">A 61-day grace period prevents immediate lapse after missed premiums, reducing urgency to draw loans—but if the policy remains inactive beyond it, any existing loans still reduce the eventual death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
