<edge source="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b" target="c929a946-29b9-4878-9e8b-1320d6fdb4af">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 explains when the policy lapses based on non-receipt of premiums during the grace period, but this explanation stands independently without needing clarification from fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b" target="e27b0a94-4088-4246-ba72-d6793b6cd04d">
  <data key="d3">Failure to make a required premium payment within the 61-day grace period leads to the policy's lapse, negating any chance of reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b" target="15cc61a2-a432-4cb5-8906-a25d63f7e7f6">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence establishes that missing payment during the grace period causes policy lapse. The second claims that upon lapse, the surrender value is paid out—but this directly contradicts the chunk summary’s assertion that the surrender value is forfeited when payment isn't made.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRADICTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b" target="66d61507-a301-4354-ad15-acfad1eafccb">
  <data key="d3">The failure to pay within the grace period leads to policy lapse, but even if reinstated later, certain claims like suicide-related payouts remain restricted based on timing rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b" target="f059bbb2-2661-4ab8-9504-a5a0a25687f5">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence concerns policy termination due to unpaid premiums after the grace period. The second discusses benefits available when suicide occurs within two years of policy issuance. These topics pertain to separate policy provisions and do not influence one another.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b" target="2ec53e58-1461-418f-af0f-33f4dab5f971">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence concerns policy termination due to unpaid premiums, while the second clarifies how index-based benefits are structurally implemented without actual fund ownership. The topics do not intersect logically.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b" target="d95da1e8-f071-414b-b0ad-9b56d2f0e759">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence concerns policy termination due to unpaid premiums, while the second clarifies how index-based growth mechanisms work without stock ownership. The topics are unrelated in context and function.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b" target="6e42de55-cde0-435f-b499-10c6b12172e2">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence outlines the financial consequence of failing to pay premiums within the grace period, resulting in policy termination. The second sentence clarifies the regulatory classification of the product as non-securities, unrelated to payment timelines or lapsation rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b" target="1fb961d9-6574-4554-b263-906d75b3f515">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay premiums within the 61-day grace period results in policy lapse, which could prevent any benefits from being paid—even if the cause were later found to involve a material misrepresentation under the contestability clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b" target="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence outlines the penalty for failing to pay premiums on time, resulting in policy termination. The second sentence clarifies how index-based performance is calculated by excluding certain dividend elements.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b" target="a6b58496-e890-407d-99f3-f8e86cce69dd">
  <data key="d3">The failure to pay premiums within the grace period results in policy lapse, independent of any changes in cap rates. Cap rate fluctuations occur separately and do not influence the timing or outcome of premium delinquency.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b" target="7e3f4dce-a967-443e-8c1e-f4c1a24f502c">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence outlines the condition under which a policy terminates due to non-payment. The second sentence explains that participation rates, affecting potential returns, can vary yearly, independent of lapse rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b" target="b080d9ad-b053-459f-8150-83b862b99de1">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence outlines the condition under which the policy terminates due to non-payment. The second sentence explains a safeguard protecting against declining interest caps, independent of payment status.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b" target="a416fa11-2b3f-4f38-958d-ff8e13bcbb1a">
  <data key="d3">The failure to pay premiums within the grace period results in policy lapse, but this does not affect the guarantee of minimum participation rates. The policy’s structural protections remain intact even upon lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b" target="09f59f75-d8f5-4cf9-b763-8e9b77770ca0">
  <data key="d3">The failure to pay premiums within the grace period results in policy lapse, independent of any changes to fixed account interest rates. The timing of a lapse is unaffected by whether fixed rates increase or decrease annually.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b" target="af34274c-dfee-4fb4-a491-3e2e93de0364">
  <data key="d3">The failure to pay premiums within the grace period results in policy lapse, affecting coverage continuity. This does not impact the guarantee that fixed account rates remain above minimum thresholds.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b" target="4323367b-0222-42cb-99fe-8a2785ec96d3">
  <data key="d3">The failure to make a timely premium payment results in policy lapse, but this outcome has no bearing on whether dividends are paid when the index performs poorly.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b" target="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069">
  <data key="d3">The failure to pay premiums within the grace period results in policy termination, but this does not affect the guarantee of no losses from negative index performance.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b" target="5ba693f1-db68-45ea-a535-eef1cf763796">
  <data key="d3">The failure to pay premiums within the grace period leads to policy lapse, emphasizing financial responsibility. This contrasts with the separate principle that past index performance cannot ensure future gains, highlighting caution against over-reliance on historical data.</data>
  <data key="d4">IRRELEVANT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b" target="b1733959-f2c8-49a1-abbf-c49d75d321d4">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence outlines a policy termination condition based on non-payment during the grace period. The second sentence offers general customer service contact details, which do not relate to the financial or procedural consequences described earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b" target="47fe3387-29bc-4869-a3a5-637bc22b6a91">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s automatic lapse after the grace period underscores the importance of timely premiums, while the mention of “zero” as the hero highlights built-in safeguards against loss, reinforcing the idea that the policy protects against worst-case scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d4">THEMATIC SUPPORT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b" target="87987c98-b6f9-450a-8c71-84809999dd2b">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence outlines a key policy term regarding lapse conditions due to non-payment. The second sentence offers general contact information for the insurer, which does not relate to the operational consequences described in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b" target="ca17e9e7-d97b-4fc9-973c-68dc1b6b96e8">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence outlines a financial condition related to policy continuation based on timely premiums. The second sentence provides administrative context about where the contract was signed, unrelated to the financial consequences described earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b" target="1b5bac8e-3dbc-4701-8ee4-2896a945787f">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence outlines a condition under which the policy terminates due to non-payment. The second sentence identifies the individual responsible for authorizing the document but does not relate to any operational or contractual outcome tied to payment timelines.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b" target="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay premiums within the 61-day grace period leads to policy lapse, resulting in the loss of any remaining surrender value, as stated in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b" target="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225">
  <data key="d3">A lapsed policy prevents any future partial withdrawals since the contract terminates; thus, even though withdrawals would otherwise reduce the death benefit, they cannot occur post-lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECONDITION_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">A lapsed policy prevents any death benefit payout, rendering outstanding loans irrelevant since there’s no claimable benefit. However, if the policy stays active despite loans, those debts still reduce the payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
