<edge source="1fb961d9-6574-4554-b263-906d75b3f515" target="c929a946-29b9-4878-9e8b-1320d6fdb4af">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a two-year contestability clause means insurers can challenge claims due to misrepresentation early in the policy term, independent of whether the policy has lapsed due to non-payment. This does not affect nor depend on the specific timing of lapse described in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1fb961d9-6574-4554-b263-906d75b3f515" target="e27b0a94-4088-4246-ba72-d6793b6cd04d">
  <data key="d3">The two-year contestability clause enables the insurer to investigate and deny benefits due to misrepresentation at issuance, regardless of whether the policy was reinstated via the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1fb961d9-6574-4554-b263-906d75b3f515" target="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b">
  <data key="d3">During the first two years, insurers retain the right to contest claims due to misrepresentation, but only if the policy remains active; otherwise, it would have already lapsed due to non-payment before such challenges arise.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1fb961d9-6574-4554-b263-906d75b3f515" target="15cc61a2-a432-4cb5-8906-a25d63f7e7f6">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a contestability period for misrepresentation has no bearing on whether the surrender value is returned when the policy lapses.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1fb961d9-6574-4554-b263-906d75b3f515" target="f059bbb2-2661-4ab8-9504-a5a0a25687f5">
  <data key="d3">The insurer’s ability to contest misrepresentations applies within the first two years, overlapping temporally with the suicide exclusion, though it pertains to fraud rather than intent. The existence of one does not affect the operation of the other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1fb961d9-6574-4554-b263-906d75b3f515" target="66d61507-a301-4354-ad15-acfad1eafccb">
  <data key="d3">During the initial two years from the issue date, insurers can challenge claims due to material misrepresentations. Even if a suicide occurs within two years of reinstatement, such a claim might still be contested if earlier misstatements were discovered.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1fb961d9-6574-4554-b263-906d75b3f515" target="6e42de55-cde0-435f-b499-10c6b12172e2">
  <data key="d3">The contestability clause governs claims eligibility based on misstatements at application; it does not influence whether the policy qualifies as a securities product.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1fb961d9-6574-4554-b263-906d75b3f515" target="d95da1e8-f071-414b-b0ad-9b56d2f0e759">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a contestability clause for misrepresentation does not influence how index participation works. This statement provides information about claim validity based on honesty at application but has no bearing on whether stock ownership is involved in indexing mechanisms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1fb961d9-6574-4554-b263-906d75b3f515" target="2ec53e58-1461-418f-af0f-33f4dab5f971">
  <data key="d3">The contestability clause limits claims based on misrepresentation in early policy life but has no bearing on how index participation works. This statement stands independently regarding policy validity rather than financial mechanism.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1fb961d9-6574-4554-b263-906d75b3f515" target="7e3f4dce-a967-443e-8c1e-f4c1a24f502c">
  <data key="d3">The contestability clause limits claims based on misrepresentation in the initial two years but does not influence annual adjustments to participation rates.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1fb961d9-6574-4554-b263-906d75b3f515" target="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a contestability clause does not affect how dividends are treated in index performance calculations. The two provisions operate independently within different sections of the policy’s terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1fb961d9-6574-4554-b263-906d75b3f515" target="a6b58496-e890-407d-99f3-f8e86cce69dd">
  <data key="d3">The contestability clause prevents payouts due to misrepresentation in the initial two years but does not influence how cap rates evolve over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1fb961d9-6574-4554-b263-906d75b3f515" target="09f59f75-d8f5-4cf9-b763-8e9b77770ca0">
  <data key="d3">The contestability clause applies only to claims arising from material misrepresentation within the first two years; it does not influence how fixed account rates are adjusted annually.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1fb961d9-6574-4554-b263-906d75b3f515" target="a416fa11-2b3f-4f38-958d-ff8e13bcbb1a">
  <data key="d3">The contestability clause regarding material misrepresentation does not influence or relate to the guarantee of minimum participation rates. They operate independently within distinct sections of the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1fb961d9-6574-4554-b263-906d75b3f515" target="af34274c-dfee-4fb4-a491-3e2e93de0364">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a contestability clause does not influence or relate to the guaranteed floor on fixed account rates. The two clauses operate independently within distinct sections of the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1fb961d9-6574-4554-b263-906d75b3f515" target="b080d9ad-b053-459f-8150-83b862b99de1">
  <data key="d3">The contestability clause allows the insurer to challenge claims based on misrepresentation within the first two years, but it does not affect how rate caps are determined or protected by guaranteed floors.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1fb961d9-6574-4554-b263-906d75b3f515" target="5ba693f1-db68-45ea-a535-eef1cf763796">
  <data key="d3">The contestability clause allows the insurer to challenge claims based on misrepresentation in the initial two years, reinforcing the need for accurate information at application. This supports broader disclosure principles, such as cautioning against relying on historical data when assessing future benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">DISCLOSURE_SUPPORT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1fb961d9-6574-4554-b263-906d75b3f515" target="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069">
  <data key="d3">The contestability clause limits claims based on misrepresentation in the initial two years but does not relate to investment performance safeguards.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1fb961d9-6574-4554-b263-906d75b3f515" target="b1733959-f2c8-49a1-abbf-c49d75d321d4">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence outlines a time-bound exclusion regarding claims due to false statements at application. The second sentence gives general contact details for the company, which does not relate to the enforcement or scope of the contestability clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
