<edge source="1fb961d9-6574-4554-b263-906d75b3f515" target="47fe3387-29bc-4869-a3a5-637bc22b6a91">
  <data key="d3">The contestability clause limits claims based on misrepresentation early in the policy term, while the mention of 'zero' as the hero highlights the absence of loss from market downturns. Both reflect safeguards against financial risk, though through distinct mechanisms.</data>
