<edge source="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3" target="c929a946-29b9-4878-9e8b-1320d6fdb4af">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of dividends from index component calculations pertains to investment valuation methods and has no bearing on when the policy lapses.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3" target="e27b0a94-4088-4246-ba72-d6793b6cd04d">
  <data key="d3">Index-based performance calculations exclude dividends from index components, regardless of whether a policy is being reinstated during a grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3" target="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence defines a technical aspect of index performance computation by omitting dividends from component indices. This has no bearing on whether a policy lapses due to unpaid premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3" target="15cc61a2-a432-4cb5-8906-a25d63f7e7f6">
  <data key="d3">The second statement clarifies that dividends are not part of index performance, whereas the first describes what happens to the surrender value at lapse. No connection exists between the treatment of dividends and the handling of surrendered funds.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3" target="f059bbb2-2661-4ab8-9504-a5a0a25687f5">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence explains that dividends from index elements are excluded from performance metrics. This has no bearing on the payout rules described in the first sentence regarding suicide-related claims.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3" target="66d61507-a301-4354-ad15-acfad1eafccb">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence clarifies that index performance does not include dividends from index components. This detail is unrelated to the suicide exclusion described in the first sentence regarding benefit amounts.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3" target="1fb961d9-6574-4554-b263-906d75b3f515">
  <data key="d3">Information about excluded dividends has no bearing on whether the insurer can contest claims based on misrepresentation. They relate to separate policy mechanisms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3" target="6e42de55-cde0-435f-b499-10c6b12172e2">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of dividends from index performance calculations supports transparency about how gains are measured, reinforcing that the product operates outside traditional investment vehicles such as securities.</data>
  <data key="d4">NOT RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3" target="d95da1e8-f071-414b-b0ad-9b56d2f0e759">
  <data key="d3">Since dividends from index constituents are explicitly omitted from index performance, it reinforces that investors aren't gaining exposure through dividend income—which aligns with the absence of direct stock ownership mentioned in fact sentence 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">REINFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3" target="2ec53e58-1461-418f-af0f-33f4dab5f971">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of dividends from index component performance aligns with the lack of direct ownership of index funds, reinforcing that investors do not gain benefits tied to equity distributions even when participating in index movements.</data>
  <data key="d4">RELATED_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3" target="7e3f4dce-a967-443e-8c1e-f4c1a24f502c">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of dividends from index performance does not impact how annual participation rates may fluctuate; they operate independently within the policy's indexing mechanics.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3" target="b080d9ad-b053-459f-8150-83b862b99de1">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of dividends from index performance does not affect the guarantee of minimum cap rates, which remain protected regardless of dividend treatment.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3" target="09f59f75-d8f5-4cf9-b763-8e9b77770ca0">
  <data key="d3">The statement about excluded dividends relates to how index performance is calculated, independent of any fixed account rate adjustments. Fixed account rates changing annually does not affect or depend on whether dividends are included in index returns.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3" target="a6b58496-e890-407d-99f3-f8e86cce69dd">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of dividends from index performance affects how gains are measured, while changing cap rates determine the upper limit of those gains each year. Together, they shape investor understanding of expected returns but operate independently.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3" target="a416fa11-2b3f-4f38-958d-ff8e13bcbb1a">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of dividends from index performance does not impact the guarantee of minimum participation rates, which remain protected regardless of dividend treatment.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_EFFECT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3" target="af34274c-dfee-4fb4-a491-3e2e93de0364">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence explains that dividends from index parts aren't part of index performance metrics. The second states that fixed account interest rates cannot drop below guaranteed levels. These relate to separate financial mechanisms without direct interaction.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3" target="5ba693f1-db68-45ea-a535-eef1cf763796">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of dividends from index performance calculations means investors should not assume higher returns simply because dividends exist. This reinforces the broader caution that even comprehensive historical data cannot ensure future success.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3" target="b1733959-f2c8-49a1-abbf-c49d75d321d4">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 explains that dividends from index components are excluded from index performance calculations. This detail is independent of the contact information provided in fact sentence 2.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3" target="47fe3387-29bc-4869-a3a5-637bc22b6a91">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of dividends from index performance reinforces the stability of guaranteed returns, supporting the notion that zero loss potential makes “zero” a protective feature in the policy’s design.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3" target="4323367b-0222-42cb-99fe-8a2785ec96d3">
  <data key="d3">Since dividends from index components are excluded from performance calculations, they cannot contribute to gains even when the index declines, resulting in no dividend participation during negative market periods.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3" target="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of dividends from index component calculations affects how performance is measured, but does not impact the guarantee against losses from negative index moves, which remains intact regardless of dividend treatment.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3" target="ca17e9e7-d97b-4fc9-973c-68dc1b6b96e8">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains that dividends from index components do not affect index performance metrics. This information has no bearing on where the policy was signed.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3" target="1b5bac8e-3dbc-4701-8ee4-2896a945787f">
  <data key="d3">The statement about excluded dividends relates to how index performance is calculated but has no bearing on the identity or role of the signatory.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3" target="87987c98-b6f9-450a-8c71-84809999dd2b">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence explains how index performance is calculated by omitting dividends. This has no bearing on the second sentence, which simply lists the insurer's website for contacting support.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
