  <data key="d3">Annual changes to cap rates relate to interest rate mechanisms and do not influence or explain the specific timing of policy lapse described in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6b58496-e890-407d-99f3-f8e86cce69dd" target="e27b0a94-4088-4246-ba72-d6793b6cd04d">
  <data key="d3">Annual changes in cap rates do not influence the duration or conditions of the 61-day grace period for reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6b58496-e890-407d-99f3-f8e86cce69dd" target="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b">
  <data key="d3">Annual changes in cap rates reflect shifts in guaranteed interest limits, unrelated to whether premiums were paid during the grace period. The policy’s lapse depends solely on payment status, not on rate adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6b58496-e890-407d-99f3-f8e86cce69dd" target="15cc61a2-a432-4cb5-8906-a25d63f7e7f6">
  <data key="d3">Annual adjustments to cap rates are independent of whether a surrendered value is paid out upon policy lapse, as they pertain to interest rate caps rather than cash settlement terms.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6b58496-e890-407d-99f3-f8e86cce69dd" target="f059bbb2-2661-4ab8-9504-a5a0a25687f5">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence explains that cap rates governing index-based gains can vary yearly. This feature has no bearing on the calculation of benefits in cases of suicide during the initial two-year period described in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6b58496-e890-407d-99f3-f8e86cce69dd" target="66d61507-a301-4354-ad15-acfad1eafccb">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence explains that cap rates can vary yearly, affecting index-linked benefits. This has no bearing on the conditions surrounding suicide-related claims described in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6b58496-e890-407d-99f3-f8e86cce69dd" target="1fb961d9-6574-4554-b263-906d75b3f515">
  <data key="d3">Annual adjustments to cap rates affect potential returns on the policy’s indexed component but have no bearing on whether the insurer can contest claims based on misrepresentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6b58496-e890-407d-99f3-f8e86cce69dd" target="6e42de55-cde0-435f-b499-10c6b12172e2">
  <data key="d3">Annual changes in cap rates reflect dynamic feature of the policy's indexing mechanism; however, this operational detail has no bearing on whether the product qualifies as a security.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6b58496-e890-407d-99f3-f8e86cce69dd" target="d95da1e8-f071-414b-b0ad-9b56d2f0e759">
  <data key="d3">Annual changes in cap rates depend on the underlying mechanics of index participation, which do not include actual stock ownership, meaning rate adjustments reflect contractual terms rather than investment behavior.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6b58496-e890-407d-99f3-f8e86cce69dd" target="2ec53e58-1461-418f-af0f-33f4dab5f971">
  <data key="d3">Annual changes in cap rates affect the maximum return possible on index-linked growth. This operational detail stands separately from the clarification that participants don't own underlying index funds directly.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6b58496-e890-407d-99f3-f8e86cce69dd" target="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3">
  <data key="d3">Annual adjustment of cap rates influences the ceiling on returns, whereas excluding dividends ensures consistency in index measurement. These elements jointly inform return mechanics without mutual dependency.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6b58496-e890-407d-99f3-f8e86cce69dd" target="7e3f4dce-a967-443e-8c1e-f4c1a24f502c">
  <data key="d3">Cap rates determine the maximum interest rate applied to account gains, while participation rates define what percentage of those gains are credited to the policy. Both are subject to yearly adjustment based on underlying index performance and insurer discretion.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_ADJUSTED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6b58496-e890-407d-99f3-f8e86cce69dd" target="09f59f75-d8f5-4cf9-b763-8e9b77770ca0">
  <data key="d3">Cap rates changing annually affect the upper limit of returns in indexed accounts, whereas fixed account rates determine guaranteed returns regardless of market conditions. These are parallel mechanisms governing different parts of the policy's growth potential.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY ADJUSTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6b58496-e890-407d-99f3-f8e86cce69dd" target="b080d9ad-b053-459f-8150-83b862b99de1">
  <data key="d3">The possibility of annual changes in cap rates is bounded by a guarantee that they will not fall below certain minimum levels, ensuring predictable limits on rate reductions.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6b58496-e890-407d-99f3-f8e86cce69dd" target="a416fa11-2b3f-4f38-958d-ff8e13bcbb1a">
  <data key="d3">Cap rates may vary yearly, but participation rates remain safeguarded by guaranteed floors, ensuring consistent member benefits regardless of market volatility.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6b58496-e890-407d-99f3-f8e86cce69dd" target="af34274c-dfee-4fb4-a491-3e2e93de0364">
  <data key="d3">Cap rates being subject to annual adjustment reflects market responsiveness, while the guarantee of minimum fixed account rates offers protection against decline regardless of such changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6b58496-e890-407d-99f3-f8e86cce69dd" target="5ba693f1-db68-45ea-a535-eef1cf763796">
  <data key="d3">Cap rates changing annually reflects ongoing adjustments in return limits, but this does not imply anything about whether past performance predicts future outcomes, which remains independent.</data>
  <data key="d4">UNRELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6b58496-e890-407d-99f3-f8e86cce69dd" target="47fe3387-29bc-4869-a3a5-637bc22b6a91">
  <data key="d3">Changes in cap rates affect how benefits are calculated over time, but the emphasis on "zero" as protective reflects confidence in the policy’s design against market downturns.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUALIZES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6b58496-e890-407d-99f3-f8e86cce69dd" target="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069">
  <data key="d3">Changes in cap rates affect how much interest can accrue but do not influence whether the policy guarantees no losses from negative index performance.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
