  <data key="d3">Annual adjustment of fixed account rates has no bearing on the grace period or the consequences of non-payment, such as policy lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09f59f75-d8f5-4cf9-b763-8e9b77770ca0" target="15cc61a2-a432-4cb5-8906-a25d63f7e7f6">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence notes that fixed account rates are subject to annual adjustment. This has no bearing on whether the surrender value is paid out upon lapse, which is governed by different terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09f59f75-d8f5-4cf9-b763-8e9b77770ca0" target="f059bbb2-2661-4ab8-9504-a5a0a25687f5">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence explains that fixed account rates are subject to annual adjustment, whereas the first sentence defines benefits payable upon suicide within two years. The topics pertain to different policy features and do not influence each other.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09f59f75-d8f5-4cf9-b763-8e9b77770ca0" target="66d61507-a301-4354-ad15-acfad1eafccb">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence explains that fixed account rates are subject to annual review and adjustment. This does not influence or relate to the payout terms specified in the first sentence regarding suicide benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09f59f75-d8f5-4cf9-b763-8e9b77770ca0" target="1fb961d9-6574-4554-b263-906d75b3f515">
  <data key="d3">Annual adjustment of fixed account rates has no bearing on the insurer’s ability to contest claims based on material misrepresentation during the initial two-year period.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09f59f75-d8f5-4cf9-b763-8e9b77770ca0" target="6e42de55-cde0-435f-b499-10c6b12172e2">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 explains that fixed account rates can adjust annually, reflecting variable rate features. This detail stands independently from fact sentence 1’s assertion about the policy not being a securities product, as rate adjustments do not affect its regulatory classification.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09f59f75-d8f5-4cf9-b763-8e9b77770ca0" target="d95da1e8-f071-414b-b0ad-9b56d2f0e759">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 states that fixed account interest rates can vary yearly. This statement is unrelated to how index participation works or whether it involves stock ownership.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09f59f75-d8f5-4cf9-b763-8e9b77770ca0" target="2ec53e58-1461-418f-af0f-33f4dab5f971">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 notes annual changes in fixed account rates, reflecting potential shifts in guaranteed returns. Fact sentence 1 clarifies that index-linked gains don't come from actual fund ownership. The two statements describe independent elements of the policy's financial framework with no mutual dependence.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09f59f75-d8f5-4cf9-b763-8e9b77770ca0" target="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3">
  <data key="d3">Annual changes in fixed account rates occur regardless of dividend treatment in index performance. The inclusion or exclusion of dividends has no bearing on the frequency or possibility of rate revisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09f59f75-d8f5-4cf9-b763-8e9b77770ca0" target="a6b58496-e890-407d-99f3-f8e86cce69dd">
  <data key="d3">Fixed account rates adjusting yearly set the baseline guaranteed return, distinct from cap rates that govern capped gains in indexed accounts. Both reflect periodic recalibrations but operate independently within separate investment structures.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY ADJUSTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09f59f75-d8f5-4cf9-b763-8e9b77770ca0" target="7e3f4dce-a967-443e-8c1e-f4c1a24f502c">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 states that fixed account rates, offering stable returns, are subject to annual review. These changes might affect policyholders’ expectations when compared to fluctuating participation rates.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09f59f75-d8f5-4cf9-b763-8e9b77770ca0" target="af34274c-dfee-4fb4-a491-3e2e93de0364">
  <data key="d3">The possibility of annual rate changes is limited by a floor set by guaranteed minimums, preventing any decline below those levels.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09f59f75-d8f5-4cf9-b763-8e9b77770ca0" target="a416fa11-2b3f-4f38-958d-ff8e13bcbb1a">
  <data key="d3">The possibility of annual adjustments to fixed account rates coexists with the guarantee that participation rates won't drop below set minimums, ensuring predictable performance floors despite variable interest conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09f59f75-d8f5-4cf9-b763-8e9b77770ca0" target="5ba693f1-db68-45ea-a535-eef1cf763796">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that fixed account rates are subject to annual changes, reflecting potential volatility in guaranteed returns. This contrasts with fact sentence 2, which cautions that prior index performance cannot ensure future gains, emphasizing broader market uncertainty.</data>
  <data key="d4">NOT RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09f59f75-d8f5-4cf9-b763-8e9b77770ca0" target="47fe3387-29bc-4869-a3a5-637bc22b6a91">
  <data key="d3">The mention of fluctuating fixed account rates relates to investment volatility, while describing 'zero' as the hero highlights the safety net against losses. Together, they underscore design elements focused on protecting principal despite market fluctuations.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09f59f75-d8f5-4cf9-b763-8e9b77770ca0" target="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069">
  <data key="d3">The possibility of changing fixed account rates reflects adjustments in guaranteed returns over time, while the zero-loss guarantee protects against downturns in indexed components. Together, they highlight design elements ensuring predictable growth and risk limitation.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
