<edge source="47fe3387-29bc-4869-a3a5-637bc22b6a91" target="c929a946-29b9-4878-9e8b-1320d6fdb4af">
  <data key="d3">The idea that “zero” is heroic refers to the absence of financial loss due to market downturns, consistent with the document's emphasis on guaranteed minimums. This concept has no bearing on the nonsensical assertion about lapse timing in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="47fe3387-29bc-4869-a3a5-637bc22b6a91" target="e27b0a94-4088-4246-ba72-d6793b6cd04d">
  <data key="d3">Describing 'zero' as the hero underscores the absence of downside risk, which complements the practical safeguard offered by the 61-day grace period in preserving policyholder protections.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="47fe3387-29bc-4869-a3a5-637bc22b6a91" target="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b">
  <data key="d3">Describing “zero” as the hero reflects the policy's feature of eliminating downside risk from market fluctuations, which complements the structural safeguard of allowing reinstatement during the grace period before full lapse occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL ENHANCEMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="47fe3387-29bc-4869-a3a5-637bc22b6a91" target="15cc61a2-a432-4cb5-8906-a25d63f7e7f6">
  <data key="d3">The concept of “zero” as a protector implies that despite losing surrender value during lapse, the policyholder faces no additional loss beyond what's already accounted for, aligning with the safety net described in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="47fe3387-29bc-4869-a3a5-637bc22b6a91" target="f059bbb2-2661-4ab8-9504-a5a0a25687f5">
  <data key="d3">The idea of “zero” as a protective force reflects the policy’s design to prevent losses from market declines, whereas the first sentence addresses a limitation on benefits during early policy life. These ideas coexist conceptually but do not influence each other directly.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPTUAL_COUNTERPART</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
<edge source="47fe3387-29bc-4869-a3a5-637bc22b6a91" target="66d61507-a301-4354-ad15-acfad1eafccb">
  <data key="d3">The idea that “zero” is the hero reflects the policy’s guarantee against losses from negative market moves, which complements the restrictive nature of clauses like the suicide exclusion by reinforcing overall safety net provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL SUPPORT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
