<edge source="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069" target="c929a946-29b9-4878-9e8b-1320d6fdb4af">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence outlines a guarantee preventing financial loss from poor index performance. This protection has no connection to the ambiguous assertion in the first sentence regarding lapse timing.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069" target="e27b0a94-4088-4246-ba72-d6793b6cd04d">
  <data key="d3">Zero downside risk from index declines protects the policyholder's account value regardless of market behavior. This feature operates separately from the grace period rules governing payment deadlines.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069" target="61eb2693-c254-4b76-aefb-4ce00bdc5d2b">
  <data key="d3">Even if a policy lapses due to non-payment, the feature preventing losses from negative index returns remains intact, though it becomes irrelevant post-lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069" target="15cc61a2-a432-4cb5-8906-a25d63f7e7f6">
  <data key="d3">Zero downside risk shields the policyholder from losses caused by declining indices, complementing the surrender value provision that offers cash recovery when the policy ends without renewal.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069" target="f059bbb2-2661-4ab8-9504-a5a0a25687f5">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence describes how the policy prevents monetary loss from adverse index movements, whereas the first focuses on benefits payable in case of suicide during the initial two years. There is no direct connection between these clauses.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069" target="66d61507-a301-4354-ad15-acfad1eafccb">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence describes a built-in safety net preventing monetary loss from poor index performance, whereas the first sentence concerns eligibility conditions for payouts in case of suicide. No direct connection exists between the two clauses.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069" target="1fb961d9-6574-4554-b263-906d75b3f515">
  <data key="d3">Financial guarantees protecting against negative index results operate independently of the policy’s ability to contest claims due to misrepresentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069" target="6e42de55-cde0-435f-b499-10c6b12172e2">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee against losses from negative index movements underscores the policy’s conservative design. This feature supports the claim that it is not a securities product, emphasizing stability over market exposure.</data>
  <data key="d4">JUSTIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069" target="d95da1e8-f071-414b-b0ad-9b56d2f0e759">
  <data key="d3">Because the policyholder does not own underlying stocks directly, they are shielded from negative index changes, making it impossible to incur financial loss despite downturns in the referenced index.</data>
  <data key="d4">UNDERPINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069" target="2ec53e58-1461-418f-af0f-33f4dab5f971">
  <data key="d3">Because the policyholder does not directly own index funds, they are insulated from adverse index movements, making it possible to have a zero-loss outcome regardless of index performance.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069" target="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3">
  <data key="d3">Even though dividends from index components are not counted in performance metrics, the policy still protects holders from losing money when indices decline, ensuring stability independent of dividend inclusion rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069" target="a6b58496-e890-407d-99f3-f8e86cce69dd">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of no loss from negative index performance does not impact or rely on whether cap rates change annually.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069" target="7e3f4dce-a967-443e-8c1e-f4c1a24f502c">
  <data key="d3">Even with variable participation rates affecting credit allocation, the policy’s design prevents any monetary loss due to poor index performance, ensuring downside protection irrespective of rate adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069" target="09f59f75-d8f5-4cf9-b763-8e9b77770ca0">
  <data key="d3">The absence of downside risk from index declines underscores the safety net built into the policy’s indexing feature, complementing the stable but potentially adjustable fixed account rates offered by the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069" target="b080d9ad-b053-459f-8150-83b862b99de1">
  <data key="d3">Because cap rates are protected by guaranteed minimums, any negative index performance results in a zero outcome rather than financial loss, making the policyholder's capital fully safeguarded.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESULT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069" target="a416fa11-2b3f-4f38-958d-ff8e13bcbb1a">
  <data key="d3">Since negative index movements cannot lead to losses, this outcome depends on the existence of guaranteed minimum participation rates that protect the policy’s value.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069" target="af34274c-dfee-4fb4-a491-3e2e93de0364">
  <data key="d3">Zero downside risk arises because fixed account rates are anchored by guaranteed minimums, preventing any financial loss despite adverse index movements.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069" target="5ba693f1-db68-45ea-a535-eef1cf763796">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of no downside risk from negative index performance justifies the disclaimer that past performance doesn't ensure future outcomes, emphasizing safety over historical trends.</data>
  <data key="d4">JUSTIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069" target="47fe3387-29bc-4869-a3a5-637bc22b6a91">
  <data key="d3">The assurance that a zero outcome prevents monetary loss underpins the symbolic role of zero as a protective force in the policy’s design.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069" target="b1733959-f2c8-49a1-abbf-c49d75d321d4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains that the policy guarantees no loss from negative index movements. This statement has no bearing on the contact details provided in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069" target="4323367b-0222-42cb-99fe-8a2785ec96d3">
  <data key="d3">The policy guarantees no financial loss when index performance is negative, and this protection is maintained because the policyholder does not receive dividends during such periods, preventing any additional losses.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069" target="87987c98-b6f9-450a-8c71-84809999dd2b">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence explains a protective feature against market downturns in the policy’s indexed component. The second sentence offers general contact details for the insurance provider, which does not relate to the policy's financial safeguards.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
